msgstr ""
"Depot building for buying trains. In a radius around the building, trains "
"are automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_RAIL_DEPOT_NAME"
msgstr "Train Depot"

msgid "DEPOTS_RAIL_MAINT_STATION_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In a radius around the building, trains are automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_RAIL_MAINT_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Train Maintenance Building"

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_DEPOT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Depot building for buying trucks and buses. In a radius around the building, "
"trucks and buses are automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_DEPOT_NAME"
msgstr "Road Depot"

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_MAINT_STATION_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In a radius around the building, trucks, buses and trams are automatically "
"maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_MAINT_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Road Maintenance Building"

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_TRAM_DEPOT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Depot building for buying trams. In a radius around the building, trams are "
"automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_ROAD_TRAM_DEPOT_NAME"
msgstr "Tram Depot"

msgid "DEPOTS_WATER_MAINT_STATION_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "In a radius around the building, ships are automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_WATER_MAINT_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Ship Maintenance Building"

msgid "DEPOTS_WATER_SHIPYARD_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Depot building for buying ships. In a radius around the building, ships are "
"automatically maintained."

msgid "DEPOTS_WATER_SHIPYARD_NAME"
msgstr "Ship Depot"

msgid "DLC_DELUXE_UPGRADE_PACK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Transport Fever 3: Deluxe Upgrade allows you to take your network to the "
"next level with iconic vehicles, more world-famous landmarks, and new unique "
"wildlife from around the globe.\n"
"\n"
"Six Legendary Vehicles for Land, Sea, and Air:\n"
"- Concorde: fastest passenger airplane of all times\n"
"- London Bus: timeless symbol of public transport\n"
"- Trans-Europe Express: milestone of luxury rail travel\n"
"- Peterbilt 359: legend of trucking power and endurance\n"
"- Hong Kong Tram: iconic double-decker streetcar\n"
"- Sikorsky S-76 Spirit: the go-to helicopter for highest comfort standards\n"
"\n"
"Two Famous Landmarks From Around the Globe:\n"
"- Eiffel Tower: icon of European architecture\n"
"- Taj Mahal: masterpiece of the world's heritage\n"
"\n"
"Four Distinctive Animals Representing Different Climate Zones:\n"
"- Orca: dangerous ruler of the subarctic oceans\n"
"- Komodo Dragon: apex predator of the tropical islands\n"
"- Boar Family: resilient inhabitants of the temperate forests\n"
"- Bison: calm giant of the dry grasslands\n"
"\n"
"Three New Handcrafted Maps For All Kind of Challenges:\n"
"- Redrock Bends: conquer winding rivers, steep canyons, and growing "
"transport challenges\n"
"- Northern Gates: navigate dramatic fjords, scattered islands, and "
"impassable mountain barriers\n"
"- Emerald Shores: balance costly infrastructure and waterways across "
"volcanic island paradises\n"
"\n"
"Additional Extras For Even More Fun:\n"
"- Tycoon Cars: bring your road traffic to the next level\n"
"- Fun Elements: hot air balloon, handcar and a decorative maze for your "
"headquarters\n"
"- Soundtrack Collection: build your network to the tunes of all our previous "
"titles"

msgid "DLC_DELUXE_UPGRADE_PACK_NAME"
msgstr "Deluxe Upgrade"

msgid "DLC_DELUXE_UPGRADE_PACK_SUMMARY"
msgstr ""
"The Transport Fever 3: Deluxe Upgrade allows you to take your network to the "
"next level with iconic vehicles, more world-famous landmarks, and new unique "
"wildlife from around the globe to your base game."

msgid "DLC_PREORDER_PACK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Pre-Order Pack rewards early supporters of Transport Fever 3 with "
"exclusive content that adds iconic scale and atmosphere to your world:\n"
"\n"
"A Brand-New Historical Vehicle:\n"
"- TS Queen Mary: legendary ocean liner, meticulously recreated in stunning "
"detail\n"
"\n"
"A World-Famous Landmark:\n"
"- Great Pyramid: most iconic wonder of the ancient world\n"
"\n"
"A Majestic Wildlife Addition:\n"
"- Tropical elephant: majestic symbol of strength and life in tropical regions"

msgid "DLC_PREORDER_PACK_NAME"
msgstr "Pre-Order Pack"

msgid "DLC_PREORDER_PACK_SUMMARY"
msgstr ""
"The Pre-Order Pack rewards early supporters of Transport Fever 3 with "
"exclusive content that adds iconic scale and atmosphere to your world."

msgid "ELECTRIFICATION_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Electrification"

msgid "ELECTRIFICATION_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Electric trains can only be assigned to a line if every track and station "
"along the route is electrified.\n"
"Existing tracks can be upgraded using the electrification tool found in the "
"construction menu. Tracks highlighted in beige lack electrification, while "
"those in blue are already equipped with a catenary.\n"
"When building new tracks, you can directly select tracks that are equipped "
"with a catenary."

msgid "Enable Drag-and-Confirm Construction Mode"
msgstr "Drag-and-Confirm Construction Mode"

msgid "Fareham"
msgstr "Fareham"

msgid "Fareham Saw Mill"
msgstr "Fareham Saw Mill"

msgid "GAMEPAD_EXTEND_LINE_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Often you want to modify an existing line. Start by selecting the line you "
"want to change, either in the 3D world or in the line manager window. With "
"the line selected, you can modify it in several ways: you can move stops, "
"remove them, or add an additional stop by selecting a station in the 3D "
"world. The new stop is added after the stop that is currently selected in "
"the line manager window."

msgid "GAMEPAD_WAYPOINT_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"If you want to reroute your vehicles to avoid quiet town roads or if you "
"want to ease traffic congestion, you can add waypoints on your line. Select "
"the stop after which you want to add your waypoint in the line manager "
"window, then hold [iaHint=IA_PRECISION_MODE/] and press [iaHint=IA_APPLY/] "
"while hovering over a location on the map to place your waypoint."

msgid "GAMESPEED_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Change the Game Speed"

msgid "GAMESPEED_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"You can change the game speed by selecting any of the four buttons. If you "
"want to take your time to set up lines or build constructions, you can "
"select pause mode. To fast forward, you can speed up the game with the x2 "
"and x4 buttons."

msgid "GUIDE_BUILD_STATIONS"
msgstr ""
"Stations can be built in towns or near industries to transport people or "
"cargo."

msgid "Grange-over-Sands"
msgstr "Grange-over-Sands"

msgid "Grange-over-Sands Clay Pit"
msgstr "Grange-over-Sands Clay Pit"

msgid "Grange-over-Sands Fishing Grounds"
msgstr "Grange-over-Sands Fishing Grounds"

msgid "Grange-over-Sands Oil Platform"
msgstr "Grange-over-Sands Oil Platform"

msgid "Grange-over-Sands Oil Refinery"
msgstr "Grange-over-Sands Oil Refinery"

msgid "HARBOR_LARGE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Port for passengers and cargo that can be extended with modules. It can be "
"used by small and large ships."

msgid "HARBOR_LARGE_NAME"
msgstr "Large Passenger/Cargo Port"

msgid "HARBOR_SMALL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Port for passengers and cargo that can be extended with modules. It can be "
"used by small ships."

msgid "HARBOR_SMALL_NAME"
msgstr "Small Passenger/Cargo Port"

msgid "HEADQUARTERS_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The headquarters is a symbol of the company's ambitions. Its impressive "
"stature in classic design represents the company's lasting influence and "
"success.\n"
"\n"
"Promotes the nearest town to the capital and increases its growth rate. Can "
"be extended with modules that provide additional benefits."

msgid "HEADQUARTERS_NAME"
msgstr "Headquarters"

msgid "HELP_BULLDOZER"
msgstr ""
"The bulldozer is used to remove infrastructure and other objects.\n"
"Demolishing buildings in towns is expensive and lowers reputation, but is "
"sometimes necessary."

msgid "HELP_COMPANY_ASSETS"
msgstr ""
"This tab shows various information about company assets.\n"
"The statistics on the left show the current number of stations, vehicles and "
"other company assets.\n"
"The diagrams show the expansion of the tracks and cargo transportation over "
"time."

msgid "HELP_COMPANY_DELIVERYTIME"
msgstr ""
"This diagram shows the time in which each cargo type must be delivered from "
"origin to destination.\n"
"Delayed delivery can have a negative impact on town growth. The expected "
"delivery time changes when the game progresses over multiple years.\n"
"The cargo satisfaction layer can be used to analyze the current situation."

msgid "HELP_COMPANY_FINANCES"
msgstr ""
"The first three diagrams provide a quick overview of the company's financial "
"situation.\n"
"The towns chart shows the growth of the residential, commercial and "
"industrial districts of all towns combined."

msgid "HELP_COMPANY_LOANS"
msgstr ""
"Here loans can be taken out to fund the construction of infrastructure.\n"
"The various offers that are available differ in amount, term and interest "
"rate. New offers appear on a regular basis, so keep an eye out for the best "
"deals.\n"
"Up to four loans can be taken out at the same time and can be repaid early "
"if sufficient capital is available."

msgid "HELP_COMPANY_OVERVIEW"
msgstr ""
"The financial overview shows income and costs over recent years.\n"
"Each of the categories can be expanded to show more detailed information.\n"
"Vehicles generate income from ticket sales, but also have running costs. "
"Infrastructure such as stations or tracks have upkeep costs."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_AIR_BUILDINGS"
msgstr ""
"Air buildings are used as basis for aircraft lines.\n"
"The buildings can be placed in the world and then combined in the line "
"manager to form lines.\n"
"Airfields and airports are used for airplanes, while helipads and heliports "
"are used for helicopters.\n"
"The integrated depot allows to buy aircraft and also provides an area for "
"their maintenance.\n"
"While building, the catchment and maintenance areas are displayed."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_GENERATOR_INDUSTRIES"
msgstr ""
"The industry generator is used to create multiple industries on the map from "
"a random seed.\n"
"It is possible to keep existing industries and only create additional ones.\n"
"For a map to be playable, several industries should be created. The "
"industries should be connected to towns by roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_GENERATOR_STREETS"
msgstr ""
"The connection generator is used to create road connections between towns "
"automatically. Industries will be connected as well.\n"
"Connections can be changed in the preview, before generating the roads. A "
"new connection is created by clicking on two town dots. Connections can be "
"removed by clicking on the lines.\n"
"It is also possible to keep existing roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_GENERATOR_STREETS_CONTROLLER"
msgstr ""
"The connection generator is used to create road connections between towns "
"automatically. Industries will be connected as well.\n"
"It is also possible to keep existing roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_GENERATOR_TOWNS"
msgstr ""
"The town generator is used to create multiple towns on the map from a random "
"seed.\n"
"It is possible to keep existing towns and only create additional ones.\n"
"For a map to be playable, several towns should be created and connected with "
"roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_INDUSTRY_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"These tools are used to create new industries.\n"
"For a map to be playable, several industries should be placed. The "
"industries should be connected to towns by roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_MAP_EXPORT"
msgstr ""
"Heightmaps can be exported to an image file.\n"
"This can be useful to modify a map in an external tool and then import it "
"again.\n"
"It can be selected whether to create an image with 16-bit or 8-bit color "
"depth."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_MAP_GENERATORS"
msgstr ""
"The heightmap generator is used to generate terrain and vegetation from a "
"random seed.\n"
"Various settings are available to obtain the desired landscape."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_MAP_IMPORT"
msgstr ""
"Heightmaps can be imported from an image file.\n"
"It is recommended to use a 16-bit grayscale image.\n"
"The height and width of the image must be a multiple of 256 plus 1.\n"
"The minimum and maximum height of the terrain and the water level can be set "
"before importing the image."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_PERKS_LANDMARKS"
msgstr ""
"Landmarks can be placed to decorate the game world and are visited by "
"residents.\n"
"Each unique building grants a special bonus to the municipal area in which "
"it is built.\n"
"Landmarks are unlocked by reaching new company ranks."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_PERKS_MECHANICS"
msgstr ""
"The marketing campaign can be launched in a town to encourage more residents "
"to use public transportation.\n"
"Greenify industry can be applied to an industry to reduce its emissions.\n"
"These tools are unlocked by reaching new company ranks."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_PERKS_PROSPECTION"
msgstr ""
"Prospecting is used to search for unexploited occurrences of a resource near "
"a specific town.\n"
"After selecting the town, prospecting begins. If a suitable location can be "
"found, a new industry is founded. If no suitable location is found within a "
"certain time, prospecting fails.\n"
"Prospecting is unlocked by reaching new company ranks."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_RAIL_BUILDINGS"
msgstr ""
"Rail buildings are used as basis for train lines.\n"
"Stations can be placed in the world and then combined in the line manager to "
"form lines.\n"
"The depot allows to buy trains and also provides an area for their "
"maintenance.\n"
"The maintenance building can be placed to provide additional maintenance "
"areas.\n"
"While building, the catchment area of stations and maintenance area of "
"depots and maintenance buildings is displayed."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_RAIL_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"Track tools are used to modify existing tracks.\n"
"Signals can be placed on tracks to control rail traffic. A train will only "
"drive, if it can exclusively reserve the entire path from its current "
"position to the next signal or station.\n"
"The electrification and noise barrier tools allow to add or remove catenary "
"respectively noise barriers to existing tracks."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_RAIL_TRACKS"
msgstr ""
"Tracks are used to connect train stations and depots.\n"
"Track types differ in supported speeds, pollution and costs. The catenary "
"enables the use of electric trains.\n"
"New types will be unlocked over time.\n"
"Tracks can be modified after construction using track tools.\n"
"Rail traffic can be controlled with path signals."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_ROADS_CONSTRUCTIONS"
msgstr ""
"Road constructions are used to build predefined road layouts.\n"
"These can vary from roundabouts to complex highway intersections."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_ROADS_ROADS"
msgstr ""
"Roads are used to connect road stations and depots as well as towns and "
"industries.\n"
"There are three different types of roads: town streets, country roads and "
"highways.\n"
"Town streets have sidewalks and towns can expand along them. The green area "
"while building town streets shows where town buildings may be build.\n"
"Country roads can be used to connect towns. They can be used by pedestrians, "
"but they become unhappy while walking along them.\n"
"Highways allow for high traffic connections and cannot be used by "
"pedestrians.\n"
"Towns will not construct buildings along country roads or Highways.\n"
"The different road types vary in supported speeds, number of lanes and "
"extras such as noise barriers."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_ROADS_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"Road tools are used to modify existing roads.\n"
"There are individual tools for adding or removing specific extras such as "
"tram tracks, bus lanes, or noise barriers.\n"
"While using, it can be selected whether the change is made symmetrically on "
"both sides or only on a single lane.\n"
"The locking tool marks roads as locked, preventing automatic changes to the "
"road.\n"
"The crossing tool allows to change the road and tram lanes at crossings."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_ROAD_BUILDINGS"
msgstr ""
"Road buildings are used as basis for truck, bus or tram lines.\n"
"Stops and stations can be placed in the world and then combined in the line "
"manager to form lines.\n"
"Depots allow to buy trucks, buses or trams and also provide an area for "
"their maintenance.\n"
"The maintenance building can be placed to provide additional maintenance "
"areas.\n"
"While building, the catchment area of stations and maintenance area of "
"depots and maintenance buildings is displayed."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_ROAD_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"Road tools are used to modify existing roads.\n"
"The tram track tool allows to add or remove tram tracks. Tracks at "
"intersections are automatically built, but can be controlled with the "
"crossing tool.\n"
"The bus lane tool allows to add or remove bus lanes. Bus lanes are "
"exclusively for trucks and buses and will not be used by cars when "
"possible.\n"
"While using, it can be selected whether the change is made symmetrically on "
"both sides or only on a single lane."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_TERRAIN_ASSETS"
msgstr ""
"These tools are used to decorate the game world with a variety of assets.\n"
"Placing assets has no influence on the gameplay and is free of charge."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_TERRAIN_PAINTER"
msgstr ""
"These tools are used to paint the terrain with a variety of materials.\n"
"Painting the terrain has no influence on the gameplay and is free of charge."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_TERRAIN_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"These tools are used to modify the terrain.\n"
"Rivers and lakes can also be modified. The terrain layer shows where ships "
"can navigate.\n"
"Modifying the terrain has costs and lowers the reputation in the nearest "
"town."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_TERRAIN_VEGETATION"
msgstr ""
"These tools are used to decorate the game world with a variety of plants and "
"rocks.\n"
"The assets can be placed individually or in brush mode.\n"
"Demolishing trees and rocks lowers the reputation in the nearest town."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_TOWN_TOOLS"
msgstr ""
"The town builder is used to create a new town.\n"
"The size of the town and the cargo demands can be selected.\n"
"For a map to be playable, several towns should be placed and connected with "
"roads."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_WAREHOUSES"
msgstr ""
"Warehouses are used to store and transfer cargo between different means of "
"transportation.\n"
"Specialized warehouses enable faster loading speeds, but can only store "
"certain types of cargo.\n"
"While building, the catchment areas of stations are displayed that can store "
"cargo in the warehouse."

msgid "HELP_CONSTRUCTION_WATER_BUILDINGS"
msgstr ""
"Water buildings are used as basis for ship lines.\n"
"Ports can be placed along the coast line and then combined in the line "
"manager to form lines.\n"
"The depot allows to buy ships and also provides an area for their "
"maintenance.\n"
"The maintenance building can be placed to provide additional maintenance "
"areas.\n"
"While building, the catchment area of ports and maintenance area of depots "
"and maintenance buildings is displayed."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_CARGO_FLOW"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the amount of cargo that is transported on a specific "
"route. It also shows how well a town's industrial and commercial districts "
"are supplied with cargo.\n"
"By zooming closer, more detailed information is displayed.\n"
"The demanded amount of cargo must be supplied to all buildings in the "
"industrial and commercial districts of a town to maximize the town's growth."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_CARGO_ONTIME"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows if cargo is delivered fast enough and reaches its "
"destination on-time.\n"
"Each cargo type must be delivered within the time specified on the delivery "
"time tab in the company finances window.\n"
"Routes are colored according to the average delivery time. Additionally, "
"colored labels above warehouses and vehicles show the amount of cargo "
"currently on-time.\n"
"Delayed delivery has a negative impact on town growth. The current rating of "
"a town is displayed above it."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_CIVILIZATION"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the districts of towns.\n"
"Residents live in the residential district, shop in the commercial district "
"and work in the industrial district or industries. They travel from their "
"homes to the shops and then move back home before going to work.\n"
"Residents will only work in remote industries if public transportation is "
"available. Residents also like to shop or work in neighboring towns. Public "
"transport lines should be set up accordingly.\n"
"The color intensity shows the current level of the buildings."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_INFRASTRUCTURE"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the speed limits of tracks and roads as well as the "
"catchment or maintenance areas.\n"
"The curvature of tracks and roads reduces the maximum speed, therefore it is "
"recommended to build straight if possible.\n"
"Different speed limits apply to different types of tracks, roads and "
"bridges.\n"
"It can be selected whether to show the catchment areas of passenger stations "
"respectively cargo stations or the maintenance areas of maintenance "
"buildings and depots."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_INTRO"
msgstr ""
"Data layers visualize important information about the game world.\n"
"Each layer icon can be selected to get more information."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_NOISE"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the noise emitted by vehicles and buildings.\n"
"Noise has a negative impact on town growth, if it occurs near residential "
"buildings. The current rating of a town is displayed above it."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_PASSENGER_FLOW"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the amount of travelers using a specific route to reach a "
"destination.\n"
"By zooming closer, more detailed information is displayed.\n"
"Private and public transport can be turned on and off individually. The view "
"can be limited to a single town of origin."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_PASSENGER_SATISFACTION"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows passenger happiness when using public transport.\n"
"Passengers are happy when leaving their home and become less happy the "
"longer the journey takes. In vehicles with a high level of comfort, "
"happiness decreases only slowly, whereas in less comfortable vehicles it "
"decreases faster. It decreases even quicker when passengers have to wait at "
"stations for a long time. Happiness will recover as soon as passengers "
"return home.\n"
"Traveling routes are colored according to the recent average happiness. "
"Additionally, colored labels above stations and vehicles show the current "
"happiness.\n"
"Low passenger happiness has a negative impact on town growth. The current "
"rating of a town is displayed above it."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_POLLUTION"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the pollution emitted by vehicles and buildings.\n"
"Pollution has a negative effect on the growth of the town in whose municipal "
"area it is emitted. The boundaries of the town regions are also visible in "
"the layer. The current rating of a town is displayed above it.\n"
"The pollution distribution is influenced by the wind. The strength and "
"direction of the wind is displayed at the bottom right."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_TERRAIN"
msgstr ""
"This layer provides information about the nature of the terrain by showing "
"different contour lines and navigable waters.\n"
"Vehicles need more power when they have to drive uphill. Therefore, large "
"gradients should be avoided.\n"
"When building tracks or roads, it is best to follow the contour lines to "
"save money, as terrain modifications are expensive.\n"
"Ships can only sail in navigable waters. For ship lines to function, a path "
"with navigable waters must exist from start to finish. Bridges must be built "
"with enough height to allow ships to pass. The terrain tools can help to "
"make additional water navigable."

msgid "HELP_LAYER_TRAFFIC"
msgstr ""
"This layer shows the current state of the road and rail traffic.\n"
"Roads and track segments with traffic jams and slowed vehicles are colored.\n"
"Road traffic jams have a negative impact on town growth. The current traffic "
"rating of a town is displayed above it.\n"
"To reduce congestion, the road network or public transport can be improved."

msgid "HELP_MANAGEMENT"
msgstr ""
"The line manager is the central navigation tool to create and manage all "
"transport networks as well as build and coordinate your vehicle fleet.\n"
"The tool is divided into two parts: the upper part allows to create new "
"lines and provides a list of all existing lines. The lower part allows to "
"manage and assign a selection of vehicles.\n"
"Lines can be expanded by selecting their name to display all its stops and "
"simultaneously list all assigned vehicles in the lower part.\n"
"A new line can be created by either pressing the \"New Line\" button on the "
"top or by directly selecting a station in the world. If a line is already "
"selected, selecting a stop in the real world expands the line. If a point on "
"a road or track is selected instead of a stop then a waypoint is added to "
"the line. This feature can be used to avoid certain areas being passed by "
"the line.\n"
"By selecting one or more vehicles in the lower area, various management "
"actions are provided such as reversing the direction of travel, stopping, "
"changing the color, duplicating, or replacing with other vehicles. Trams and "
"trains can also be modified to add or remove individual wagons. Vehicles can "
"also be sent to other lines or depots."

msgid "HELP_MISSION"
msgstr ""
"The mission window displays the current and completed tasks, the general "
"mission objectives and conditions for earning stars and the special badge.\n"
"The task descriptions consist of the spoken instruction and a brief summary "
"of the task.\n"
"Select the highlighted words to jump to important task locations.\n"
"If applicable, the window also contains the task progress."

msgid "HELP_MUSIC_PLAYER"
msgstr ""
"This is the music player.\n"
"Here, the title and length of the current song are displayed.\n"
"It is also possible to switch between songs in the playlist, pause the "
"music, or adjust the volume."

msgid "HELP_NOTIFICATIONS"
msgstr ""
"The notification log shows all current and previous notifications in "
"chronological order.\n"
"The list can be narrowed down to a specific type by using the \"Category\" "
"filter.\n"
"\"History\" and \"Active\" toggle between all notifications and those that "
"are currently active.\n"
"The settings button allows to configure for which types of notifications a "
"pop-up should appear at the top of the screen."

msgid "HELP_PROGRESS_COMPANY"
msgstr ""
"This window shows the status of the company.\n"
"On the left, the current company rank is shown as well as the future ranks "
"that can be reached.\n"
"On the top the current world population is displayed together with the "
"amount to reach to earn a new rank.\n"
"The list in the center shows all the perks that are unlocked at the rank "
"selected in the list on the left."

msgid "HELP_START"
msgstr ""
"The context help provides further information on the various menus and "
"windows.\n"
"Its content automatically adapts to the currently open menu or window.\n"
"The context help can be opened or closed by pressing "
"[iaHint=IA_CONTEXT_HELP/]."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_DEPOTS"
msgstr ""
"The depot overview shows detailed information about all depots and "
"maintenance buildings.\n"
"\"Parked\" shows all vehicles that are not assigned to a line and parked in "
"the depot.\n"
"\"Maintained\" indicates which vehicles are currently maintained.\n"
"\"Usage\" provides information about the current usage and available "
"maintenance pool.\n"
"The table can be filtered by vehicle type and sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_INDUSTRIES"
msgstr ""
"The industry overview shows detailed information about all industries.\n"
"\"Input\" and \"Output\" show the current annual consumption respectively "
"production of cargo.\n"
"\"Workload\" indicates whether the industry is producing at full capacity. "
"In order to achieve full workload, a steady supply of all required cargo "
"types is necessary.\n"
"\"Boosters\" and \"Workplaces\" provide information on the current status of "
"the boosters.\n"
"\"Shipment\" shows the amount of cargo shipped annually.\n"
"The table can be sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_LINES"
msgstr ""
"The line overview shows detailed information about all lines.\n"
"\"Load\" and \"Capacity\" provide information about the current and maximum "
"load of all vehicles combined.\n"
"\"Utilization\" indicates what percentage of the capacity is currently "
"used.\n"
"\"Satisfaction\" shows the percentage of happy passengers respectively cargo "
"that is on-time.\n"
"\"Frequency\" indicates the time interval between the vehicles.\n"
"\"Rate\" measures the amount of cargo or passengers a line can transport per "
"year.\n"
"\"Balance\" shows the annual profit or loss.\n"
"The table can be filtered by vehicle type and sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_STATIONS"
msgstr ""
"The station overview shows detailed information about all stations.\n"
"\"Lines\" indicates the number of lines using the station.\n"
"\"Type\" shows whether it is a cargo, passenger or mixed station.\n"
"\"Utilization\" provides information on how many passengers are waiting at "
"the station and how much space is available\n"
"\"Delay\" shows the amount of unsatisfied passengers respectively delayed "
"cargo.\n"
"\"Upkeep\" indicates the annual costs of the station.\n"
"The table can be filtered by vehicle type and sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_TOWNS"
msgstr ""
"The town overview shows detailed information about all towns.\n"
"\"Size\" and \"Population\" show the current size of the town.\n"
"\"Public Transport\" and \"Private Transport\" indicate the number of "
"residents who use public respectively private transport to reach their "
"destinations.\n"
"The cargo demands and current coverage are visible as well.\n"
"The bars on the right show the town's current ratings.\n"
"The table can be sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_VEHICLES"
msgstr ""
"The vehicle overview shows detailed information about all vehicles.\n"
"\"Load\" and \"Capacity\" provide information about the current and maximum "
"load of the vehicle.\n"
"\"Utilization\" indicates what percentage of the capacity is currently "
"used.\n"
"\"Satisfaction\" shows the percentage of happy passengers respectively cargo "
"that is on-time.\n"
"\"Condition\" indicates how well a vehicle is maintained.\n"
"\"Balance\" shows the annual profit or loss.\n"
"The table can be filtered by vehicle type and sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_STATISTICS_WAREHOUSES"
msgstr ""
"The warehouse overview shows detailed information about all warehouses.\n"
"\"Stocks\" shows the supported cargo types for the warehouse.\n"
"\"Stored\", \"Capacity\" and \"Utilization\" indicate the current amount of "
"stored cargo, the total capacity of all buildings and the current "
"utilization.\n"
"The table can be sorted by each column."

msgid "HELP_SUBSIDY"
msgstr ""
"From time to time, industries or towns offer subsidies for performing "
"specific tasks.\n"
"Each subsidy will provide an upfront funding to get started. If the "
"subsidy's requirement criteria are reached within the time limit, additional "
"benefits are paid out. However, if the deadline is missed, the upfront "
"payment must be repaid and further penalties are imposed."

msgid "HELP_VEHICLE_STORE"
msgstr ""
"The vehicle store allows to buy new vehicles and modify compositions.\n"
"The list on the left shows all vehicles that are currently available for "
"purchase. The availability of vehicles depends on the current year and the "
"selected depot type.\n"
"Selecting a vehicle displays more information on the right side. Especially "
"the performance parameters of each vehicle are of interest, as different "
"circumstances ask for different values. Each vehicle has its advantages and "
"disadvantages.\n"
"For trains and trams, several locomotives and wagons can be combined in a "
"composition. The combined properties of the composition are displayed at the "
"bottom right. The speed is determined by the speed of the slowest vehicle. "
"Performance indicates how well the composition behaves on steep terrain."

msgid "HELP_WEATHER_AND_TIME"
msgstr ""
"The weather and time window allows to change various aspects of weather and "
"time.\n"
"Current weather and time can be adjusted via sliders, while progression is "
"determined by the \"Cycle\" setting:\n"
"\"Custom\" ensures the selected weather or time remains unchanged.\n"
"\"Dynamic\" randomly interpolates between different values.\n"
"\"Continuous\" enables a natural day-night cycle.\n"
"\"Local Time\" synchronizes the time with the local time zone.\n"
"Date progression is controlled by the calendar speed slider. The progression "
"can be paused by moving the slider all the way to the left.\n"
"When sandbox mode is enabled, it is additionally possible to jump to "
"specific dates and adjust the lighting environment."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_ANIMAL"
msgstr ""
"Animals don't affect gameplay, but they sure look amazing, as long as they "
"don't get hit by a vehicle.\n"
"Different species of animals can be found all over the map, and they vary "
"depending on the climate.\n"
"Will you be able to spot them all?"

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_BRIDGE"
msgstr ""
"This window allows to upgrade an existing bridge to a new type.\n"
"Different types have varying speed limits, which are displayed below the "
"bridge image.\n"
"Upgrade costs depend on the selected type and length of the bridge."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_CROSSING"
msgstr ""
"This window allows to enable or disable traffic lights.\n"
"Once enabled, the individual traffic light phases can be adjusted.\n"
"Selecting a phase previews its green and red lanes, which can be toggled by "
"selecting them.\n"
"The duration for each phase can be set, and phases can be configured to be "
"skipped if no vehicles are waiting. A minimum duration can be set for "
"skippable phases.\n"
"A dynamic progress bar displays the remaining time of the active phase."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_DEPOT"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the depot or maintenance "
"building, such as the size of the maintenance pool and the vehicles being "
"maintained.\n"
"Each building can only maintain a certain number of vehicles at a time. If "
"more capacity is required, additional buildings can be placed."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_HEADQUARTER"
msgstr ""
"The headquarters is a symbol of the company's success and the starting point "
"for its expansion.\n"
"It promotes the nearest town to the capital and increases its growth rate.\n"
"The headquarters can be extended with modules, such as buildings and "
"decorations, by selecting the \"Configure\" button.\n"
"Additional modules are unlocked by reaching new company ranks."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_INDUSTRY"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the industry, such as the "
"production rule and rates, booster status and current stocks.\n"
"Production rates can vary between industries of the same type and may change "
"over time. Industries that require input show the current production rate "
"and the maximum that could be achieved with a full supply.\n"
"Industries automatically start production as soon as all required materials "
"are in stock.\n"
"The station tab provides information about the integrated stations."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_LANDMARK"
msgstr ""
"Landmarks are unique buildings that can be placed in the game world.\n"
"Each one grants a bonus to certain vehicles within the same municipal area "
"and is visited by residents.\n"
"All the necessary resources must be supplied to the construction site in "
"order to complete the construction.\n"
"Additional landmarks are unlocked by reaching new company ranks."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_LINE"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the line, such as its load, "
"vehicles and the annual transportation rate.\n"
"The transportation rate should match the demand respectively production of "
"the connected locations."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_PERSON"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the resident, such as the "
"travel destinations, means of transportation used and current happiness "
"level.\n"
"Residents travel from their homes to the shops and then move back home "
"before going to work. They are happy when leaving their home and become less "
"happy the longer the journey takes. Happiness will recover as soon as they "
"return home."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_RAILROAD_CROSSING"
msgstr ""
"This window allows to upgrade an existing rail crossing to a new type.\n"
"Upgrade costs depend on the selected type."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_SIGNAL"
msgstr ""
"This window allows to change a normal path signal into a one-way signal.\n"
"Signals are used to control rail traffic. A train will only drive, if it can "
"exclusively reserve the entire path from its current position to the next "
"signal or station.\n"
"Although trains generally prefer to travel in the direction indicated by the "
"white arrow, a normal path signal also allows rail traffic from the opposite "
"direction to pass when necessary. Switching to a one-way signal completely "
"blocks all oncoming traffic."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_STATION"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the station, such as the "
"lines using it, the number of waiting passengers as well as the "
"specialization of the terminals.\n"
"Modular stations can be extended with new modules by selecting the "
"\"Configure\" button."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_TOWN"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the town, such as its size, "
"supply status and ratings.\n"
"Each element in the overview section can be selected to reveal more detailed "
"information about its status.\n"
"In order for a town to grow, passenger transport must be provided and the "
"cargo demands must be satisfied.\n"
"It is important to keep an eye on the town's ratings, as poor ratings will "
"have a negative impact on growth."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_TOWNBUILDING"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the building, such as the "
"residents working, shopping or living there.\n"
"Residential buildings are sensitive to noise, so noise in their surroundings "
"should be minimized.\n"
"Commercial and industrial buildings require a steady supply of cargo."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_TUNNEL"
msgstr ""
"This window allows to upgrade an existing tunnel to a new type.\n"
"Upgrade costs depend on the selected type and length of the tunnel."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_VEHICLE"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the vehicle, such as its "
"load, condition and the line it is assigned to.\n"
"Vehicles must be maintained in order to reach their full potential. Badly "
"maintained vehicles will suffer from lower performance and higher emissions. "
"Special maintenance buildings can be built along their route to improve "
"maintenance."

msgid "HELP_WINDOW_WAREHOUSE"
msgstr ""
"This window lists all relevant information about the warehouse, such as its "
"stocks, current fill levels and the supported cargo types.\n"
"Specialized stocks can be restricted to a specific cargo type by selecting "
"the cargo icon.\n"
"The warehouse can be extended with new modules by selecting the "
"\"Configure\" button."

