msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_D_9"
msgstr "That you’re lucky I gave you this job!"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_ROUTE_1"
msgstr ""
"The tourists are here. The citizens of New Orleans, music, and good food! "
"What route is the procession taking, Miss Baker?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_ROUTE_2"
msgstr ""
"I’d suggest a route from City Park along Canal Street, Mr. Mayor—if you ask "
"me!"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_ROUTE_3"
msgstr "That sounds good."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_ROUTE_4"
msgstr "I’ll see to it!"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TASK_GUMBO_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"Good. Once the catch comes in, the soup kitchens will be swamped. Then this "
"place will finally smell like Mardi Gras! Now all that’s left to do is steal "
"the Good Old Cowboys’ instruments. Then it’ll sound like it too."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_1"
msgstr ""
"Congratulations, Mr. Mayor. The hotel offers an amazing view of the city’s "
"social hotspots!"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_10"
msgstr ""
"It sounds so easy, cooking up a gumbo. And it would be too, if we had any "
"fish or seafood."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_11"
msgstr ""
"Unfortunately, the old warehouse got swept away. Where are the fishermen "
"supposed to bring their catch?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_12"
msgstr ""
"So, first we’re gonna need a warehouse at the port. Could you take care of "
"that?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_2"
msgstr ""
"You again? Don’t you have that terrible music to be practicing? What’s it "
"called again?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_3"
msgstr "I’m not a musician, but the music’s called ragtime."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_4"
msgstr ""
"That’s it. Terrible stuff. Sounds like someone treading on a dog’s tail!"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_5"
msgstr ""
"And I’m treading on your feet to remind you that the city isn’t a self-"
"service store for the strong."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_6"
msgstr "Only the strong can help the weak."

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_7"
msgstr ""
"But now that the hotels and the city’s budget are taken care of, Miss Baker, "
"do you have anything against us turning our attention to Mardi Gras?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_8"
msgstr ""
"Are you honestly trying to take our Black community into consideration?"

msgid "MISSION_01_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_LOGS_END_HOTEL_9"
msgstr ""
"Then just make sure you get a decent gumbo cooked up fast! And as for music, "
"we’ve got the Good Old Cowboys."

msgid "MISSION_01_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The Mardi Gras festival is just around the corner in New Orleans, but the "
"aftermath of a major storm is giving the mayor a headache. The city depends "
"on the revenue generated by visitors, and the local population does not want "
"to miss out either. A solution is urgently needed."

msgid "MISSION_01_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"A storm has battered our beautiful city—just a few weeks before Mardi Gras "
"too. It couldn’t have come at a worse time: The festival is vital for the "
"city’s finances. It’ll be a disaster if the tourists stay away! Not to "
"mention the tarnished reputation of the city. You have to help us!"

msgid "MISSION_01_LOCATION"
msgstr "New Orleans, United States"

msgid "MISSION_01_MEDAL"
msgstr "Subdue the alligators, fast."

msgid "MISSION_01_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Subdue the alligators, fast."

msgid "MISSION_01_NAME"
msgstr "Saving Mardi Gras"

msgid "MISSION_01_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Clean up the storm damage and help New Orleans so the Mardi Gras festival "
"can still go ahead."

msgid "MISSION_01_STAR_1"
msgstr "Save Mardi Gras."

msgid "MISSION_01_STAR_2"
msgstr "Help New Orleans a little more."

msgid "MISSION_01_STAR_3"
msgstr "Help New Orleans a lot more."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Select the [link=pos_street_depot_zone]depot[/link] to manage the vehicles "
"stored in it."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Very good! Our wagon is ready in the depot. Send the wagon on the new line "
"so it can find its way to the hotel and back."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_NAME"
msgstr "Assign the Carriage"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Assign the bought horse carriage to the transport line to the "
"[link=entity_hotel]hotel construction site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_SHIP_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Now we need to tell the captain where to head. Your choice: shrimp or fish?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_SHIP_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Ship Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_SHIP_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Assign the ship on a new line from the [link=entity_harbor]port[/link]: "
"downstream for [link=entity_shrimps]shrimp[/link] or upstream for "
"[link=entity_fish]fish[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_VEHICLES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"All set? How on earth did I manage to pull this off again?! Send the floats "
"out on the parade route. They’re stationed in the depot next to the French "
"Quarter hotel."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_VEHICLES_NAME"
msgstr "Assign the Floats"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_ASSIGN_VEHICLES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Assign the parade floats from the [link=entity_depot_3]vehicle depot[/link] "
"to the new Mardi Gras line."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "What is it?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Fantastic. Now we have a big problem that you’ll need to deal with!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Mayor"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_NOBONUS_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "What is it?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_NOBONUS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Okay, I guess not then, but we have a more pressing problem that you’ll need "
"to deal with!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_BRIDGE_NOBONUS_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Mayor"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_HOTEL_FOOD_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Of course!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_HOTEL_FOOD_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Mmm, something smells delicious. I think I have an idea. I could use your "
"help with an unusual task. Quick chat, just the two of us?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_HOTEL_FOOD_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Mayor"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_HOTEL_FOOD_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you want to know what the mayor wants from you?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_MUSIC_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Sure!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_MUSIC_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "No time."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_MUSIC_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Could you spare a little time for… some good music?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_MUSIC_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Katie"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BEFORE_MUSIC_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Do you want to help Katie take Mardi Gras in some new musical directions as "
"well?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_PATH_HINT"
msgstr "Select the road building tool from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_PATH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The marvels of technology! You don’t see that around here every day! Now we "
"can rebuild the road."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_PATH_NAME"
msgstr "Build the Road"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_PATH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the missing road segment by connecting the two ends of the "
"[link=pos_street]road[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_STREET_FIRST_DEPOT_HOTEL_HINT"
msgstr "Select the road depot from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_STREET_FIRST_DEPOT_HOTEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"All right. First, we need to build a vehicle depot so we can buy a wagon for "
"the wood delivery."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_STREET_FIRST_DEPOT_HOTEL_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Road Depot"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_STREET_FIRST_DEPOT_HOTEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a road depot in the [link=pos_street_depot_zone]highlighted area[/"
"link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_TRACKS_HINT"
msgstr "Select the track building tool from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_TRACKS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Come on then, you know what needs to be done. Let’s repair the track."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_TRACKS_NAME"
msgstr "Build the Bridge"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUILD_TRACKS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the missing track segment by connecting the two [link=pos_tracks]ends "
"of the track[/link] to repair the bridge."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BULLDOZE_HINT"
msgstr "Select the bulldozer from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BULLDOZE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "I’m counting on you for this. You do have heavy machinery, don’t you?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BULLDOZE_NAME"
msgstr "Bulldoze the Trees"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BULLDOZE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Bulldoze the fallen trees to clear the area next to the "
"[link=pos_street]road[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_COACH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"But that line won’t do us any good without a horse-drawn wagon traveling on "
"it."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_COACH_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Wagon"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_COACH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a horse carriage in the [link=entity_depot_2]depot[/link] and assign it "
"to the line between the warehouse and the hotel."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_HINT"
msgstr "Select the depot to buy vehicles in it."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Neat! Now we need to buy a wagon in the depot to transport cargo."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Horse Carriage"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_FIRST_TRUCK_HOTEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a horse carriage in the [link=pos_street_depot_zone]road depot[/link] "
"that can transport the wood into the city."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_SHIP_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "There’s no getting around it. We’ll have to buy the fishermen a boat."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_SHIP_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Boat"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_BUY_SHIP_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy the fishermen a new boat in the [link=entity_shipyard]shipyard[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_DELETE_LOGS_LINE_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Use the line manager to delete the line. The horse carriage will be sold "
"automatically."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_DELETE_LOGS_LINE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"This is going to be one fancy hotel. Just make sure the driver isn’t "
"aimlessly driving around, that’ll be a burden on the city’s finances."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_DELETE_LOGS_LINE_NAME"
msgstr "Delete the Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_DELETE_LOGS_LINE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Delete the wood delivery line."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_EXTEND_LINE_HINT"
msgstr "Use the line manager to edit the line."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_EXTEND_LINE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"You could just extend the New Orleans bus line by one stop in Lake Shore. "
"That way, we wouldn’t even have to buy new coaches!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_EXTEND_LINE_NAME"
msgstr "Extend the Bus Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_EXTEND_LINE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Extend the blue [link=entity_park]New Orleans[/link] bus line to connect "
"[link=entity_village]Lake Shore[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_END_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Release the Alligators"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_END_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Andrew says the lumberjacks are back at the logging camp. It's about time, "
"too—time is what we're shortest on."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_END_NAME"
msgstr "Release the Alligators"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The lumberjacks don’t dare go into the forest now. We need to round up the "
"alligators there so the city can receive lumber deliveries again."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION_1"
msgstr "An alligator has taken up residence in the logging camp!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION_2"
msgstr "Have you seen the alligator in the street near the gate yet?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION_3"
msgstr "There’s another one lurking among the trees."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION_4"
msgstr "Seems one’s hiding in the shack. Did you find it yet?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_INSTRUCTION_5"
msgstr ""
"You’ve already found the lazybones basking in the sun among the logs in the "
"logging camp, right?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_NAME"
msgstr "Find the Alligators"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_FIND_ALLIGATORS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Move the camera and select the alligators in the [link=entity_forest]logging "
"camp[/link] to catch them."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_GUMBO_BUILD_STORAGE_HINT"
msgstr "Select the warehouse from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_GUMBO_BUILD_STORAGE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "You have no idea how grateful folks will be to have a new warehouse."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_GUMBO_BUILD_STORAGE_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Warehouse"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_GUMBO_BUILD_STORAGE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build an universal warehouse in the [link=pos_warehouse_zone]highlighted "
"area[/link]!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_FISH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "We’re making progress! Now the fish can be delivered to the hotel."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_FISH_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Fish"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_FISH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Deliver the fish to the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_SHRIMP_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Neat! Now the shrimp can be delivered to the hotel."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_SHRIMP_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Shrimp"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_BONUS_SHRIMP_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Deliver the shrimp to the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_FISH_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Great plan!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_FISH_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "No, thanks."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_FISH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"But if the hotels were to serve Cajun cuisine… the tourists would lap it up, "
"the register would be ringing, and the locals would get some recognition… "
"You see what I mean?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_FISH_NAME"
msgstr "Decide your Action"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_FISH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you want to supply the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link] with fish?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_SHRIMPS_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Great plan!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_SHRIMPS_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "No, thanks."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_SHRIMPS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"But if the hotels were to serve Cajun cuisine… the tourists would lap it up, "
"the register would be ringing, and the locals would get some recognition… "
"You see what I mean?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_SHRIMPS_NAME"
msgstr "Decide your Action"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_DECIDE_SHRIMPS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you want to supply the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link] with shrimp?"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_LINE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Now we need to establish a line between the stop and the hotel."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_LINE_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Transport Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_HOTEL_LINE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a line between the station at the [link=pos_warehouse_zone]warehouse[/"
"link] and the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_MAKE_FIRST_TRUCK_LINE_HOTEL_HINT"
msgstr "Select the line manager from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_MAKE_FIRST_TRUCK_LINE_HOTEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need to create a line—from the logging camp to the construction site in "
"the city—so the wagon driver knows where to go."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_MAKE_FIRST_TRUCK_LINE_HOTEL_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Transport Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_MAKE_FIRST_TRUCK_LINE_HOTEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a new line and select the stops at the [link=entity_forest]logging "
"camp[/link] and the [link=entity_hotel]hotel construction site[/link] to set "
"the transport route for the wood."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_START_TRAIN_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Select the vehicle to open its details and use the start/stop function."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_START_TRAIN_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Wonderful. Now we should inform the engineer in Kenner that he can get his "
"train moving again."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_START_TRAIN_NAME"
msgstr "Start the Train"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_START_TRAIN_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Start the [link=entity_train]train[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_STATION_HINT"
msgstr "Select the station from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_STATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"To deliver food to the hotel, we’ll need a stop for the delivery truck "
"outside the warehouse."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Station"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_STATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a road station next to the [link=pos_warehouse_zone]warehouse[/link] "
"at the port."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_TRANSPORT_FIRST_LOGS_HOTEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Fantastic. The wagon is on its way now!"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_TRANSPORT_FIRST_LOGS_HOTEL_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Wood"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_TRANSPORT_FIRST_LOGS_HOTEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the wood to the [link=entity_hotel]hotel construction site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_WAYPOINTS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Okay, everything’s in place. Set up a route from City Park along Canal "
"Street."

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_WAYPOINTS_NAME"
msgstr "Create the Line"

msgid "MISSION_01_TASK_WAYPOINTS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create the line for the Mardi Gras procession starting at "
"[link=pos_park]City Park[/link] and place waypoints in the highlighted areas."

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "Lead Engineer"

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Dr. Karl Albert Brandtner"

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Construction Manager"

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Lorenzo Bianchi"

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Mayor"

msgid "MISSION_02_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Anton Zurbriggen"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_ACCEPT_1"
msgstr "Skiers bring money. That’s what you mean, Mr. Zurbriggen, am I right?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_ACCEPT_2"
msgstr "Uh, yes."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_ACCEPT_3"
msgstr "You can go home now, Mr. Zurbriggen."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_ACCEPT_4"
msgstr "Very well… err… Thank you very much… gentlemen…"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr "Naturally, it’s regrettable for picturesque reasons. But oh well."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr "The coach drivers will also curse it. But Zermatt will be prosperous."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr "Do you think so? I reckon this skiing thing is just a fad."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_4"
msgstr ""
"You will see: It’s just the same as with the automobile. It’ll take off!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_5"
msgstr ""
"Now you’re being ridiculous, Andrew! The automobile is a completely "
"senseless invention!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_DECLINE_1"
msgstr "Let us concentrate on our main task!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"My dear Dr. Brandtner, I have heard things are going well for you at the "
"Simplon Pass."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_TASK_1"
msgstr ""
"Well, I am the mayor of a small village named Zermatt. Every now and then, "
"however, motor-coaches full of skiers go astray and end up in our village."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_TASK_2"
msgstr ""
"That’s a mystery to me too, but you will have to speak to the police about "
"that. I don’t see how I am supposed to prevent that."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_TASK_3"
msgstr ""
"No, you misunderstand me. That is precisely the point: to bring more of "
"these people to Zermatt. Would you be willing to support us and build a "
"railroad from Brig to Zermatt?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BONUS_TASK_4"
msgstr ""
"A branch line to Zermatt would increase the demand on the main line. Skiers "
"in Milan traveling to Zermatt with just one change!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_1"
msgstr ""
"It’s time for us to deal with the debris. My workers have started to build a "
"pizza oven into the tunnel opening out of boredom."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_2"
msgstr ""
"There’s a mine dump deeper in the valley, on the other side of Gravellona."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_3"
msgstr "Fitting name…"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_4"
msgstr "You can explain that to us when we’re done here, Andrew."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_5"
msgstr ""
"The dump doesn’t have a cargo station. Doing it by truck alone would take "
"too long."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_1"
msgstr ""
"The train from Brig to Milan and our machine train share the track between "
"Domodossola and the tunnel construction site. We need to build a siding, so "
"the trains don’t get in each other’s way."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_2"
msgstr ""
"There seems to be a suitable location above Domodossola. The circular tunnel "
"for the ascent is already two-track!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_3"
msgstr ""
"It’s pronounced Domodossola. Fortunately, all we need now are switches "
"before and after it."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_4"
msgstr "Good. We can use that to our advantage."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_ELECTRIC_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr "Wonderful. Here’s to glorious times at the Simplon Pass."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"Good day, I am Dr. Karl Albert Brandtner. And you are Mr. Bianchi of Impresa "
"Generale di Costruzioni Bianchi & Figli?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_10"
msgstr ""
"I don’t understand it either, Professore. Sicily is nice and warm, but it’s "
"always too cold for me at the top of Mount Etna."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_11"
msgstr ""
"No one would think of going skiing there, right? May I introduce my "
"assistant, Andrew? He’s American!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_12"
msgstr "Good day, Signore Bianchi! It’s a pleasure to make your acquaintance."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_13"
msgstr ""
"Good day, Signore Andrea. I have a brother-in-law in New York, Massimo "
"Mazzola. Do you know him by any chance?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_14"
msgstr "No, I’m from New Orleans. That’s about as far as Hamburg to Palermo."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"Si, Professore! Road and rail construction have been my life ever since I "
"was a child down in Palermo! I’ve seen it all and built it all."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr "So I have heard. But you can read, can’t you?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"And write. And do arithmetic, Professore. Learned it all. I was a good "
"student. But too poor for high school."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr "Aha. Good. Are you familiar with the assignment?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr ""
"Si. We have a parallel ventilation shaft, which you already installed with "
"the first tunnel. This needs to be expanded. The line is to have a much "
"higher capacity!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr ""
"Well, that’s something. Where do you anticipate the greatest challenges?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr ""
"Passenger numbers will need to be maintained during construction. And at the "
"same time, we’ll also have the construction site vehicles to handle."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_INTRO_9"
msgstr ""
"Quite right, Mr. Bianchi. It is best that we increase the capacity during "
"the construction! Everyone wants to go skiing all of a sudden! Completely "
"irrational!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_1"
msgstr ""
"Ah, the best quality. There were far too many accidents caused by falling "
"rocks during the construction of the first tunnel. We want to avoid that!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_2"
msgstr ""
"Yes, there’s a reason why the developer switched contractors. Too many work "
"stoppages. That’s expensive!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_3"
msgstr ""
"Next, Professore, we need machines. I’ve already forwarded the specifiche to "
"the machine factory."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_4"
msgstr "I see. Did you discuss those with me?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_5"
msgstr "With myself. And I took the specifications from the plans."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MACHINERY_6"
msgstr "Very well."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_1"
msgstr ""
"It was a pleasure working with you, Bianchi. Your reputation is well "
"deserved, and I admit that my preconceptions were misguided."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_2"
msgstr "The pleasure is all mine. And I compliment you on your assistant."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_3"
msgstr ""
"Well, sadly, he’ll be leaving me soon. He’s moving to Norway, for love."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_4"
msgstr ""
"Ah, not a country that’s full of construction sites. Just fjords and fish. "
"What takes you there, Andrew?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_5"
msgstr ""
"I’m taking a little break. Learning how to fish. Starting a family. And then "
"looking for work somewhere in the world. I never stay anywhere long, "
"Lorenzo. But having a home port to return to every once in a while—I "
"wouldn’t mind that!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_6"
msgstr ""
"Everyone has to live their own life, as my mamma used to say. I wish you "
"luck! Professore? You too!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_7"
msgstr "Dottore, please. And I wish you the same, Mr. Bianchi."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_8"
msgstr "I know, Dottore. But to me, you’ll always be Professore!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_STATION_CHECKED_1"
msgstr ""
"The locomotive can pull four cars in any case, perhaps more. This way, we "
"can double the number of passengers and compensate for any possible "
"disruptions."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TRAIN_IMPROVEMENT_1"
msgstr ""
"Gentlemen, I have good news. The engineers in the canton of Zurich have done "
"it, we’re going electric."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TRAIN_IMPROVEMENT_2"
msgstr ""
"Allow me to introduce the Ce 6/8 II, colloquially known as the Crocodile."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TRAIN_IMPROVEMENT_3"
msgstr "Oh, che bellezza! So, now we have to electrify the line?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TRAIN_IMPROVEMENT_4"
msgstr ""
"Only as far as Domodossola. A Milanese conglomerate will take over south of "
"there!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TRAIN_IMPROVEMENT_5"
msgstr ""
"Damned northern Italian construction mafia. I guess there’s nothing we can "
"do about it. But electrifying the line as far as Domodossola—Domodossola, "
"Professore—is a nice job too."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_1"
msgstr ""
"First, we need support beams. Otherwise, the tunnel will collapse on us."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_2"
msgstr ""
"I’ve spoken to the logging camp already. The beams are ready. We just need "
"to pick them up and bring them to the construction site."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"I thought you wanted to know when the tunnel was tutti complete, Dottore?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr ""
"That’s right, Mr. Bianchi! Oh! Even the new track has been laid already?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr ""
"Certo, Dottore! We laid the second track and tidied up the construction site "
"so it’s picobello. Now two trains can pass each other."

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_START_1"
msgstr "Can you do that, Bianchi?"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_START_2"
msgstr "Of course, Professore! It is as good as done!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_START_3"
msgstr "Dottore will do. I’m not a professor!"

msgid "MISSION_02_CUTSCENE_TUNNEL_START_4"
msgstr "Of course, Professore!"

msgid "MISSION_02_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Train travel is booming, with more people than ever wanting to travel back "
"and forth between northern Italy and Switzerland. It’s just a pity that the "
"Simplon Tunnel only has a single track. However, the railroad company is "
"ready to invest. They’ve hired two top experts for the job: Dr. Karl Albert "
"Brandtner from Hamburg, and Lorenzo Bianchi, a Sicilian."

msgid "MISSION_02_GUIDE_VEHICLE_STORE_EXPLAIN_CATEGORIES"
msgstr "Make sure that the attached cars can carry passengers."

msgid "MISSION_02_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"Brig–Milan. Well, it looks like they’re finally going ahead with the "
"expansion of the Simplon Tunnel to two tracks. Not exactly simple, "
"especially with all the obstacles that keep cropping up! So, instead of "
"happening in 1912, it’s starting eight years later."

msgid "MISSION_02_LOCATION"
msgstr "Domodossola, Italy"

msgid "MISSION_02_MEDAL"
msgstr "Bring the skiers to Zermatt."

msgid "MISSION_02_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Bring the skiers to Zermatt."

msgid "MISSION_02_NAME"
msgstr "Alpine Crossing"

msgid "MISSION_02_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Expand the railroad line via the Simplon Pass and improve the train service "
"between Brig and Milan."

msgid "MISSION_02_STAR_1"
msgstr "Transport 300 passengers through the tunnel."

msgid "MISSION_02_STAR_2"
msgstr "Transport 300 passengers through the tunnel before 1924."

msgid "MISSION_02_STAR_3"
msgstr "Transport 300 passengers through the tunnel before 1923."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BEFORE_BONUS_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "What’s it about?"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BEFORE_BONUS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "You have heard quite right."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BEFORE_BONUS_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Person"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BEFORE_BONUS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "An unknown, rather modest-looking man would like to talk to you."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Of course! Break a leg!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "This skiing business doesn’t have a future!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Dottore, there’s sure to be a lot of money in it that will help us finance "
"the main line."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_NAME"
msgstr "Decide your Action"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Should we handle the line to [link=entity_zermatt]Zermatt[/link]?"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Gentlemen! We have a nice little side project for when things stall in the "
"tunnel. We’re off to Zermatt to lay some tracks. But anyone who goes skiing "
"will regret it!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Line"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BONUS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a train line between [link=entity_zermatt]Zermatt[/link] and "
"[link=entity_brig_station]Brig[/link] and transport the first passengers."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_STATION_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Change the terminal length in the construction settings on the right before "
"placing it."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_STATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We have approval for a 120-meter freight station right next to the mine "
"dump. That needs to be built first."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Build the Unloading Station"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_STATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a 120m long cargo station next to the [link=entity_dump_site]mine "
"dump[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_TRACKS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"There’s already a switch south of Domodossola that we can use to connect the "
"cargo station to the rail network."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_TRACKS_NAME"
msgstr "Build the Rails"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_DIRT_ROUTE_TRACKS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the tracks to connect the station at the [link=entity_dump_site]mine "
"dump[/link] to the [link=entity_track_domodossola]track[/link] south of "
"Domodossola."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_HINT"
msgstr "Install switches by dragging tracks between the yellow markers."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Now all we need are switches before and after it."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_NAME"
msgstr "Build Switches"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_BYPASS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the switches before and after the [link=entity_tunnel_loop]loop "
"tunnel[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_SIGNAL_HINT"
msgstr "Select the signals from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_SIGNAL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Don’t forget the signaling system to tell the trains when they can leave the "
"tunnel."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_SIGNAL_NAME"
msgstr "Build Signals"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUILD_FIRST_SIGNAL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build signals at the marked [link=entity_tunnel_loop]locations[/link] by the "
"switches."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_MACHINE_TRAIN_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Make sure your wagons are specialized for transporting flatbed cargo. "
"Specialized wagons have an improved loading speed."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_MACHINE_TRAIN_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "We need to buy a cargo train to transport the parts."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_MACHINE_TRAIN_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Train"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_MACHINE_TRAIN_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a specialized train for flatbed cargo in the "
"[link=entity_depot_domo]train depot[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_STONES_TRAIN_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We should purchase a train designed specifically for transporting gravel and "
"stones."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_STONES_TRAIN_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Train"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_BUY_STONES_TRAIN_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a train specialized in transporting bulk cargo in the nearby "
"[link=entity_depot_domo]depot[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CHECK_BRIG_STATION_HINT"
msgstr ""
"For each terminal, its length, its capacity and the number of waiting "
"passengers are shown."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CHECK_BRIG_STATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"May I ask you to focus on the task at hand? By the time the tunnel is "
"constructed, our clients expect a considerable increase in passenger "
"numbers. Let us take a look at the numbers for the station."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CHECK_BRIG_STATION_NAME"
msgstr "Open the Station Statistics"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CHECK_BRIG_STATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Open the details of the [link=entity_brig_station]station[/link] in Brig and "
"look at the terminal’s key metrics."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CLONE_STONES_TRAIN_HINT"
msgstr "Select the vehicle to open its details and use the clone function."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CLONE_STONES_TRAIN_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need a second train. The first one doesn’t have enough capacity. We need "
"another one of these."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CLONE_STONES_TRAIN_NAME"
msgstr "Clone the Train"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_CLONE_STONES_TRAIN_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Clone the [link=entity_stone_train]stone train[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_LOGS_HINT"
msgstr "Build a depot, buy a fitting truck and set up the line."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_LOGS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"First, we’ll need a vehicle depot near the logging camp. Then we need to set "
"up a transport route to the construction site."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_LOGS_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Wood"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_LOGS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver wood from the [link=entity_forest]logging camp[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_construction_tunnel]tunnel construction site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_CONTINUED_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "The siding is complete, Lorenzo. The machines should be arriving soon!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_CONTINUED_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Machines"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_CONTINUED_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver machines to the [link=entity_construction_tunnel]construction site[/"
"link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "The train is ready. I’ll tell the engineer what he needs to do!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Transport Line"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_MACHINES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a line from the [link=entity_station_domo]station[/link] in "
"Domodossola to the [link=entity_construction_tunnel]construction site[/link] "
"and assign the train to this line."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_STONES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"And now we should tell the engineer what he should load and unload, and "
"where."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_STONES_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Stones"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_DELIVER_STONES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the stones from the tunnel "
"[link=entity_construction_tunnel]construction site[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_dump_site]mine dump[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_COMPLETE_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "I’m on my way!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_COMPLETE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Professore, your presence is needed urgently at the tunnel!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_COMPLETE_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Lorenzo"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_TRAIN_HINT"
msgstr "Select the vehicle to open its details and use the replace function."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_TRAIN_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"So, Professore. Now we can hit the tracks in this beauty—what’s its name "
"again? Tschi e sei otto due? Coccodrillo Svizzero!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_TRAIN_NAME"
msgstr "Replace the Train"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIC_TRAIN_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Replace the [link=entity_pers_train]passenger train[/link] with a new train "
"made up of the Ce 6/8 II and matching passenger cars."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIFY_HINT"
msgstr "Select the electrification tool from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIFY_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Let’s get started with the electrification before his German pronunciation "
"drives me crazy."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIFY_NAME"
msgstr "Electrify the Tracks"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_ELECTRIFY_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Electrify the line from [link=entity_brig_station]Brig[/link] to "
"[link=entity_station_domo]Domodossola[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_HIGHER_RATE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Now the tracks are open for more traffic on the Simplon line. The tunnel "
"serves only one purpose: more passengers! Lots more passengers."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_HIGHER_RATE_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Passengers"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_HIGHER_RATE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Transport 300 passengers through the [link=pos_tunnel]tunnel[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_1_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Build the three signals at the siding south of Domodossola. Otherwise, we "
"can’t put it into operation."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_1_NAME"
msgstr "Build Signals"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_1_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the three signals at the marked [link=signals2_pos]locations[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_2_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"And now build the three signals in the opposite direction. This will "
"significantly improve the flow of traffic!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_2_NAME"
msgstr "Build Signals"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_LARGE_BYPASS_SIGNALS_2_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build the three signals at the marked [link=signals2_pos]locations[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_MISSION_END_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Oh, indeed!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_MISSION_END_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Mr. Brandtner, I think we did it."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_MISSION_END_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Andrew"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_SELL_VEHICLES_HINT"
msgstr ""
"All relevant lines now have a notification, because the vehicles cannot load "
"and unload cargo at the tunnel anymore. Delete the cargo lines to sell all "
"vehicles automatically."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_SELL_VEHICLES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Perfect timing. I guess we can sell the spoil train and the trucks again "
"now. That’ll bring in a little extra cash on the used market."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_SELL_VEHICLES_NAME"
msgstr "Sell the Cargo Vehicles"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_SELL_VEHICLES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Sell the cargo vehicles that were used at the tunnel construction site."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_TRAIN_LONGER_COMPLETE_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let’s get started!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_TRAIN_LONGER_COMPLETE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The extended train seems to be an acceptable stopgap for now. So, we should "
"make sure to get the construction site operational quickly."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_TRAIN_LONGER_COMPLETE_NAME"
msgstr "Start the Construction"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_VEHICLE_STORE_HINT"
msgstr "Select the vehicle to open its details and use the modify function."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_VEHICLE_STORE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "See to that, Andrew!"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_VEHICLE_STORE_NAME"
msgstr "Extend the Train"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_VEHICLE_STORE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Modify the [link=entity_pers_train]train[/link] and add at least two "
"additional passenger cars."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_WAIT_FOR_MACHINES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Now we have to wait for the machines to arrive."

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_WAIT_FOR_MACHINES_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Machines"

msgid "MISSION_02_TASK_WAIT_FOR_MACHINES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver machines to the [link=entity_construction_tunnel]construction site[/"
"link]."

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "Archaeologist"

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Nasra Ramahi"

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Bedouin"

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Salim Al-Zalabia"

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Explorer"

msgid "MISSION_03_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Baron von Schlitzwiesen"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_BERGUNG_1"
msgstr ""
"Nasra, there’s an old quarry here. On the way there, one of the Bedouin "
"scouts found a man’s body by the lonely mountain. Or what was left of it."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_BERGUNG_2"
msgstr "The desert shows no mercy, Andrew."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_BERGUNG_3"
msgstr "The workers are asking what we should do with the body."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_BERGUNG_4"
msgstr ""
"We will retrieve him and give him a proper burial here. It is the decent "
"thing to do."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_BERGUNG_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"We found a skeleton wearing American clothes and a brown hat, holding a whip "
"in its hand. Other than that, we found nothing that could help identify him. "
"May his soul rest in peace."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_DIESEL_1"
msgstr ""
"We have arrived in the old town. And the English must have been in a great "
"hurry. There’s still lots of fuel lying around here."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_DIESEL_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"Well, whatever comes our way next, at least we won’t have to worry about "
"fuel anymore!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_1"
msgstr ""
"Those are… pottery fragments with Egyptian hieroglyphs. How did they get "
"here? This was Babylonia. They used cuneiform. Not hieroglyphs. Did the "
"Egyptians ever rule here?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_10"
msgstr "Our dear friend, the highly esteemed Baron von…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_11"
msgstr "Max von Schlatzenfaxen."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_12"
msgstr ""
"…Max von Schlatzenfaxen, has unfortunately become lost in the desert. My "
"Bedouins are searching for him, but the chances of finding him alive are "
"slim."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_13"
msgstr "How dreadful!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_14"
msgstr "He must have completely misunderstood one of my directions!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_15"
msgstr ""
"Let’s hope you don’t make a habit of it. But at least we have this discovery…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_16"
msgstr "Oh yes, Salim. You must take a look… a global sensation!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_2"
msgstr "Ah, you know …"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_3"
msgstr "It was a rhetorical question: No, they didn’t. This is sensational!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_4"
msgstr "Here comes Salim. The German can’t be far behind."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_5"
msgstr ""
"And he will claim all the glory for himself… But there is no way I am "
"marrying him! Over my dead body!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_6"
msgstr ""
"As-salamu alaykum, Nasra. No, you will not marry him, flower of the desert."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_7"
msgstr "Because you’ve ensured that, esteemed Sheikh?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_8"
msgstr "A terrible tragedy has occurred."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_END_9"
msgstr "Another one. What is it this time?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_EXCAVATION_1"
msgstr ""
"I had thought making it here would have given me some sense of triumph. But "
"all I feel is defeat."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_EXCAVATION_2"
msgstr "Still, all our machines are ready. All that’s left to do now is dig."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_EXCAVATION_3"
msgstr "Why should we do that?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_EXCAVATION_4"
msgstr "Because the digging will distract you, Nasra. It’s what you love!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_EXCAVATION_5"
msgstr "Yes, you are right. I need a distraction."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"Salim Al-Zalabia, my name is Nasra Ramahi. May Allah always bless you with "
"His mercy. My father sends his best wishes and regards!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_10"
msgstr ""
"Maintenance? That is possible. Repairs? Not so much. But indeed, there are "
"safe places where we Bedouins have rested for centuries."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_11"
msgstr "Andrew will handle the details."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_12"
msgstr ""
"Esteemed Sheikh Al-Zalabia, I’ve marked your old Bedouin camps on this map. "
"May I have your permission to store maintenance tools there?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_13"
msgstr ""
"I will instruct my tribe leaders to permit this for my old friend’s daughter."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"And he sends me the flower of the desert, his dearly beloved daughter. May "
"Allah, praised be His name, protect you in all your endeavors."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr "So, you know what this is about?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"You mean to go to Wadi Rum to carry out excavations—an undertaking that "
"demands everything, even of the most fearless men."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr ""
"Well, I have Andrew, my right-hand man, and others will come along. I have "
"my father’s full backing."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr ""
"The wish of my friend and business partner is my command. I will do "
"everything within my power to assist you."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr "We need to get our convoy of trucks from Aqaba to the excavation site."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr ""
"Trucks are heavy and sand is light, and yet in the end, sand always "
"prevails. It can devour even the largest of resources."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_INTRO_9"
msgstr ""
"I was told there are places in the desert that we can use for maintenance "
"and repairs."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_1"
msgstr "Miss Ramahi! I have been expecting you. Charming, simply charming."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_10"
msgstr ""
"I think I’m slowly beginning to understand what went wrong with colonialism…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_11"
msgstr "Baron, let the King know that I am his loyal servant."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_12"
msgstr ""
"Very good. Gentlemen? A good day to you! My lady? I kiss your hand! Truly "
"enchanting!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_13"
msgstr ""
"Someone needs to pay the King a visit and tell him about this German robber "
"baron."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_14"
msgstr "It won’t make any difference."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_15"
msgstr "We will find a way, Nasra."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_16"
msgstr ""
"Good. Let’s carry on and let that German think everything is fine. Where is "
"this steel mill located?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_2"
msgstr "And your name is Schlitzwiesen, I presume."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_3"
msgstr ""
"Baron von Schlitzwiesen, please, my dear lady. My family’s history stretches "
"back to the 12th century."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_4"
msgstr "And to what do I owe the honor of your visit?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_5"
msgstr ""
"Well, I took the liberty of informing King Hussein that I successfully "
"connected the old ore mine to the road network."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_6"
msgstr "That YOU connected it? That was…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_7"
msgstr ""
"He was very pleased and asked me to let you know that he would be most happy "
"to resume ore deliveries to an old steel mill that should be around here "
"somewhere. The sheikh should know where exactly."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_8"
msgstr "Indeed, yes…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_IRON_9"
msgstr ""
"And the King also ordered Mr. Al-Zalabia to provide me with his full support "
"in all my future endeavors."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_1"
msgstr ""
"Miss Ramahi, your beauty grows by the day. You must come with me to see the "
"King! I must ask him for your hand!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_10"
msgstr ""
"A woman as lead author? No renowned journal would accept that! If I could "
"speak with you briefly, Mr. Zalabia, just the two of us…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_11"
msgstr ""
"I have to accompany the German. You are on the final stretch to your "
"excavation site now. Nothing should go wrong from here. Ma’salama, Nasra Al-"
"Ramahi."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_12"
msgstr "Zalabia betrayed me. I’m calling the whole thing off!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_13"
msgstr "Don’t do that. And you’re wrong, Nasra. Trust the sheikh."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_14"
msgstr ""
"I am just a woman to him, and now he is scheming with that Schlitzweasel."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_15"
msgstr ""
"I suggest we make our way to the excavation site first. And then you can "
"talk to him again."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_16"
msgstr "You are right, Andrew. Now is not the time for giving up."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_2"
msgstr ""
"The young lady’s father is the person to approach with such requests, sir."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_3"
msgstr "But I am already engaged, Mr. Schlitzikowski."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_4"
msgstr ""
"Baron von Schlitzwiesen. Not just a pretty face, this little one. Feisty. I "
"like that! You were engaged, but your fiancé is dead, and our marriage will "
"be a good business transaction."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_5"
msgstr "Here it comes—a steel mill for a wedding."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_6"
msgstr ""
"Americans! So naïve! I am but a representative of the steel mill. And "
"naturally, there will be no marriage until the results of my excavation are "
"published!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_7"
msgstr "YOUR excavation?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_8"
msgstr ""
"Well, naturally, I am not going to get my own hands dirty. But on the bright "
"side, it means my little Nasra gets to be listed as co-author in the "
"publication."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_9"
msgstr "Co-author? When I am the one doing all the work?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_1"
msgstr ""
"I see you have brought an impressive amount of excellent equipment, Mr…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_10"
msgstr ""
"And that is why he enjoys my trust. Let us begin. We need to transport tools "
"to the old iron mine."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_2"
msgstr "Andrew. Just call me Andrew."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_3"
msgstr ""
"Our plans are ambitious, indeed. This time, we want to get ahead of the "
"Europeans with the next great discoveries in our region."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_4"
msgstr ""
"I wanted to talk to you about that, Nasra. A European spoke to me a few days "
"ago. A German aristocrat. He appeared to have no lack of goodwill from the "
"royal family."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_5"
msgstr "What does that mean for us?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_6"
msgstr ""
"It means we have to prepare ourselves for difficulties. Orders from the "
"royal family cannot simply be ignored."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_7"
msgstr ""
"But there is something else. After the war, the English left behind several "
"factories and an iron mine here. Officially, they now belong to us. But what "
"use are factories to us Bedouins?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_8"
msgstr ""
"You are traders, esteemed Sheikh. If we restore access to these factories, "
"and you present them to the royal family as a gift…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_OASIS_9"
msgstr ""
"…then King Hussein might be a little less impressed by the German. Your "
"American has his head screwed on, Nasra."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_1"
msgstr "You are, without a doubt, the daughter of your great father, Nasra."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_2"
msgstr ""
"Shukran—thank you, Sheikh Al-Zalabia. But unfortunately, our work here is "
"not yet finished."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_3"
msgstr "And I see our German friend is hot on our heels. Here he comes now…"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_4"
msgstr "A very good day to you, gentlemen! Miss Ramahi, enchanté!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_5"
msgstr "Let me guess, Mr. von Schlitzewitz: new agreements with the King?"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_6"
msgstr ""
"Baron von Schlitzwiesen, if you please. Yes, naturally. He was quite taken "
"with my idea of putting the old machine factory back in proper working order."

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_7"
msgstr ""
"Well then, now that everything is in order, a hotel in Aqaba awaits, "
"complete with air conditioning and a shower. Gentlemen? Miss Ramahi? "
"Charming, truly!"

msgid "MISSION_03_CUTSCENE_STEEL_8"
msgstr ""
"Well, now we have to find that old British machine factory. Any hints, dear "
"Sheikh?"

msgid "MISSION_03_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Following her archaeology studies, Nasra Ramahi, the eldest daughter of a "
"wealthy Jordanian diplomat family, is returning to her hometown of Aqaba. "
"Like the British explorers excavating in the neighboring city of Petra, she "
"wants to make a name for herself. Using her family’s wealth, Nasra plans a "
"desert expedition to search for artifacts in Wadi Rum."

msgid "MISSION_03_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"All the years of frustration led me to where I am now: at the start of a "
"seemingly impossible task. It is not my first, and I have overcome them all "
"so far. Perhaps at the end of this challenge, I will etch my name indelibly "
"into the annals of archaeology."

msgid "MISSION_03_LOCATION"
msgstr "Wadi Rum, Jordan"

msgid "MISSION_03_MEDAL"
msgstr "Recover the remains."

msgid "MISSION_03_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Recover the remains."

msgid "MISSION_03_NAME"
msgstr "Desert Adventure"

msgid "MISSION_03_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Accompany Nasra on her expedition through the desert and unearth artifacts."

msgid "MISSION_03_STAR_1"
msgstr "Complete the excavations."

msgid "MISSION_03_STAR_2"
msgstr "Lose fewer than 3 trucks before the excavations are complete."

msgid "MISSION_03_STAR_3"
msgstr "Lose no trucks before the excavations are complete."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_BERGUNG_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Search around in the ruins to find the remains, it is worth a medal of honor."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_BERGUNG_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Let’s retrieve the corpse and bury it."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_BERGUNG_NAME"
msgstr "Find the Remains"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_BERGUNG_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Select the remains of the dead adventurer from the "
"[link=pos_lonely_mountain]ruins[/link] beyond the lonely mountain so he can "
"be given a proper burial."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_EXCAVATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"What will help Nasra most right now is a distraction—ideally by kicking off "
"the excavation and quickly making a significant find!"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_EXCAVATION_NAME"
msgstr "Excavate"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_EXCAVATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Dig in the [link=excavation_pos]highlighted area[/link] with the "
"terraforming tool to start the excavation. Select the artefacts."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_FATAL_MAINTENANCE_HINT"
msgstr ""
"They will not suffer any damage when close to successfully erected camps. "
"Use waypoints to enforce the correct route for the vehicles."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_FATAL_MAINTENANCE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need to make sure we schedule regular enough maintenance stops—keep a "
"close eye on the condition of our trucks! Once they start falling apart, "
"we’ll never get them going again!"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_FATAL_MAINTENANCE_NAME"
msgstr "Protect the Trucks"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_FATAL_MAINTENANCE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Ensure your trucks stay well-maintained, you will lose them when their "
"condition drops to 0%."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_GET_TO_OASIS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Al-Zalabia lives a little outside Aqaba. I suggest we set up our first "
"maintenance camp there. That will make him feel more involved in the "
"operation. He doesn’t trust me."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_GET_TO_OASIS_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Tools"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_GET_TO_OASIS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_tools]tools[/link] with trucks from the "
"[link=entity_depot]depot[/link] to the marked [link=entity_oasis]location[/"
"link] outside Aqaba."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_EXCAVATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"All right. It is up to us now. We should have enough experience in the "
"desert to find the safe route ourselves. First, let’s analyze the terrain! "
"The machines need firm ground."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_EXCAVATION_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Machines"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_EXCAVATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver machines to the [link=entity_excavation_site]excavation site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_IRON_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Solve Salim's riddle to identify the right one of the three paths. Deliver "
"tools to the camp sites along this path to set up maintenance camps. Use the "
"line manager to adjust the line after a camp is constructed to move forward "
"to the next camp site."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_IRON_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The desert lays its traps, Nasra. The direct route can be deceptive, a Fata "
"Morgana. But it almost always rewards those who stick to the right path."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_IRON_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Tools"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_IRON_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_tools]tools[/link] to the [link=entity_mine]iron mine[/"
"link]."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_MACHINES_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Follow Salim’s wise words to find the right path between the sand dunes."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_MACHINES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Sand is like water: It swallows the heavy and carries the light. Big dunes "
"are like big waves. Only attempt to cross them if you can swim."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_MACHINES_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Steel"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_MACHINES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver steel from the [link=entity_steel_mill]steel mill[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_machine_factory]machine factory[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_STEEL_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Salim's words once again help to identify the correct route where camps can "
"be set up. You may use multiple trucks on different lines and build "
"warehouses to transport cargo efficiently."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_STEEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"I have marked it here. Remember: The desert knows life. A detour will get "
"you where you need to go. Most of the time. A step back often provides the "
"required perspective."

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_STEEL_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Iron Ore"

msgid "MISSION_03_TASK_RIDDLE_STEEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver iron ore from the [link=entity_mine]mines[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_steel_mill]steel mill[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_04_ANDREW_REMINDER"
msgstr ""
"Hey, what’s going on with this stage? It’s still not up. We need to speed "
"things up."

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "Producer"

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Bart Korner"

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Sheriff"

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Richard O'Sullivan"

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Spectator"

msgid "MISSION_04_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Sun Flowers"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_BLANKETS_DELIVERED_1"
msgstr "Thanks, this could’ve ended really badly. What a storm!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_1"
msgstr "They’re your father’s nightmare!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_2"
msgstr "They don’t walk down the street like normal people."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_3"
msgstr "They were sent from heaven—prophets with amplifiers."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_4"
msgstr "Direct from London, England."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_5"
msgstr "Here comes our generation! Here come THE WHAT!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_ENDING_6"
msgstr ""
"Hey, brother! Grooviest festival ever! And I should know—I’ve been bothering "
"organizers at them all!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_FOOD_1"
msgstr ""
"Korner, this won’t do. You can’t just go blasting your uncivilized music "
"here for three days and not offer folks something to eat!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_FOOD_2"
msgstr ""
"Yo, freaks! The people are hungry. Is there anything to eat? Donuts? Veggie "
"burger stands? Anything?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_FOOD_3"
msgstr ""
"Cops and hippies united against me! I shoulda stayed with the record company."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INSTRUMENTS_1"
msgstr ""
"Ricky Heaven just dropped by: The truck carrying his instruments has gotten "
"stuck! The traffic is backing up all around."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INSTRUMENTS_2"
msgstr "Our opening act?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INSTRUMENTS_3"
msgstr "But he’s prepared to perform with borrowed instruments."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INSTRUMENTS_FOUND_1"
msgstr ""
"Okay, Ricky can start. He’ll get everyone warmed up for the headline act. I "
"get the feeling this could be his big break!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INSTRUMENTS_FOUND_2"
msgstr ""
"Yours too, Boss. I’ve seen it all before. But never anything like this!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"…Picture it, Richie: Jane Hopkins, Jimmy Heinrichs, Joe Coachman, The What!—"
"all in one field. Peace, music, love, and revolution. It’s gonna be bigger "
"than any one of us. This is gonna be eternal."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"I don’t know about that. I would have shut it down, but the judge thought "
"otherwise. Still, you’re dancing to my tune here."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr ""
"Forget it, Sheriff. This is freedom of expression! First Amendment! Art! And "
"also, private property…"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"And they’re forecasting rain. You really want to set up the amps and lights "
"in the mud? Without a proper stage, all those electric guitars are going to "
"be way too dangerous."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr "Sure thing, Sheriff. Of course we’re gonna put up a proper stage!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr "Aren’t you too old to be fooling around like this, Mr…?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr ""
"Andrew. Just Andrew, my son. I was there at the turn of the century to see "
"the birth of jazz in New Orleans. Let the young folks do their thing!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr "All right, the stage. Let’s give the sheriff what he wants."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_NO_SMOKING_1"
msgstr ""
"Backed-up traffic, missing instruments, people going hungry, diarrhea. Now a "
"flood of biblical proportions, and the sheriff wants me to bribe him. The "
"hippie’s back on his feet, I hear, and there’s no rainbow in sight. I give "
"up."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_NO_SMOKING_2"
msgstr "Hey, Barty boy! You got a light? My… uh… campfire went out."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_NO_SMOKING_3"
msgstr "This is a no-smoking area."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_NO_SMOKING_4"
msgstr ""
"No-smoking area? Don’t be so uncool, man. Guess I’ll just ask the sheriff "
"then. He’s up for re-election in November and can’t afford to disappoint the "
"voters."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_NO_SMOKING_5"
msgstr "Andrew, the hippie just delivered me my rainbow!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_1"
msgstr "Korner, are you out of your mind?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_10"
msgstr "Mississippi. 1906. Don’t you remember?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_11"
msgstr "Now all I need is that hippie to show up."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_12"
msgstr "He’s lying in his tent, looking pretty pale…"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_13"
msgstr "I’ve got too much on my plate Andrew, deal with it."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_1_FAILED_1"
msgstr ""
"Looks like I have no choice but to clear out your festival. The conditions "
"here are unacceptable."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_2"
msgstr "What’s the problem, Sheriff?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_3"
msgstr "You’re dumping all of your visitors’ excrement into the river?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_4"
msgstr ""
"Do you see any sewage pipes around here? The stuff in the toilets has to go "
"somewhere. So, we’ve had to improvise. What’s the problem?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_5"
msgstr ""
"Go ask at your medical tent. Folks are bathing in the river! There are "
"dozens out there puking their guts up!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_6"
msgstr "Oops. Didn’t mean for that to happen!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_7"
msgstr ""
"I don’t give a crap! Go fetch medication from Bethel. Fast—or I’m pulling "
"the plug. And then hire a company to clean the toilets regularly!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_8"
msgstr "I hate to say I told you so, Boss."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_9"
msgstr "Did you?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_POISON_AVERTED_1"
msgstr "This is the last time I turn a blind eye. Keep away from the river."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_1"
msgstr "Okay… Korner here, what’s up?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_2"
msgstr ""
"Korner, I wish you nothing but bad luck, really I do, but I’ve got to warn "
"you: There’s a storm brewing. The wind’s picking up, and the sky’s like "
"lead. Give it an hour and the rain will be coming down in buckets."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_3"
msgstr ""
"Is that supposed to shock me, Richie? Apparently, someone tried to ride "
"their Harley into the side of a tent somewhere on the grounds and launch "
"themselves into the air! And you’re telling me I’m gonna need an ark!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_4"
msgstr ""
"No need for an ark. The campgrounds will survive. But I want you to round up "
"blankets and everything you can to treat hypothermia."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_5"
msgstr ""
"Because of a few drops of rain? They’re not gonna melt out there. And it’s "
"August! This is ridic… oh… I see. Where can I get the blankets?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_RAIN_6"
msgstr "My brother-in-law has a textile factory nearby. Make my family happy."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_SEWAGE_RIVER_1"
msgstr "That’ll do for now. Just keep an eye on it."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_1"
msgstr "Good thing the World Health Organization called off its visit."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_2"
msgstr "We’re doing everything we can."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_3"
msgstr ""
"Any progress on the continuous waste disposal front? The toilets will be "
"overflowing again soon."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_4"
msgstr "We’re in negotiations."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_5"
msgstr ""
"Let’s hope they’re quick. Until there’s proper disposal in place, none of "
"those savages are going on stage."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_6"
msgstr "Negotiations? That’s the first I’ve heard."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_7"
msgstr ""
"That’s because they’re not happening. I just wanted to get rid of the "
"sheriff. I’ll sort it with the sewage plant right away."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_STEADYSEWAGE_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"You can breathe easy again, Boss. The sewage plant operator’s dealing with "
"the wastewater from now on!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_1"
msgstr ""
"Guess the farmers ’round here care more about profit than culture, decency, "
"and taste in music. All right. The festival can continue for now."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_2"
msgstr ""
"Food first, revolution later! Anyways, we can’t let supplies run out. You "
"see to that, Andrew!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_3"
msgstr "Sure thing."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_4"
msgstr ""
"Listen up. Get some toilets in here, Korner. The people are pouring in. And "
"they’re crapping all over the place! This stops now, or this horror show is "
"over!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_5"
msgstr ""
"We oughta deal with the toilet situation. O’Sullivan might just be a cop, "
"but he’s got a point…"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILETS_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"Okay, I think that should be enough for now. Let’s just hope people actually "
"use them—and don't just go in the woods."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_1"
msgstr ""
"Peace, brother. The toilets are totally overflowing! Someone tossed a uke in "
"there too, and now… it’s floating everywhere, man."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_2"
msgstr "A ukulele? Then of course it’s overflowing. Whose idea was that?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_3"
msgstr ""
"That’s what I said, dude. A triangle, that’d be totally cool. But a uke? Way "
"too big, man! But no one ever listens to me!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_4"
msgstr ""
"Okay, let’s stay pragmatic. More visitors need more toilets. You’ve dealt "
"with this before, back in New Orleans."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_5"
msgstr "We had the Mississippi there. That washed all our filth away."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_6"
msgstr "That’s the solution."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_TOILET_OVERFLOW_7"
msgstr "But everything that came downstream ended up on our doorstep."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_VEGETABLES_1"
msgstr ""
"Hey, dude. Pretty uncool that all we can get to eat around here is dead "
"animals."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_VEGETABLES_2"
msgstr ""
"Do you want to eat living animals? What are you, some kind of survivalist?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_VEGETABLES_3"
msgstr ""
"Man, we wanna heal the world. Vegetables! The revolution needs vegetables!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_VEGETABLES_4"
msgstr "Are you all crazy?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_VEGETABLES_5"
msgstr ""
"Hey, peace, man. Salad and pumpkins for everyone, that’s all we’re asking "
"for. We gonna televise the revolution or starve, man?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_1"
msgstr ""
"Uh, Boss. Speaking of that… The What are refusing to trudge through the mud "
"from Bethel to the stage. They say it’s either by air or not at all. They "
"don’t play in rain boots."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_10"
msgstr "And congratulations on your re-election!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_11"
msgstr "Just this one time. And I won’t get fooled again!"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_2"
msgstr ""
"What? They’re our first headliners. We need a helicopter. We need "
"O’Sullivan! Give me the radio."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_3"
msgstr "What is it?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_4"
msgstr "Richie, we need your police helicopter."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_5"
msgstr "Are you out of your mind, Korner? No way. Why should I?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_6"
msgstr ""
"You want the youth vote in November, don’t you? You wouldn’t want the deal "
"with your brother-in-law to come to light, would you?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_7"
msgstr "You’re a real scumbag, Korner! What do you want me to do?"

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_8"
msgstr ""
"Tell the chopper to fly The What here from Bethel. And fast! Ricky Heaven’s "
"started to improvise! Things’ll go south if this goes on any longer."

msgid "MISSION_04_CUTSCENE_WHAT_9"
msgstr "I hate you, Korner."

msgid "MISSION_04_DESC"
msgstr ""
"A dairy pasture is the inadvertent center of a musical revolution. A "
"festival the likes of which the world has never seen is about to take place "
"here: Woodstock! The only trouble is, world-famous bands are turning up, and "
"the organizer can’t let things get out of hand. The sheriff would have shut "
"it down before it even started, but he cannot stop it without good reason."

msgid "MISSION_04_GUIDE_INSTRUMENTS_1"
msgstr ""
"Some hippie left his guitar among the tents. We’ll borrow that for a little "
"while."

msgid "MISSION_04_GUIDE_INSTRUMENTS_2"
msgstr ""
"Hey, guys. Some freak left his electric piano to the left of the stage. Do "
"you need it, or can I use it as a table in our tent?"

msgid "MISSION_04_GUIDE_INSTRUMENTS_3"
msgstr ""
"The bass player from the Bethel fire brigade band lent us his instrument. He "
"left it at the end of the long path. Guess he didn’t want to be seen on the "
"festival grounds."

msgid "MISSION_04_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"Being the first at something. Well, this will be a first, perhaps even a one-"
"of-a-kind: the greatest rock festival of all time. Legends will be born, "
"global stars, and incredible music. I will build a legend greater than Neil "
"Armstrong."

msgid "MISSION_04_LOCATION"
msgstr "Bethel, United States"

msgid "MISSION_04_MEDAL"
msgstr "Find the instruments."

msgid "MISSION_04_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Find the instruments."

msgid "MISSION_04_NAME"
msgstr "Biggest Festival Ever"

msgid "MISSION_04_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Help the music producer with his festival preparations and get the band on "
"stage."

msgid "MISSION_04_STAR_1"
msgstr "Start the concert with 500 attendees."

msgid "MISSION_04_STAR_2"
msgstr "Start the concert with 750 attendees."

msgid "MISSION_04_STAR_3"
msgstr "Start the concert with 1000 attendees."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_INSTRUMENTS_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "For you, always"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_INSTRUMENTS_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "Not right now"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_INSTRUMENTS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Boss, you got a minute?"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_INSTRUMENTS_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Andrew"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_INSTRUMENTS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Andrew has a problem."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_POISON_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "All right"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_POISON_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "The sheriff. And he’s adamant he sees you “right now.”"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_POISON_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Sheriff"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_POISON_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "The sheriff is angry and wants to talk to you immediately."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_TOILETS_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let him in"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_TOILETS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "That hippie’s outside."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_TOILETS_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Sun Flowers"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BEFORE_TOILETS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Sun Flowers has a complaint."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BLANKETS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "A sign! All right. I’ll go get those blankets."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BLANKETS_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Blankets"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BLANKETS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_fabric]blankets[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BUILD_STAGE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"See if you can’t find a few music fans among the local lumberjacks who can "
"sell us some cheap scrap wood and deliver it. It’s only gotta last three "
"days."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BUILD_STAGE_NAME"
msgstr "Build the Stage"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_BUILD_STAGE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_forest]wood[/link] to the [link=entity_stage]stage "
"construction site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_EMPTY_TOILET_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"For three days, it’ll be enough to dump the stuff in the river. See to it."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_EMPTY_TOILET_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Sewage"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_EMPTY_TOILET_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the wastewater to the [link=entity_dump]disposal site[/link] on the "
"river."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_FOOD_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Hey, there’s a canning factory not too far from here. Beef, I think. We just "
"need to transport it."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_FOOD_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Canned Food"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_FOOD_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_food]canned food[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link] so that at least half of the tents "
"are supplied."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_GROWTH_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Supply the required cargo and hold positive ratings to let the camp grow."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_GROWTH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Looking pretty good here. But to make this all worthwhile, we’re gonna need "
"at least 500 visitors! Better yet, 1,000."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_GROWTH_NAME"
msgstr "Attract a Crowd"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_GROWTH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Grow the [link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link] to at least 500 attendees."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_INSTRUMENTS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"All right, we’ve got this. See if you can find any we can borrow from the "
"audience. There must be hundreds of six-strings out there."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_INSTRUMENTS_NAME"
msgstr "Find the Instruments"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_INSTRUMENTS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Select all 3 instrument cases on the grounds around the "
"[link=entity_stage]stage[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_POISON_HINT"
msgstr "Use enough trucks to deliver the required medicine in time."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_POISON_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"There’s a pharmacy in Bethel. We need tablets for vomiting and diarrhea."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_POISON_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Medicine"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_POISON_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver medicine from [link=entity_pharmacy]Bethel[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link] before it’s too late."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_RAIN_TRIGGER_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Hand it over"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_RAIN_TRIGGER_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Boss, the sheriff is on the radio."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_RAIN_TRIGGER_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Sheriff"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_RAIN_TRIGGER_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "The sheriff is trying to warn us."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_STEADYSEWAGE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need a continuous transport service between the sewage plant and the "
"festival toilets, so they don’t overflow."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_STEADYSEWAGE_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Sewage"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_STEADYSEWAGE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the wastewater to the [link=entity_sewage_facility]sewage plant[/"
"link] south of the campgrounds."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TOILETS_HINT"
msgstr "Select the toilets from the construction menu below."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TOILETS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"You take care of the toilets, and I’ll get to writing a book: Revolution for "
"Dummies…"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TOILETS_NAME"
msgstr "Build Toilets"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TOILETS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Build 3 toilets in [link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link] area."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TRIGGER_FINAL_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Stage clear"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TRIGGER_FINAL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Folks are getting impatient for things to get started. Are we ready for the "
"first main act?"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TRIGGER_FINAL_NAME"
msgstr "Start the Show"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_TRIGGER_FINAL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Give Bart the “stage clear” signal. Then there’s no going back."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_VEGETABLES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"There’s gotta be a farm around here somewhere. Get some vegetables! Quick. "
"Or Bart’s gonna flip."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_VEGETABLES_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Vegetables"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_VEGETABLES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_vegetables]vegetables[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_camping]campgrounds[/link] so that at least half of the tents "
"are supplied."

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_WHAT_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"O’Sullivan to chopper. Bring me The What. And tell them to leave the chopper "
"in one piece, or else I’ll impound the drummer’s sticks!"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_WHAT_NAME"
msgstr "Transport The What"

msgid "MISSION_04_TASK_WHAT_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport The What from the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link] to behind the "
"[link=entity_stage]stage[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_05_ANDREW_HARBOR"
msgstr ""
"We need to build the infrastructure piece by piece. The moment the first oil "
"delivery reaches the refinery, we’ll start making money. Then we’ll be able "
"to expand our supply chain."

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "Entrepreneur"

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Nils Eriksen"

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Corporate Agent"

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Astrid Larsson"

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Assistant"

msgid "MISSION_05_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Andrea"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_1"
msgstr ""
"Congratulations. That find was more than I’d expected from your band of "
"deckhands. But I’m afraid it still won’t be enough. I’ve already secured the "
"best locations."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_2"
msgstr ""
"You have the better equipment, more money, and maybe the better drilling "
"sites too. But my “deckhands” have something your people don’t. They have a "
"home to lose."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_3"
msgstr ""
"And that’s going to find you oil? Fish oil maybe. You don’t stand a chance. "
"And don’t go getting any stupid ideas: My drilling sites are well secured!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_4"
msgstr "Nice one, Boss."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_5"
msgstr ""
"Those were hollow words, Andrea. And Larsson knows it. We need to find more "
"oil!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_6"
msgstr ""
"Let’s find more oil then! We could check out how strong her security really "
"is. My great-uncle Andrew from New Orleans says you’ve got to be flexible in "
"this line of work."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_7"
msgstr "You have a great-uncle from New Orleans?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_1_8"
msgstr "He managed the logistics at Woodstock, but he’s 80 now and retired."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_1"
msgstr ""
"Nils, Nils, Nils. And I was so close to making you my right-hand man. Get "
"out of my oil fields, or your love for your homeland will land you behind "
"bars."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_2"
msgstr "It was worth a try. But we should be more careful next time."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_FAILURE_1"
msgstr ""
"Listen up, buddy. Playing dirty is an expensive part of the business. We've "
"got the money, you don't. Why can't you just accept that?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_FAILURE_2"
msgstr ""
"Because I’m not going to leave Norway’s oil and its nature for you sharks to "
"devour."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_FAILURE_3"
msgstr ""
"I’ve informed the authorities of your scheming. At least you won’t be on the "
"streets or going hungry for the next few years."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"Nils! You’re planning to go up against me? What a waste. You could have been "
"my right-hand man."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"We will extract this oil without ruining Norway in the process. You have "
"money, we have public opinion. And we will establish the Norwegian oil "
"industry! That license will be ours."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr ""
"What a pity! All right then, you go ahead and celebrate your little founding "
"party. See you!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr "Bad news, Boss?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr "We need to pick up the pace. Is our survey ship ready?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr "It’s in the port. We just need to brief the crew."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"This is Lasse. Three days ago, my boat was smashed against the rocks in the "
"storm. I’m stuck in the lighthouse as it’s too far to swim. And I never did "
"learn to walk on water."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_2"
msgstr "Lasse?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_3"
msgstr "The lighthouse keeper. Odd fellow. Is there any more?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"So, just imagine me standing on the beach, sticking my thumb up in the wind. "
"Could someone just drop anchor, bring me on board, and give me a ride to the "
"mainland?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_5"
msgstr ""
"The lighthouse doesn’t have a fresh water supply. And for three days "
"already? We should help him."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_6"
msgstr "Doesn’t actually sound so urgent."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_OUTRO_1"
msgstr "Thanks for the lift! How's it going with your oil?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_OUTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"So-so. We’re too slow. What are you going to do now? You need a new boat, "
"huh?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_OUTRO_3"
msgstr ""
"Nothing a few fresh planks and a bit of tar won’t fix. Do you know Trygve "
"Thomassen in Mørkved?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_OUTRO_4"
msgstr "The shipwright?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_LIGHTHOUSE_OUTRO_5"
msgstr ""
"Nephew of mine. He could probably squeeze another knot or two out of your "
"ships. Just tell him I sent you."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_1"
msgstr "I’ve got to give it to you, you’re tough, Nils Eriksen."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_2"
msgstr "We’re not done yet, Larsson."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_3"
msgstr ""
"Maybe not you. But the seagulls are saying that your drill heads are. They "
"really are cheap."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_4"
msgstr ""
"Our budget is biting us hard from every angle. But what choice do we have?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_5"
msgstr "There’s a letter here from a certain Olav Olafsen from Løding."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_6"
msgstr ""
"He runs a metallurgy company and has just developed a new steel alloy that "
"could significantly improve our drill heads and other machine components."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_7"
msgstr "An old classmate. Write back, tell him we have no money."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_MACHINES_8"
msgstr ""
"That’s the thing. He says he only needs the materials. Besides, if this goes "
"well, he’ll be able to patent the alloy and market it worldwide. Here’s the "
"list of the supplies he’d need from us."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_1"
msgstr ""
"You win this round, Nils. Just, and with the help of your… relatives. We’ll "
"meet again—sometime, some place. And there’ll be no district administration "
"to help you."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_10"
msgstr ""
"Well, at least I know now what Astrid meant by “little revenge.” Too bad, "
"though, that it’s not that little. Take care, Andrea. I’m sure we’ll be in "
"touch!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_11"
msgstr "Don’t be angry with me, Boss. I’ll send you postcards!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_2"
msgstr ""
"Whatever, Larsson. I’ll always have the satisfaction of knowing I kept you "
"out of Norway."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_3"
msgstr ""
"Nils, the oil business isn’t only decided out on the oil fields. You have "
"played your role. Now it’s someone else’s turn: the politicians."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_4"
msgstr "We’ve taken the first step. We’re no longer just a nation of fishers."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_5"
msgstr ""
"Yes, but we won’t know if your country will be able to manage the next step "
"for some years yet. And my little revenge is coming your way soon. Take care!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_6"
msgstr "Yes, if our greed doesn’t… Andrea? You want to talk to me?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_7"
msgstr "I… I wanted to thank you. For the opportunity!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_8"
msgstr ""
"You have to seize opportunities, Andrea. And you did just that. I owe you my "
"thanks. Without you…"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_1_STAR_9"
msgstr ""
"Yes, you have to. And that’s why—I’m sorry for this—I’m quitting. Astrid "
"offered me a position as a logistics specialist. I'm going to Asia."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_1"
msgstr ""
"You win this round, Nils. We’ll meet again—sometime, some place. And next "
"time I won’t make the mistake of underestimating you. Congratulations, for "
"now."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_10"
msgstr ""
"…Of course you have to take this opportunity. Well, at least I know now what "
"Astrid meant by “little revenge.” Tell Astrid she better look after you, "
"otherwise…"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_11"
msgstr ""
"Thanks, Boss. I’ll think up an “otherwise”, and I’ll send you postcards too!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_2"
msgstr "Thanks, Larsson. It has been my pleasure keeping you out of Norway."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_3"
msgstr ""
"You’ve kept me out, perhaps. But the oil business isn’t only decided out on "
"the oil fields, Nils. Still, you have played your part."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_4"
msgstr "We’ve taken the first step. We’re no longer just a nation of fishers."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_5"
msgstr ""
"You did well. Let’s see if your politicians can handle all that money. I "
"almost feel bad about my little revenge. But I just couldn’t say no. "
"Farewell!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_6"
msgstr ""
"What little revenge? And the politicians… Oh, Andrea! Glad you stopped by!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_7"
msgstr "Hello, Nils… I… I wanted to thank you. For the opportunity!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_8"
msgstr ""
"You have to seize opportunities, Andrea. And you did just that. I owe you my "
"thanks. Without you… I would have lost."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_2_STARS_9"
msgstr ""
"While we’re talking about opportunities… I’m quitting. Astrid offered me a "
"position as a logistics specialist. And it’s in Asia. Please forgive me, but…"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_1"
msgstr ""
"Congratulations, Nils, you won. Too bad you didn’t join my team. But strong "
"competition keeps things interesting, I guess."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_10"
msgstr ""
"While we’re talking about opportunities… I’m quitting. Astrid offered me a "
"position as a logistics specialist. And it’s in Asia. Please forgive me, but…"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_11"
msgstr ""
"Well, at least I know now what Astrid meant by “little revenge.” And of "
"course you have to take this opportunity. Congratulations! Tell Astrid she "
"better look after you, otherwise…"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_12"
msgstr ""
"Thanks, Boss. I’ll think up an “otherwise”, and I’ll send you postcards too!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_2"
msgstr "Thanks, Larsson. It has been my pleasure keeping you out of Norway."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_3"
msgstr ""
"You’ve kept me out, perhaps. But the oil business isn’t only decided out on "
"the oil fields, Nils. That’s what politics are for."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_4"
msgstr "We’ve taken the first step. We’re no longer just a nation of fishers."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_5"
msgstr ""
"The first step, yes. You should be proud of that. I just hope your "
"politicians are even half as smart with your country’s new wealth. And by "
"the way, I’ve seized the opportunity for a little revenge. Sorry, that’s "
"just how the game works!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_6"
msgstr "Revenge? What kind of revenge?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_7"
msgstr "Take care!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_8"
msgstr "Hello, Nils… I… I wanted to thank you. For the opportunity!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_3_STARS_9"
msgstr ""
"Which you took. And for that I have to thank you. I would have lost without "
"you."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_FAILURE_1"
msgstr ""
"Oh, Nils. What did I tell you? You could have made a career here with me. "
"And now? You can’t even get a job on your dad’s cutter, not now that the oil "
"rigs have scared all the schools of herring away."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_FAILURE_2"
msgstr "We’ll meet again, Larsson."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_FAILURE_3"
msgstr ""
"Oh, not anytime soon, I fear, Nils! You were fun, really you were! So, "
"here’s a sincere piece of advice: Find yourself another line of work. "
"Somewhere far away! You’re not gonna make it in the oil business!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_OIL_1"
msgstr ""
"Well, this is a nice surprise. Do you have a connection at the district "
"administration? A relative? An in-law? Like just about everyone else around "
"here?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_OIL_2"
msgstr "You’ve not won yet, Larsson. And truth is, you’re scared of losing."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_OIL_3"
msgstr ""
"Our applications were submitted at the same time, Larsson. Now the license "
"will be granted to the first to deliver 1,000 barrels of oil to the inland "
"refinery."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_OIL_4"
msgstr ""
"I love this, Nils! My trucks are already on their way to the refinery. And "
"you don’t even have tankers. I’m going to win this fair and square!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_1"
msgstr ""
"All right. We’ve applied for the license. Now we have to prove that we can "
"actually extract the oil quickly. Astrid’s first platform’s already in place."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_2"
msgstr "I’m listening!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_3"
msgstr ""
"First, we’ll need steel from the steel mill fast. That’s why it’s important "
"we find the most efficient route across the difficult terrain. Can you do "
"that?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_4"
msgstr "Noted!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_5"
msgstr ""
"The dockworkers are already waiting for the steel to arrive in Løding. After "
"that, we’ll move the oil platforms to the oil reservoirs. Got that?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_TRANSPORT_STEEL_6"
msgstr "You got it, Boss!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_1"
msgstr ""
"I’d love to say I’d underestimated you, Nils. But the fact is, you "
"overestimated yourself. How many barrels have you delivered so far, hm?"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_2"
msgstr ""
"She’s right, Andrea. Larsson’s always ahead of us. We’ve got no chance!"

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_3"
msgstr "I don’t agree, Boss. I spoke to Kari Gundersen yesterday."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_4"
msgstr ""
"He’s the barman in Mørkved! You’re only 15—you shouldn’t be hanging around "
"bars."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_5"
msgstr ""
"He’s my uncle. And he says if you need workers, all you have to do is ask. "
"Everyone in Mørkved wants you to get the contract."

msgid "MISSION_05_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_6"
msgstr ""
"Finally, some good news! So, all we have to do now is get the workers to the "
"oil platforms!"

msgid "MISSION_05_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Following the discovery of the Ekofisk oil field, more and more fjords are "
"being opened up for drilling. Local entrepreneur Nils Eriksen wants to seize "
"this opportunity to bring prosperity to the region. However, to obtain an "
"official license to extract oil, he must compete against a foreign "
"corporation."

msgid "MISSION_05_DRILLING_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Unfortunately, the drill core analysis shows no signs of oil. We need to be "
"patient and search elsewhere."

msgid "MISSION_05_DRILLING_GOOD"
msgstr ""
"Bullseye! The detectors are going crazy! There must be a gigantic reservoir "
"here!"

msgid "MISSION_05_DRILLING_MEDIUM"
msgstr ""
"Now, this looks really good: a porous layer with oil saturation! Keep it up!"

msgid "MISSION_05_DRILLING_POOR"
msgstr ""
"According to the sludge report, there are traces of oil here. That’s "
"something at least! But will it be enough to take on Astrid?"

msgid "MISSION_05_FIRST_DRILLING"
msgstr "The first test drill has started."

msgid "MISSION_05_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"My father says I’m crazy. I was the first from our village to go to "
"university—Cambridge even. So, why would I return home just to take on an "
"international oil giant? One that had previously made me a great job offer.\n"
"But we have to protect the fjords. And Norway. This oil belongs to us all, "
"and not just a few oil barons."

msgid "MISSION_05_LOCATION"
msgstr "Ekofisk Oil Fields, Norway"

msgid "MISSION_05_MEDAL"
msgstr "Rescue Lasse!"

msgid "MISSION_05_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Rescue Lasse!"

msgid "MISSION_05_NAME"
msgstr "Oil for the People"

msgid "MISSION_05_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Extract your first 1,000 units of oil before the competitor to secure the "
"exclusive drilling rights."

msgid "MISSION_05_STAR_1"
msgstr "Deliver the oil faster than Astrid."

msgid "MISSION_05_STAR_2"
msgstr "End the game before Astrid delivers 750 units of oil."

msgid "MISSION_05_STAR_3"
msgstr "End the game before Astrid delivers 500 units of oil."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_1_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Select a question mark to send the boat there. This will start a test drill."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_1_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"All right; that’s enough practice. We marked a few locations with yellow "
"buoys yesterday. Once you drop anchor at the buoys, test drilling will start."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_1_NAME"
msgstr "Search for Oil"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_1_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Send the [link=entity_drilling_boat]boat[/link] to one of the buoys."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_HINT"
msgstr ""
"The more locations you check, the more oil extraction potential you have "
"later. But you will need to build more oil platforms, too."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We can’t get caught again. Sure, more oil would be better, but we could just "
"head straight to the district administration, couldn’t we?"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_NAME"
msgstr "Continue or Quit"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_CAUGHT_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Drill in other locations, or select the "
"[link=entity_administration_building]district administration[/link] to "
"request a license."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_ENOUGH_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Okay, that’ll have to do. We can’t afford to lose any more time. To the "
"district administration!"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_ENOUGH_NAME"
msgstr "Acquire Drilling License"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_ENOUGH_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Select the [link=entity_administration_building]district administration[/"
"link] to request a license."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_HINT"
msgstr ""
"The more locations you check, the more oil extraction potential you have "
"later. But you will need to build more oil platforms, too."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"So, if we want to search in Astrid’s territory too… the red buoys are hers. "
"Or should we call off the search here? If we’ve already found enough, we can "
"go ahead and apply for the extraction license."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_NAME"
msgstr "Continue or Quit"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_DRILLING_2_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Drill in other locations, or select the "
"[link=entity_administration_building]district administration[/link] to "
"request a license."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Like I said: odd fellow. So, how are we for time? Should we help him?"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let’s hear it"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Our drilling ship picked up a radio transmission. It sounds like a distress "
"call."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Message"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_INTRO_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you want to listen to the radio transmission?"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Lasse"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_LIGHTHOUSE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport the lighthouse keeper from the [link=entity_lighthouse]lighthouse[/"
"link] to the [link=entity_harbor]port[/link] in Mørkved."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_MACHINES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Let’s get the machines to the oil platforms so we can stay in this race."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_MACHINES_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Machines"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_MACHINES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_machines]machines[/link] to the [link=oil_area]oil "
"platforms[/link] to boost them."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_OIL_HINT"
msgstr "Send enough vehicles to complete the delivery in time."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_OIL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need a complete supply chain as soon as possible, even if it only has a "
"limited capacity at first. We need revenue!"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_OIL_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Oil"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_OIL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver 1,000 units of crude oil to the [link=entity_refinery]refinery[/"
"link] in the north."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_STEEL_COMPLETE_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Cast Off!"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_STEEL_COMPLETE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "The oil platforms are up, Boss! We’re still in the race!"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_STEEL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "We need steel at the dry dock in Løding. Organize the transport!"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_STEEL_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Steel"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TRANSPORT_STEEL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver [link=entity_steel]steel[/link] to the [link=entity_docks]docks[/"
"link] to build the oil platforms."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TUTORIAL_SHIP_HINT"
msgstr "Select a place in the water to send the boat there."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TUTORIAL_SHIP_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"That’s the ship. It’s pretty simple really: You chose a location on the "
"water, and it’ll travel there. Give it a try."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TUTORIAL_SHIP_NAME"
msgstr "Navigate the Ship"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_TUTORIAL_SHIP_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Send the [link=entity_drilling_boat]boat[/link] to the "
"[link=green_area_pos]highlighted area[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_WORKERS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The workers can’t walk to the oil platforms, of course. We should provide "
"them with the proper infrastructure."

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_WORKERS_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Workers"

msgid "MISSION_05_TASK_WORKERS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a passenger line from one of the residential districts to the "
"[link=oil_area]oil platforms[/link] so the workers can get to work."

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "President"

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Mateo Cruz"

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "First Lady"

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Salita Ananda Cruz"

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Billionaire"

msgid "MISSION_06_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Richard Cleese"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_BONUS_RAILROAD_1"
msgstr "Just a stupid childhood dream, but…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_BONUS_RAILROAD_2"
msgstr "Share it with me, my dear."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_BONUS_RAILROAD_3"
msgstr ""
"As a child, I always dreamed of traveling by train from the northern tip of "
"the country, across the eastern islands, all the way down to Davao in the "
"south—and even beyond. Without ever having to change trains!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_BONUS_RAILROAD_4"
msgstr "That would be incredible. Like the Trans-Siberian Railroad."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_BONUS_RAILROAD_5"
msgstr "The Trans-Philippine…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_FAIL_1"
msgstr ""
"So, Salita, with the next election campaign coming up, how are the polls "
"looking?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_FAIL_2"
msgstr ""
"The oil disaster has badly hurt our popularity. We shouldn’t show our faces "
"around the Bohol Sea during the election campaign…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_FAIL_3"
msgstr "Dammit, yes. We should have prevented that. That damned Cleese guy!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_SUCCESS_1"
msgstr ""
"So, with the next election campaign coming up, how are the polls looking?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_SUCCESS_2"
msgstr ""
"It was a smart move to inform the press that we prevented an oil disaster. "
"That surely earned us a few Brownie points."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_COMPLETE_SUBSIDIES_OIL_SUCCESS_3"
msgstr "Yes, if that had gone wrong…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_1"
msgstr "Hello, allow me to introduce myself…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_10"
msgstr ""
"Yes, I’m afraid so! The island is a candidate for World Heritage status and "
"has fragile flora and fauna. Our hands are tied, I’m afraid!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_11"
msgstr ""
"Well, I think you can hardly afford to turn this offer down. I’ll be here "
"for another ten days. Then I’ll be expecting the contract!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_12"
msgstr ""
"May I ask what that was all about, my dear wife? We could use the money, and "
"we have beaches in abundance!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_13"
msgstr ""
"That, my dear, was me saving you from a scandal that would have cost you "
"your office. Your opponents are just waiting for the first sign of "
"corruption!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_2"
msgstr "You’ve already told my wife your name."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_3"
msgstr ""
"Oh, that was your wife? I thought she was the receptionist. Nice to meet you!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_4"
msgstr "We’ll see about that. What is this about, Mr. Cleese?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_5"
msgstr ""
"Well, I’m a billionaire, and I’d be willing to help the Republic of the "
"Philippines out of certain financial difficulties. At a reasonable interest "
"rate, of course."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_6"
msgstr ""
"That sounds tempting, indeed. But what motivates your involvement in "
"bankrupt Third World countries?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_7"
msgstr ""
"My big heart. I could also, for instance, boost tourism by building a luxury "
"resort on a small island named Camiguin."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_8"
msgstr "Oh, that’s such a shame!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_CREDIT_9"
msgstr "Is it?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_1"
msgstr "The economy could be doing better, but it could also be a lot worse."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_2"
msgstr "So, this is no time to relax. What can we do better?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_3"
msgstr ""
"We’re still breaking too many promises, and that’s costing us money and "
"votes. What can we do about it, Andrea?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_4"
msgstr ""
"Every little improvement, every demand we meet in a factory earns us money—"
"money we can use to expand infrastructure faster and speed up operations."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_5"
msgstr "Sounds like a plan!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_6"
msgstr ""
"We mustn’t disappoint people. Not even once if we can help it. "
"Disappointments outweigh achievements ten to one in the people’s eyes!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_7"
msgstr "If only it were that easy…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_OK_8"
msgstr "but we have to try!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_1"
msgstr "I’d say we’re off to a good start!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_2"
msgstr "Good. No time to relax. There’s still plenty we can improve!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_3"
msgstr ""
"Just like during the election campaign. That attitude! That’s why the people "
"love you and follow you! What’s next, Andrea?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_4"
msgstr ""
"Every little improvement, every demand we meet in a factory earns us money—"
"money we can use to expand infrastructure faster and speed up operations. "
"And that boosts our general prosperity as well!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_5"
msgstr "All right. Just keep on going. Never let up."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_6"
msgstr ""
"We haven’t disappointed the people yet, and we should try to never "
"disappoint them. Not even once. Disappointments outweigh achievements ten to "
"one in the people’s eyes!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_7"
msgstr ""
"I couldn't agree more. That sentence should be framed and hung above "
"everyone's desk."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_STRONG_8"
msgstr "Sounds like a plan!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_1"
msgstr ""
"Let’s be honest with ourselves: That was a poor start to the presidency!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_2"
msgstr ""
"But what could we do differently? It’s so much work. And we have so little "
"money."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_3"
msgstr "Andrea, do you have an explanation?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_4"
msgstr ""
"We are too slow. It just takes too long to plan and complete the "
"infrastructure."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_5"
msgstr ""
"Every factory has its demands. If they are fulfilled, the economy will grow "
"too, along with the available budget."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_6"
msgstr "Sounds reasonable."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_7"
msgstr ""
"And we need to stop disappointing people. We made promises. It’s time to "
"keep them!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_ECON_FINAL_WEAK_8"
msgstr "Let’s get to work then!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr "Salita, my love, I fear we’ve gotten ourselves into a bit of a mess."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_10"
msgstr ""
"We have a little time for most of these contracts. We could try to factor in "
"the rail lines and interim storage as we fulfill them."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"No reason to despair, my dear Mateo. We wanted to help the people, so we’ll "
"help the people!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr "But there’s hardly any money!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"Industry is calling for better infrastructure. Many businesses are regularly "
"grinding to a halt because they can’t get the goods they need. Many of the "
"cities are decaying because the people can’t buy anything. And there are no "
"tax revenues as a result."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr ""
"But we can’t just go plastering the entire country with roads. And we don’t "
"even have a rail network. The railroads have proven indispensable for "
"freight transport in other countries."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr ""
"That sounds logical. That’ll give us more flexibility if something is "
"urgently needed somewhere."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr "This country is huge! Everything is so far apart!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr ""
"Let’s embrace that as an opportunity! We have lots of space to build things "
"for the future!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_INTRO_9"
msgstr ""
"Fortunately, we have cooperation contracts with a hungry industry—many of "
"which are also looking to finally escape the eternal quagmire of corruption."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_1"
msgstr "Shall we review your political situation?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_10"
msgstr "I was looking forward to a vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_11"
msgstr "After the election, my love. After the election."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_2"
msgstr "We haven’t accomplished as much as the public expected from us, huh?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_3"
msgstr ""
"Honestly? No, not by a long shot. Sadly, we completely overestimated "
"ourselves. And the polls show it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_4"
msgstr "So bad?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_5"
msgstr ""
"From “dawdlers” and corruption allegations, all the way to “hanging”—it’s "
"all in there."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_6"
msgstr "Hanging? Wow! So, we don’t stand a chance?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_7"
msgstr ""
"Your charm will give us a second chance, I’m sure of that. You’ll win over "
"the voters again. And now we know what we’re doing. Perhaps that should even "
"be our campaign slogan!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_8"
msgstr "And after all, the people aren’t any worse off than they were before."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_FAILED_9"
msgstr "Not much anyway. We should give it another try!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_1"
msgstr "And then there's your re-election campaign."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_2"
msgstr ""
"Well, I think we did a great job with the subsidies. That should be "
"reflected in the polls, right?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_3"
msgstr ""
"Yes, it is! Your chances of being reelected are very high—an approval rating "
"of 71%."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_4"
msgstr ""
"So, let’s relax, take the election campaign nice and easy, travel our "
"country. Think of it as a vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_5"
msgstr "That’d be fantastic, my darling."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_12_6"
msgstr "We’ve earned it, Salita!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_1"
msgstr "Shall we review your political situation?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_10"
msgstr ""
"It sounds like campaigning is going to be a tough job. I was looking forward "
"to a vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_11"
msgstr "After the election, my love. After the election."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_2"
msgstr ""
"I know, we really fell short on the subsidies. Is that reflected in the "
"polls?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_3"
msgstr "Let’s just say the voters don’t have anything against you personally."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_4"
msgstr "Well, that’s something at least!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_5"
msgstr "They just think you’re a bad politician!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_6"
msgstr "So, we don’t stand a chance?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_7"
msgstr ""
"Your charm will give us a second chance, I’m sure of that. You’ll win over "
"the voters again. And now we know what we’re doing. Perhaps that should even "
"be our campaign slogan!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_8"
msgstr ""
"And after all, the people are a little better off than they were before."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_5_9"
msgstr "Yes, but just a little."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_1"
msgstr "We need to talk about your reelection chances!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_2"
msgstr ""
"I don’t think we did all that badly with the subsidies. Is that reflected in "
"the polls at least?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_3"
msgstr ""
"Not as clearly as we would have liked. You’re going to have a fight on your "
"hands."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_4"
msgstr "I’m tired, Salita, my dear."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_5"
msgstr ""
"I understand, my brave warrior. But just think of everything we could "
"achieve in your second term, now we have a much better understanding of the "
"mechanisms of power!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_6"
msgstr "I was looking forward to a vacation with you."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_8_7"
msgstr "After the election, my love. After the election."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_1"
msgstr "The election campaign’s getting closer, Mateo."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_2"
msgstr ""
"Election campaign? Why bother? We did a perfect job with the subsidies, "
"right?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_3"
msgstr ""
"And that’s why the people love you. Approval rating over 80%. You don’t even "
"have an opponent right now."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_4"
msgstr "Then I guess it’s about time, don’t you?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_5"
msgstr "I think so. There’s nothing more we can improve. Do you really…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_6"
msgstr ""
"Our work is done, my letter of resignation signed. We’re handing over the "
"country in perfect condition. This is exactly how people should remember us!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_7"
msgstr ""
"Here’s to the golden era under President Cruz! Here’s to the Republic of the "
"Philippines!!!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_8"
msgstr "And here’s to our vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_MISSION_END_SUCCESS_ALL_9"
msgstr "To that especially!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_RAILROAD_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"By the way, I also have some wonderful news about your railroad, my dear "
"husband!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_RAILROAD_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr ""
"It’s finished and it’s a huge hit with the people—and trade and industry are "
"delighted with it too."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_RAILROAD_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr ""
"Seems I had the right vision! And you the power of persuasion! What would I "
"do without you?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_RAILROAD_COMPLETE_4"
msgstr ""
"People are already calling it the Mateolino. It was your childhood dream, "
"after all. It’ll keep you in the memories of the Philippine people forever!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_1"
msgstr "You know where I’m from."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_2"
msgstr ""
"Tagkawayan, the most beautiful place in the world, because it gave us you, "
"Salita, my love!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_3"
msgstr ""
"Well, it’s not so beautiful anymore! The last tropical storm destroyed the "
"school there. We need to rebuild it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_4"
msgstr ""
"Children are the future. The better we educate them, the better off we’ll be "
"down the road. I’m sure Andrea will be able to assist you."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_5"
msgstr "Thank you."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_6"
msgstr "Yes, sure. Come on, let’s do this. For the children."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr "Salita, we’re done. The school’s standing again."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr ""
"Please forgive me for putting my hometown first. It’s a matter that’s very "
"close to my heart."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr "Our involvement with the school has drawn a bit of attention."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_COMPLETE_4"
msgstr "And?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SCHOOL_COMPLETE_5"
msgstr "A number of other issues have been brought to my attention."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_CHAT_1"
msgstr ""
"Is there anything in it for us? Social welfare programs don’t exactly fill "
"the state’s coffers."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_CHAT_2"
msgstr ""
"The NGOs gave us a lot of support during the election. We ought to show them "
"our gratitude, if only to make sure, they’re not our enemies in the next "
"election."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_1"
msgstr ""
"Things are slightly better for the people, but we could have done more for "
"them."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_10"
msgstr "I think that, Mateo, is what makes a really good head of state."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_2"
msgstr ""
"Not good. We’re not here to have fun. How do we achieve the best for the "
"people?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_3"
msgstr ""
"By talking less and actually fulfilling the contracts we sign. However, I do "
"wonder where exactly we went wrong. Andrea?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_4"
msgstr ""
"Often, it’s the little things: You start strong and then think everything "
"will just fall into place. But there’s always a lot to do and to keep track "
"of to ensure the logistics run smoothly!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_5"
msgstr "So, our people need to be watched more closely? To be more precise?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_6"
msgstr ""
"Attention to detail but never losing sight of the bigger picture. Everything "
"we need should be available centrally and nearby so we can respond quickly. "
"That requires lots of small improvements, all in service of a greater vision."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_7"
msgstr ""
"Governing is easy. Governing well, however, clearly requires a lot of work."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_8"
msgstr ""
"And persistence. Always double-check everything. The moment you fall asleep, "
"things start to go wrong."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_OK_9"
msgstr "I’m not sure right now whether I even want to be reelected…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_1"
msgstr ""
"The people love us: schools, medical supplies, food. Things are improving "
"for everyone!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_2"
msgstr "I think I’m going to take a long vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_3"
msgstr ""
"Out of the question! If we let things slide now, it’ll all have been just a "
"flash in the pan. Andrea, what’s up next?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_4"
msgstr ""
"There are still things we can optimize. Distribution centers could be better "
"located or rebuilt, roads improved, vehicles upgraded. More bus stops, more "
"lines. The people can never have it too good!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_5"
msgstr "All right, no vacation!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_6"
msgstr ""
"That’s more like it. I promise you, at the end of your time in office, I’ll "
"treat you to a four-week luxury vacation."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_7"
msgstr "Hawaii? I’ve always wanted to go there!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_8"
msgstr ""
"In the Philippines. It’s supposed to be wonderful there. And considerably "
"more affordable!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_STRONG_9"
msgstr "I love my patriotic duty!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_1"
msgstr ""
"Well, we’re not going to be winning the Mother Teresa Award for social "
"affairs any time soon."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_2"
msgstr ""
"Where did we go wrong? The tasks didn’t sound impossible! And yet, we still "
"failed."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_3"
msgstr "None of the tasks were impossible. And this is all very frustrating."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_4"
msgstr ""
"If we still want to be able to look at ourselves in the mirror, we need to "
"do better."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_5"
msgstr ""
"Even if we’re out of the running for awards, we have to think about the "
"people and look after their needs."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_6"
msgstr "Let’s get to work then! We might only have until election day!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_SOCIAL_FINAL_WEAK_7"
msgstr ""
"And if we continue to do nothing, we’ll have a lot of free time after that."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_OK_1"
msgstr "I think we can call that a minor success."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_OK_2"
msgstr "A minor success is just the little sister of failure, right?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_STRONG_1"
msgstr ""
"People are flocking to our beaches, marveling at our landscapes, strolling "
"through Manila!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_STRONG_2"
msgstr ""
"And the government coffers are overflowing. I’d say we’ve done a very decent "
"job."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_WEAK_1"
msgstr "People would rather spend their vacation in Wyoming than here."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_TOURIST_FINAL_WEAK_2"
msgstr "Where? Oh, it doesn’t matter! Guess we’ve only got ourselves to blame."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_1"
msgstr "You don’t give up, do you? The answer is “no”!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_2"
msgstr ""
"Well, it’s not about that. We have a little problem. Our yacht has run "
"aground off Camiguin and is in danger of capsizing."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_3"
msgstr "And how is that our problem?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_4"
msgstr ""
"Well, we’re stranded on a coral reef, and we have a few thousand liters of "
"diesel in the tank…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_5"
msgstr ""
"Oh, fantastic. If you were wondering why American billionaires enjoy such an "
"outstanding reputation…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr "May I invite you aboard my yacht to thank you for your help?"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr "No, thanks. I heard the captain wasn’t really up to the job!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr ""
"You will pay. And it’s going to be a lot just so we don’t air this on our TV "
"channels."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_4"
msgstr "You heard what my husband said."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_5"
msgstr "And I came here to give your poorhouse a little helping hand…"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_6"
msgstr ""
"I’d suggest we build on this success and push our tourism promotion even "
"further. We’ve got two more subsidy requests!"

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_COMPLETE_7"
msgstr "Well, we’d be happy to hear them."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_FAILED_1"
msgstr "Damned Americans. It’ll take us decades to get rid of that."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_FAILED_2"
msgstr ""
"I’d suggest that we still stick with our tourism promotion efforts and boost "
"tourism in other parts of the country to offset the lost revenue."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_FAILED_3"
msgstr "Yes, that sounds like a reasonable, pragmatic suggestion."

msgid "MISSION_06_CUTSCENE_YACHT_FAILED_4"
msgstr ""
"We already have a few extra collaboration proposals anyway. We should follow "
"up on those!"

msgid "MISSION_06_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The Democratic Socialist candidate Mateo Cruz takes victory in the election "
"in Manila—which he hadn’t expected, and now he feels a little unprepared. "
"Now the hopes of his beloved country are resting on his shoulders. But he "
"knows one thing for certain: He can always count on the expertise of his "
"wife Salita! If only the government coffers weren’t so empty."

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_1_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"If I can read maps—and I can—we’d only have needed a boat or a bridge to "
"deliver rubber to the tire factory. Right now, we’re still at the mercy of "
"the American tire giants. Put in a little more effort, please!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_1_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Wonderful. Producing our own tires reduces the foreign trade deficit and "
"stabilizes the peso. We need to keep this up."

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_2_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Seriously? We can’t even manage to get coconuts across a short stretch of "
"land to Davao anymore? I think we’re going to have to try a lot harder!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_2_WIN"
msgstr ""
"The citizens in Davao are very grateful that they can now buy coconuts. It’s "
"the small things that encourage people to take bigger chances!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_3_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Having our own furniture industry would have been a real blessing. Imports "
"are expensive and not much help! We need to be better and braver!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_3_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Affordable furniture produced domestically! Finally, we no longer have to "
"order these things from Sweden!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_4_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"We’re extracting oil but unable to transform it into higher-value goods? Why "
"is that? There’s clearly a lack of will! We could have created some real "
"value there!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_4_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Manila finally has sufficient oil to maintain a steady energy supply. "
"That’ll keep businesses running and people in jobs!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_5_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"We have the workers and we have the factory. Yet we don’t have the buses to "
"get one to the other? Machines are a profitable business! Just ask the "
"Germans!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_5_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Domestically built machines ensure that the wheels in the country will never "
"grind to a halt again. Or perhaps I should say they’ll now start moving in "
"the first place!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_1_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"There are teachers living in Tagkawayan who can’t make it to work. And all "
"because we couldn’t get a school bus organized? Embarrassing."

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_1_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Very good: More teachers mean more and better education. That is the path to "
"a modern Republic of the Philippines!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_2_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Are we really unable to get medical aid to remote villages? Are we really "
"that overwhelmed? What are the people in Pinamalayan supposed to do? All "
"move to Manila?"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_2_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Pinamalayan finally has access to modern medicine! Very good. A healthy "
"population is a satisfied population that trusts and votes for us!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_3_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"So, we can’t supply Cebu with medication? Why not? How are people supposed "
"to go on trusting us if we just leave them hanging like that?!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_3_WIN"
msgstr ""
"And now Cebu can enjoy the benefits of modern medicine. We need to earn the "
"trust of everyday people if we don’t want to be swept aside by their "
"discontent."

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_4_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"The goal was simply to allow people to travel from Butuan to Davao. And we "
"can’t even get that right? Is this country going to remain fragmented "
"forever?"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_4_WIN"
msgstr ""
"More and more people living in rural areas are now connected to the city, "
"and work and shop there. This kind of connection makes life easier and "
"prevents an exodus from the countryside. It reduces social divides and keeps "
"families stable!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_5_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"We’re talking basics here! Food! If we can’t get supplies to every part of "
"this country, then we don’t deserve to govern! Pagadian City is built on a "
"huge, fertile island! How did this go wrong?"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_5_WIN"
msgstr ""
"The people in Pagadian City now have access to a balanced diet. This will "
"allow the city to continue to grow, easing the pressure on Davao. Health and "
"satisfaction go hand in hand! This is the way forward. Step by step!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_SUBSIDIES_EXPLAIN"
msgstr ""
"Only accept a contract if you are certain, you can fulfill it within the "
"time remaining. Otherwise, there’ll be hefty penalties that we just can’t "
"afford. So, perhaps you should prepare for a contract before you accept it."

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_1_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"How are we going to lure tourists to the Philippines when we have the most "
"beautiful beaches, but our guests go hungry? Someone explain that to me!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_1_WIN"
msgstr ""
"I want to see the ads on all my trips abroad: The Philippines. The most "
"beautiful beaches in the world! And resorts with the best cuisine!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_2_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"The most beautiful national parks in the world. We even have Mayon, an "
"active volcano! And we can’t get a single train or bus line from Manila to "
"the national park entrance? Unbelievable!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_2_WIN"
msgstr ""
"It’s inexplicable to me why anyone would want to climb an active volcano, "
"but apparently, it’s an attractive offer—and lucrative for us. We should "
"probably just keep the number of annual casualties under wraps, huh?"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_3_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Yes, I know. Coral reefs are valuable in and of themselves! But that "
"shouldn’t stop us from bringing tourists to the diving school so they can "
"learn just how precious they are!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_3_WIN"
msgstr ""
"The full splendor of the coral reefs on display for the world to see! And "
"the diving schools are also doing their bit to preserve them! It’s their "
"livelihood, after all! Win-win, I’d say!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_4_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"It’s a serious blow not to have fully connected the western cities and "
"islands up to Cebu to the capital. They are economically underdeveloped and "
"need tourism more than the east!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_4_WIN"
msgstr ""
"Having the western islands and cities now fully connected to Manila is a "
"huge success. We should build on this to grow tourism and industry!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_5_FAIL"
msgstr ""
"Fully connecting the western islands to Davao would have been a huge boost "
"for tourism! But we screwed it up. The consequences of this remain to be "
"seen!"

msgid "MISSION_06_GUIDE_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_5_WIN"
msgstr ""
"The western islands and their cities are now much closer to the southern "
"part of the country. Tourism will boom, and the nation will develop! We’ve "
"achieved something great."

msgid "MISSION_06_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"I could do with all the help I can get. You have no idea how fast an "
"election victory like this hits you. One moment, you’re the hero of the "
"streets, the fist of the people—and the next, you’re the president of a "
"country where nothing works.\n"
"And all that because I made a few promises: justice, schools, hospitals, a "
"thriving economy. But it doesn’t matter: I just have to make everything "
"better. How hard can that really be? Thankfully, I have Salita by my side. "
"She’s the brains in our family."

msgid "MISSION_06_LOCATION"
msgstr "Manila, Philippines"

msgid "MISSION_06_MEDAL"
msgstr "Construct the Trans-Philippine Railroad."

msgid "MISSION_06_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Construct the Trans-Philippine Railroad."

msgid "MISSION_06_NAME"
msgstr "Island Expansion"

msgid "MISSION_06_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Help President Cruz and the First Lady boost the Philippine economy, social "
"services, and tourism."

msgid "MISSION_06_STAR_1"
msgstr "Successfully complete 5 subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_STAR_2"
msgstr "Successfully complete 8 subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_STAR_3"
msgstr "Successfully complete 12 subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_CREDIT_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "No, I don’t know him. Let him in anyway."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_CREDIT_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Do you have an appointment with a Richard Cleese? He’s claiming you do."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_CREDIT_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Billionaire"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_ECON_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let’s hear it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_ECON_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We have the first interim report on our economic policy. Do you have a "
"moment to take a look?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_ECON_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Report"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_SOCIAL_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let’s hear it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_SOCIAL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We have the first interim report on our social policy. Would you like to "
"hear it?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_SOCIAL_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Report"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_TOURIST_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Let’s hear it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_TOURIST_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We have the first interim report on our tourism policy. Want to hear it?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_FINAL_TOURIST_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to the Report"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_RAILROAD_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Just a stupid thought, Salita."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_RAILROAD_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "You look distracted, Mateo. Something’s on your mind."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_RAILROAD_NAME"
msgstr "Respond to Salita"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_RAILROAD_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "How should Mateo answer?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_YACHT_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "You already have done."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_YACHT_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr "Uhhhh, hello, Mr. President. Mind if I disturb you for a moment?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_YACHT_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Mr. Cleese"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BEFORE_YACHT_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "It seems as if he has something important to say"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BUILD_SCHOOL_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"You heard Salita: The school needs to be rebuilt. Bring enough wood to the "
"construction site."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BUILD_SCHOOL_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Logs"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_BUILD_SCHOOL_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver wood to the [link=entity_school]school construction site[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_COMPLETE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "I always have time for you!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_COMPLETE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We’re making progress. That’s good. But I have a request, Mateo. Do you have "
"a moment?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_COMPLETE_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_NAME"
msgstr "Listen to Salita"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_HINT"
msgstr ""
"There is no need to fulfill all contracts to complete the mission, but more "
"contracts earn more stars. Failing an accepted contract carries a financial "
"risk."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"That’d probably be a good idea. We mustn’t disappoint our industry! And that "
"means we shouldn’t keep them waiting too long either. Let’s build "
"infrastructure! Let’s build big solutions!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_NAME"
msgstr "Fulfill Subsidy Contracts"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_ECONOMY_SUBSIDIES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Fulfill or reject the offered subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_CONFIRM_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "It’s pure madness. Let’s do it!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_CONFIRM_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "Best to keep our feet on the ground!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_CONFIRM_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We could do it bit by bit. We have a whole term to work with! Shall we?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_CONFIRM_NAME"
msgstr "Decide your Action"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_CONFIRM_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you want to be immortalized in the history of Philippine railroads?"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Start building the line between two stops and extend it later to have some "
"income over time."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"With you by my side, Salita, and help from Andrea, I’d dare to do anything! "
"Let’s go for it! Let’s build the Trans-Philippine Railroad!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Rail Connection"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_RAILROAD_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a continuous railroad line from [link=entity_tuguegarao]Tuguegarao[/"
"link] in the north, passing through [link=entity_manila]Manila[/link], "
"[link=entity_tagkavayan]Tagkawayan[/link], [link=entity_butuan]Butuan[/"
"link], and [link=entity_davao]Davao[/link], to "
"[link=entity_pagadian_city]Pagadian City[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"There are five problems at the very top of the list. Some of them are "
"actually pretty easy fixes, but others…"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_NAME"
msgstr "Fulfill Subsidy Contracts"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_SOCIAL_SUBSIDIES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Fulfill or reject the offered subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"And so you don’t have to spend your retirement in some rundown shack, my "
"dear Mateo, we’re going to help grow the Philippine tourism industry!"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_NAME"
msgstr "Fulfill Subsidy Contracts"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_TOURISTIC_SUBSIDIES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Fulfill or reject the offered subsidy contracts."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_YACHT_HINT"
msgstr "Build a warehouse for liquids nearby to store the oil on land."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_YACHT_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"It doesn’t matter, Salita. We have to try to pump out the diesel before it "
"destroys the reef. Or we can kiss that World Heritage status goodbye."

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_YACHT_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Oil"

msgid "MISSION_06_TASK_YACHT_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver all the oil from the [link=entity_yacht]yacht[/link] to a safe "
"destination."

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "Mayor"

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Holly Travers"

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Journalist"

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Monaro Namatjira"

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Industry Representative"

msgid "MISSION_07_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Tom McLaren"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_1"
msgstr "When did you start seeking my advice, Ms. Travers?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_2"
msgstr ""
"I’m not looking for advice, I’m afraid. Let’s call it a diplomatic proposal. "
"I was thinking of introducing a big annual cultural festival."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_3"
msgstr "And what has that got to do with me?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_4"
msgstr ""
"Well, each year we will grant a contract to whoever gets to supply the "
"drinks for the festival. Your family has a vineyard, right?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_5"
msgstr "One of the most famous estates in the entire world, McLaren Valley."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_6"
msgstr ""
"Well, that’s my offer. All you have to do is accept it. Hundreds of "
"thousands of people who need to be catered for."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_7"
msgstr "And what do you expect from me?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_8"
msgstr ""
"Fairness, Mr. McLaren. Only fairness. So that there are no complications in "
"the awarding of contracts in the coming years."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_1"
msgstr ""
"Tom, I think you can be satisfied with the success of the city festival too!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_2"
msgstr "We should make this an annual event, Holly!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_3"
msgstr "Can you stop thinking about business just once, Tom?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_BONUS_COMPLETE_4"
msgstr "I’m only thinking about the city’s culture and prosperity, Holly!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_1"
msgstr "Ms. Travers, Project: Lifeless City Center is making progress!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_2"
msgstr "Nice name, and not too far off the mark, sadly."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_3"
msgstr "What do you propose to do?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_4"
msgstr ""
"We need faster supply chains so that the goods arrive in the city on time. "
"Perhaps trucks aren’t the right solution for this. The city needs to be "
"prepared for the future."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_5"
msgstr "If anyone is still living here!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_CARGO_INTERVIEW_6"
msgstr "That’s what I’ll be judged by."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_PROBLEM_1"
msgstr ""
"Ms. Travers, the people in the city center are still facing supply issues "
"and often have to drive long distances just to get the basics, which makes "
"the problems elsewhere even worse."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_PROBLEM_2"
msgstr ""
"We are well aware of that, but unfortunately you can’t undo six decades of "
"bad planning in just two years. But I can assure your readers that we are "
"working on it."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_PROBLEM_3"
msgstr "During the election campaign, you promised a much faster solution."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_CENTER_PROBLEM_4"
msgstr ""
"It’s clear that we didn’t manage to find a quick solution. But we still want "
"to find a solution, so now we’re taking the long route. The opposition, "
"though, is still clinging to their “same old, same old”!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_1"
msgstr ""
"This is the first time in Australia’s history that a city has been placed "
"under the state government’s administration. Mr. McLaren, you are a member "
"of the prime minister’s team. Where does it go from here?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_10"
msgstr ""
"If I am called upon, I won’t say no, because I love my hometown. But believe "
"me, running my own company would be far more lucrative."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_11"
msgstr "What positive outlook do you see for Adelaideans?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_12"
msgstr ""
"Now is the time for us to roll up our sleeves and create something new. In a "
"few years, we’ll be able to see the fruits of our labor."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_13"
msgstr "Are you staying?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_14"
msgstr "Of course. Now more than ever!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_2"
msgstr ""
"Well, following the collapse of the Travers administration, the first thing "
"we need to do is take stock of the finances and prepare the public for some "
"hard times."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_3"
msgstr "What’s the initial course of action after that?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_4"
msgstr ""
"The economy needs to regain momentum, the dependence on government support "
"needs to end, many things will unfortunately get a lot more expensive."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_5"
msgstr "For example?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_6"
msgstr ""
"Public transportation, culture, daycare. Nothing will be taken for granted "
"anymore."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_7"
msgstr ""
"With this list of horrors, why would anyone choose to live in Adelaide "
"anymore?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_8"
msgstr "You’ll have to put that question to the former mayor."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_FAILED_9"
msgstr "There are rumors that you have your eye on the job."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_HERALD_1"
msgstr ""
"G’day, Monaro Namatjira from the Adelaide Herald. I have a question for you, "
"Madam Mayor."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_HERALD_2"
msgstr ""
"In your election campaign, you promised to make Adelaide Australia’s most "
"livable city. How long, if you don’t mind me asking, do you want to remain "
"as mayor?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_HERALD_3"
msgstr ""
"Obviously, a project of this scale takes years and causes a lot of pain. If "
"the citizens let me, I’ll stay in office until this goal is achieved."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_HERALD_4"
msgstr ""
"There is already pushback forming in the economy. How do you intend to deal "
"with that?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_HERALD_5"
msgstr ""
"If the city thrives, so does the local economy. The gentlemen—and the few "
"women—will see that."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"You do know, Ms. Travers, that we want the same thing at the end of the day: "
"the best for our hometown."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_10"
msgstr ""
"The Northeast has always been a structurally weak region, primarily due to "
"the poor state of its public transportation system."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_11"
msgstr ""
"And then there’s the city center. It’s so densely built up that even getting "
"the bare necessities often fails due to delayed delivery times."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_12"
msgstr ""
"Alright then, Andrea, let’s get to it. We’ve made the people some big "
"promises. We have to keep them."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"In your case, Mr. McLaren, “the best” means a thriving industry in Adelaide, "
"whereas for me it means a livable city."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr ""
"You can count on my support in improving the infrastructure, Madam Mayor."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"Let’s just hope that we can agree on what an improved infrastructure should "
"look like, Mr. McLaren! Right now, only half of our residents actually want "
"to live here! Now, please excuse me. I have a meeting."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr "I’m afraid McLaren has his own ideas on that."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr ""
"We’ll find out once he gets his media channels in line. Let’s go over our "
"list one more time:"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr ""
"There are five main areas of focus. First, there is the extension of public "
"transportation in the Southwest. However, residents there are very sensitive "
"to noise."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr ""
"In the Southeast of the city, there’s pretty much constant traffic jams "
"because you can hardly reach your destination even by taking back roads."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_INTRO_9"
msgstr ""
"Industries in the Northwest should be supported as soon as possible, but at "
"the same time we must keep pollution under control."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_40_1"
msgstr ""
"Things are going in the wrong direction, Boss. Have you seen the post on "
"Adelaide Social?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_40_2"
msgstr "The one that just went viral? I’m afraid so!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_40_3"
msgstr ""
"Ms. Travers was elected to make the city cleaner, quieter, and more livable. "
"And what happens? The exact opposite! No wonder only a minority of residents "
"still want to live here!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_40_4"
msgstr "We need to do better, Andrea! Much better!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_60_1"
msgstr "We’re making progress, Boss."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_60_2"
msgstr "How so?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_60_3"
msgstr ""
"According to a recent survey, satisfaction among the citizens with the "
"overall situation in the city has risen considerably."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_60_4"
msgstr "Wonderful! Let’s not let up!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_70_1"
msgstr "Things are looking up again!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_70_2"
msgstr "I really hope so!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_70_3"
msgstr ""
"We’ve climbed into Australia’s top three favorite cities. More than two out "
"of three residents want to live here."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_70_4"
msgstr "Only the top three? That means that things can get even better, right?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_80_1"
msgstr ""
"Ms. Travers, may I ask you for your views on the latest global city rankings?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_80_2"
msgstr "Oh, I must have missed that. How did we do?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_80_3"
msgstr ""
"Adelaide has made it onto the list of the hundred most livable cities on the "
"planet for the first time ever! Didn’t anyone tell you?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_80_4"
msgstr ""
"I mainly listen to Mr. McLaren’s stations. Enemy surveillance. DON’T write "
"that!\n"
"Write: Our goal is the top ten! But we feel honored to help make life easier "
"for our citizens!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_90_1"
msgstr "Ms. Travers, I think we’re doing a great job together!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_90_2"
msgstr ""
"Well, I’m pleased to hear that. But what is it exactly that we’ve worked on "
"together?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_90_3"
msgstr ""
"On the fact that almost all our citizens like living in this city. The "
"productivity of my workers has increased significantly!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_MILESTONE_90_4"
msgstr ""
"I’m especially pleased to hear that, Mr. McLaren. Let’s keep working on "
"increasing this productivity then!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_PROBLEM_1"
msgstr ""
"Oh yeah, this one's not bad! Wisecracker15 writes: “You’re more likely to "
"find a waterfall in Alice Springs than a bus in the Northeast!” Over 3,500 "
"likes already."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_PROBLEM_2"
msgstr "We should present Alice Springs with a waterfall!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_PROBLEM_3"
msgstr "Or give the Northeast a little more attention!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_PROBLEM_4"
msgstr "Or that. It’s your choice, Andrea!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_1"
msgstr ""
"For years now, the Northeast has been promised a bright future. How have you "
"stopped that from happening so far?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_2"
msgstr ""
"We haven’t, not actively at least. We just haven’t found the right means to "
"lift the blockade yet."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_3"
msgstr ""
"What’s holding it back? The city could really use the income a flourishing "
"Northeast would bring."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_4"
msgstr ""
"It could. But there’s no convenient, fast connection to the rest of the "
"city. Same old tune."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_5"
msgstr "So, when does the curtain fall?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_EAST_TRANSPORT_INTERVIEW_6"
msgstr "We’re working on it—and trying to prevent an encore."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_1"
msgstr ""
"Mr. McLaren, you’ve been criticizing the mayor for her ideological "
"environmental policies in the Northwest. The people there can barely breathe."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_2"
msgstr ""
"The values are better than they were 60 years ago! And people back then "
"survived just fine."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_3"
msgstr "Many people died from pneumoconiosis back then."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_4"
msgstr ""
"Burdening industry with unnecessary costs doesn’t help anyone, especially if "
"half the city ends up unemployed."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_5"
msgstr "So, we don’t have any problems? You can sleep easy?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_POLLUTION_INTERVIEW_6"
msgstr "Like a baby."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_PROBLEM_1"
msgstr ""
"Mr. McLaren, I fully understand your concerns. But sick children are too "
"high a price to pay, and we will continue to pay close attention to the "
"Northwest!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_PROBLEM_2"
msgstr ""
"Who am I to disagree with you? However, I also have no influence over my "
"radio stations and local TV channels."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_PROBLEM_3"
msgstr ""
"I’ve been living with this for six months now. And that’s exactly what the "
"residents in the Northwest expect of me as well."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_NORTH_WEST_PROBLEM_4"
msgstr ""
"McLaren Industries employs many thousands of people. It doesn’t have to stay "
"that way. And without an income, what good is even the cleanest air going to "
"do them? Think about that!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_1"
msgstr ""
"Adelaide was voted one of the three most livable cities in the world. Why is "
"this more than just good city marketing?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_2"
msgstr ""
"Good air, good infrastructure, excellent supply conditions. And all that "
"while reducing noise pollution to household noise levels."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_3"
msgstr "Andrea, many of the problems were purely of a logistical nature?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_4"
msgstr ""
"A city depends on its mobility, the movement of goods, people, and ideas. "
"You have to create space. Movement and a zest for life will then follow "
"naturally."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_5"
msgstr "We wouldn’t be where we are today without Andrea, who understood that."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_6"
msgstr "You also took a real beating!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_7"
msgstr ""
"That was my job. Holly told me it would happen when she asked me to join her "
"team. The people were rightly impatient after all the decades of short-"
"sighted decisions they’ve had to endure."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_A_8"
msgstr ""
"The Adelaide Herald congratulates you, the city—and itself too a little bit!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_1"
msgstr ""
"Adelaide was voted one of the three most livable cities in the world. Why is "
"this more than just good city marketing?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_10"
msgstr ""
"Anyway. The Adelaide Herald congratulates you, the city—and itself too a "
"little bit!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_2"
msgstr ""
"We’ve achieved all this through cooperation and the constructive criticism "
"of our citizens, which has led to a whole new city culture and our wonderful "
"city festival. This isn’t marketing, these are the facts!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_3"
msgstr "Andrea, many of the problems were purely of a logistical nature?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_4"
msgstr ""
"A city depends on its mobility, the movement of goods, people, and ideas. "
"You have to create space. Movement and a zest for life will then follow "
"naturally."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_5"
msgstr ""
"We wouldn’t be where we are today without Andrea, who understood that better "
"than anyone."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_6"
msgstr ""
"That was my job. Holly told me it would happen when she asked me to join her "
"team. The people were rightly impatient after all the decades of short-"
"sighted decisions they’ve had to endure."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_7"
msgstr "You’re a globetrotter. Where are you headed next?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_8"
msgstr "A big music festival, if family tradition is anything to go by."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_OUTRO_B_9"
msgstr ""
"Our city festival could definitely be expanded into that kind of thing. How "
"about we discuss it with the city council?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_PROBLEM_1"
msgstr "Andrea, you have to hear this one!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_PROBLEM_2"
msgstr "What is it?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_PROBLEM_3"
msgstr ""
"M1dw1f3, ... oh that's Midwife, says: “Are there any birth statistics for "
"the current traffic jam in the Southeast yet?” That’s pretty funny, right?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_PROBLEM_4"
msgstr "I’m having contractions. But we’re working on it."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_1"
msgstr ""
"Andrea, you’re the mayor’s representative for infrastructure. All I’m going "
"to say is: Southeast!"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_2"
msgstr "Honestly? Spot on. What we’ve done there so far hasn’t been enough."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_3"
msgstr "To put it nicely."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_4"
msgstr ""
"For decades, the city has relied solely on cars. We need to manage traffic "
"there or consider alternatives."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_5"
msgstr "So, all the signs are pointing toward demolition?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_EAST_TRAFFIC_INTERVIEW_6"
msgstr ""
"It’s about careful planning above all else. That takes time. I fear there’s "
"no getting around some demolition, though."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_1"
msgstr "Ms. Travers, things are getting louder and louder in the Southwest."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_2"
msgstr ""
"Yes, people want to live somewhere that has convenient access to everything, "
"but without too much noise."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_3"
msgstr "So, the people are to blame?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_4"
msgstr ""
"No, more like physics. The laws of nature apply to us too. More people means "
"more noise for a start."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_5"
msgstr "Why are the noise-reduction measures taking so long?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_NOISE_INTERVIEW_6"
msgstr ""
"We have the technology, but it all needs to be bankrolled. And in some "
"cases, these aren’t just minor tweaks."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_1"
msgstr ""
"We’re really taking a beating on social media right now. There’s a post "
"doing the rounds. Want me to read it?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_2"
msgstr "What’s it say?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_3"
msgstr ""
"This Wizz349 writes: “Ms. Travers' new transit lines in the Southwest are "
"pretty fancy, but with all the noise they'd cause, she wouldn't even be able "
"to hear herself think!” Over 2,000 shares, more than 12,000 likes. Not a bot "
"account."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_4"
msgstr "The voice of the people. Loud and clear."

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_5"
msgstr "Should we respond?"

msgid "MISSION_07_CUTSCENE_SOUTH_WEST_PROBLEM_6"
msgstr "On social media? No. We’ll only make ourselves heard through actions."

msgid "MISSION_07_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Smog, traffic, noise — despite being known as one of the most livable "
"cities, Adelaide is teetering on the brink of chaos. Mayor Holly Travers is "
"feeling it in the polls and is promising improvements. But can she rise to "
"the challenge and win back the people’s trust? Without the support of "
"skilled experts, the odds are against her."

msgid "MISSION_07_GUIDE_MILESTONE_10_1"
msgstr ""
"You can’t help but admire this battered city’s will to survive. But you do "
"start to wonder: Why does Adelaide exist? What keeps its people here?"

msgid "MISSION_07_GUIDE_MILESTONE_20_1"
msgstr ""
"My daughter spent the weekend in the countryside. Now she’s traumatized by "
"the people there going outside without respirators!"

msgid "MISSION_07_GUIDE_MILESTONE_30_1"
msgstr ""
"Adelaide is in the running for a top spot on the world’s environmental "
"disaster list! The silver lining: Maybe the UN will dispatch disaster "
"prevention units soon!"

msgid "MISSION_07_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"This is it: It’s us against the McLaren family’s millions, who failed to get "
"their mayor elected for the first time in 50 years. The city is stuck in the "
"20th century: too many cars, too much noise, and public transportation "
"desperately needs improvement.\n"
"Fortunately, I have Andrea, a logistics expert with international "
"experience, by my side."

msgid "MISSION_07_LOCATION"
msgstr "Adelaide, Australia"

msgid "MISSION_07_MEDAL"
msgstr "Cheers!"

msgid "MISSION_07_MEDAL_LOCKED"
msgstr "Cheers!"

msgid "MISSION_07_NAME"
msgstr "Big City Problems"

msgid "MISSION_07_REELECTION_HINT"
msgstr ""
"As long as at least 3 of the 5 districts are satisfied, more voters will be "
"convinced."

msgid "MISSION_07_REELECTION_NAME"
msgstr "Convince Voters"

msgid "MISSION_07_REELECTION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Satisfy the needs of the districts long enough to convince all voters."

msgid "MISSION_07_STARS_INFO"
msgstr "Satisfy the needs of the districts long enough to convince all voters."

msgid "MISSION_07_STAR_1"
msgstr "Convince all voters."

msgid "MISSION_07_STAR_2"
msgstr "Convince all voters within 4 years."

msgid "MISSION_07_STAR_3"
msgstr "Convince all voters within 2 years."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "I’ll make time for it."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_BUTTON_2"
msgstr "I'm really busy right now!"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_NAME"
msgstr "Decide your Action"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_DECISION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Do you have time to organize a cultural festival?"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need a line between the winery in McLaren Valley and the city center to "
"support the big city festival!"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Beverages"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_BONUS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the beverages from [link=entity_beverages]McLaren Valley[/link] to "
"the [link=entity_botanic_garden]botanic garden[/link] in the city center."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_CENTER_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check the cargo delivery time layer to identify where the journey takes too "
"long."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_CENTER_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Supply chains to the city center are too inefficient to meet the needs of "
"the population in a timely manner."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_CENTER_NAME"
msgstr "City Center"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_CENTER_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver at least 50 units of canned food per year to the "
"[link=entity_center]City Center[/link] while maintaining a good on time "
"delivery rating."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_COMPLETE_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Off to the press conference!"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_COMPLETE_NAME"
msgstr "Election Day"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_COMPLETE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Once you are ready, let's see what the election results are saying."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_EAST_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check the passenger happiness layer and their individual details to identify "
"why they get unhappy."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_EAST_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The northeast could be such a nice place, but the current local public "
"transportation options aren't very appealing. The wait times are too long, "
"and it's uncomfortable to boot."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_EAST_NAME"
msgstr "Northeast"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_EAST_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport at least 50 passengers per year in the "
"[link=entity_north_east]Northeast[/link] while maintaining a good passenger "
"happiness rating."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_WEST_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check the pollution layer and town details to identify the causes of "
"pollution."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_WEST_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Adelaide’s major industries are located in the Northwest. We need to support "
"them if we want to count on their votes. However, air quality must not "
"suffer as a result."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_WEST_NAME"
msgstr "Northwest"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_NORTH_WEST_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver at least 50 units of steel per year to the "
"[link=entity_north_west]Northwest[/link] while maintaining a good pollution "
"rating."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_EAST_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check the traffic and passenger flow layers to identify the bottlenecks."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_EAST_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We need to do something about the Southeast. Traffic regularly comes to a "
"standstill on the chaotic roads there."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_EAST_NAME"
msgstr "Southeast"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_EAST_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport at least 50 passengers per year in the "
"[link=entity_south_east]Southeast[/link] and ensure a good traffic rating."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_WEST_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check the noise layer and town details to identify the causes of noise."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_WEST_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Residents in the Southwest are particularly sensitive to noise. "
"Nevertheless, we must try to expand passenger transport services there."

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_WEST_NAME"
msgstr "Southwest"

msgid "MISSION_07_TASK_SOUTH_WEST_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport at least 50 passengers per year in the "
"[link=entity_south_west]Southwest[/link] while maintaining a good noise "
"rating."

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_1_INFO"
msgstr "First Japanese Woman in Space"

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_1_NAME"
msgstr "Chisato Murai"

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_2_INFO"
msgstr "Mission Director"

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_2_NAME"
msgstr "Takumi Arakawa"

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_3_INFO"
msgstr "Female Astronaut"

msgid "MISSION_08_CHARACTER_3_NAME"
msgstr "Sayoko Tanizaki"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_A_1"
msgstr ""
"Takumi, a press release was just announced that the third astronaut is a "
"European?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_A_2"
msgstr ""
"An Italian, yes. Diplomacy. International cooperation. Cofinancing. We’re "
"not an isolated country anymore, Chisato-san."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_A_3"
msgstr "No, and I very much welcome that. When will we meet our colleague?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_A_4"
msgstr ""
"He’s in the training center. Sayoko’s already interviewing him for her "
"channel!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_A_5"
msgstr "How reassuring."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_1"
msgstr ""
"Please tell me, Murai-buchō: Were you very nervous before you flew the first "
"time?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_2"
msgstr "Is this another one of your live broadcasts?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_3"
msgstr "No, the camera’s off."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_4"
msgstr "You’ve already been to the ISS."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_5"
msgstr "Yes, but the moon is something completely different."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ADDITIVE_B_6"
msgstr ""
"You should always be nervous, Tanizaki-san. Being nervous heightens your "
"awareness. Nervousness is good! It’s fear that paralyzes you."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_AUDIENCE_1"
msgstr ""
"Here we are, dear followers, outside the Spaceport Hotel, where the prime "
"minister and her entourage will be staying in just a few weeks. And with a "
"bit of luck, I will get to shake her hand."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_AUDIENCE_2"
msgstr ""
"You will not, Tanizaki-san. You are going to give her a traditional bow. "
"This is not NASA!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_AUDIENCE_3"
msgstr ""
"And here’s the well-meaning educational advice from Murai-buchō, who’s been "
"making sure my feet stay firmly planted on Earth since day one. As a person, "
"that is. But eventually I will get to lift off! Catch you tomorrow, guys!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_AUDIENCE_4"
msgstr ""
"Whether you do actually lift off in the end, Tanizaki-san, also depends on "
"you doing a little less PR work and a little more training."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_AUDIENCE_5"
msgstr "I’m on my way, Murai-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_CATERING_1"
msgstr ""
"Andrea, perhaps we should serve something other than just Japanese cuisine? "
"We do have international guests."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_CATERING_2"
msgstr ""
"And an Italian astronaut. It’d be a meaningful gesture of humility and "
"friendship between nations if we perhaps offered an Italian fish dish too."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_CATERING_3"
msgstr "I’ve never been to Italy. Do they know how to prepare fish there?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_CATERING_4"
msgstr "Italian food is almost on par with Japanese cuisine!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_CATERING_5"
msgstr "You are very diplomatic, Andrea. If you say that, it must be amazing."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_1"
msgstr ""
"Just six months until launch. Where do we stand on the logistics front, "
"Andrea-san?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_10"
msgstr ""
"And then there’s all the deliveries to the launch pad, shuttling staff to "
"the control center, and so on. I do not envy you, Andrea-san. But I have "
"every confidence in you."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_11"
msgstr "Then it’s time for me to get back to work, Arakawa-buchō!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_12"
msgstr ""
"The rocket assembly line needs to be continuously supplied with machine "
"parts from the machine factory. This is our number one priority. No rocket, "
"no moon mission!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_13"
msgstr ""
"The fuel for the rocket consists of kerosene and an oxidizer. The kerosene "
"needs to be transported from the refinery to the space center. It’s also "
"unclear whether the refinery has enough capacity!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_14"
msgstr ""
"The oxidizer comes from the chemical plant. That needs to be brought to the "
"space center. This factory is also having production issues and needs more "
"workers."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_15"
msgstr ""
"Most workers live in the cities farther north. We need a bus line to "
"Nishinoomote that connects the cities to the space center."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_2"
msgstr ""
"Good morning, Arakawa-buchō! We are experiencing difficulties with fuel "
"deliveries. We need kerosene and oxidizer. The supply chains to both the "
"refinery and chemical plant haven’t been established yet, and the factories "
"still haven’t reached the required capacity."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_3"
msgstr ""
"The construction of the launch vehicle is on schedule, however, but we need "
"to sort out the logistics for the required propulsion system parts soon. The "
"machine factory is having some capacity and supply issues."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_4"
msgstr ""
"Excuse me, but… do you really not have a family name? That takes some "
"getting used to for an old Japanese man."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_5"
msgstr "Call me Andrea, please. Just Andrea. As if Andrea were my family name."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_6"
msgstr "Very well, Andrea-san. How concerned are you about the problems?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_7"
msgstr ""
"It’s going to be tight, but we can do it. It’s also a matter of the budget."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_8"
msgstr ""
"Do bear in mind that the country has to save money. The less everything "
"costs, the better it is for Japan!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_INTRO_9"
msgstr ""
"And when the prime minister shows up for the launch, she and her entourage "
"won’t want to take a public bus from their hotel to the observation platform."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_KEROSENE_A_1"
msgstr ""
"I have quite literally highly explosive news! Today, the first deliveries of "
"kerosene arrived here at the space center. And the announcement of who will "
"be joining us on board as the third astronaut will be made very soon. I am "
"super excited! Stay tuned!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_KEROSENE_B_1"
msgstr ""
"Andrea-san, according to my chemical scientists, the kerosene delivered so "
"far cannot be used. It is missing an important additive."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_KEROSENE_B_2"
msgstr "What do we need to do?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_KEROSENE_B_3"
msgstr ""
"Stop the current deliveries and send the kerosene that has already been "
"delivered back to the refinery. You should also arrange delivery of the "
"additive from the chemical plant to the refinery."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_KEROSENE_B_4"
msgstr "I’m on it!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_A_1"
msgstr ""
"Right now, dear followers, the rocket doesn’t look like it’d reach the moon. "
"But with me here is a legend of Japanese space travel, Chisato Murai—the "
"first Japanese woman in space. Murai-buchō, what do you think about the "
"progress of the rocket construction?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_A_2"
msgstr ""
"This kind of assembly would usually take three months, so I am very "
"optimistic that everything will work out. Wait, is this being broadcast live?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_A_3"
msgstr ""
"We currently have 7,600 viewers! Who do you think will join us as the third "
"astronaut?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_A_4"
msgstr "You should focus on your training, Tanizaki-san! Turn that thing off."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_1"
msgstr ""
"And that’s all from the Tanegashima Space Center, where I’m preparing for my "
"second space mission. You heard what she said: Tanizaki-san needs to train. "
"I’ll see you again tomorrow!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_2"
msgstr "The rocket is making progress."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_3"
msgstr "It’s beautiful!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_4"
msgstr "The zenith of Japanese engineering."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_5"
msgstr ""
"And yet, without your logistical brilliance, Andrea-hakase, there would just "
"be an empty launch pad here."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_B_6"
msgstr "Just Andrea, please. I don't have a PhD, Murai-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_C_1"
msgstr ""
"The rocket that will take me to the moon looks absolutely incredible. You "
"can’t even imagine how enormous it is when you stand next to it!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_C_2"
msgstr "It’s not taking just you to the moon, Sayoko. We’re a team!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MACHINE_C_3"
msgstr "Of course, Murai-buchō!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MORE_MONEY_A_1"
msgstr ""
"The additional funds have been granted, Andrea-san. But the prime minister "
"made a very expressive frown when doing so."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_MORE_MONEY_B_1"
msgstr ""
"The additional funds have been granted, but the way the prime minister "
"looked at me made it quite clear that this would be the last time."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_1"
msgstr "You seem as calm as a deep forest lake on a windless day, Chisato-san."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_2"
msgstr ""
"But deep below the surface, on the lakebed, a great fish watches tirelessly "
"over everything that is happening above him, Takumi-san."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_3"
msgstr "And what does the great fish see?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_4"
msgstr ""
"A small, young pike who wants to rule the pond—and one day she will. And an "
"unfamiliar, old fish who is very polite and careful not to encroach on "
"anyone’s territory."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_5"
msgstr ""
"The Norwegian without a family name? Yes, very polite. And everything is "
"fine?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_A_6"
msgstr "Everything is fine until it’s no longer fine."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_B_1"
msgstr ""
"Chisato-san, do you believe young Sayoko will be of any help to you on board?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_B_2"
msgstr ""
"She is so different from us. She’s very talented. And very easily "
"distracted. Without those distractions, up there in space, her talent will "
"prevail."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_B_3"
msgstr ""
"She wants to create a window into our world. But she still has to learn that "
"in doing so, she is reducing herself to a puppet."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_B_4"
msgstr "Were we any smarter, Takumi-san? Thirty years ago?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_OXIDIZER_B_5"
msgstr "Are we today, Chisato-san?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_1"
msgstr "Arakawa to Murai-buchō. All systems checked?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_2"
msgstr "All systems checked. Everything’s running as it should."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_3"
msgstr "T-minus 20 seconds. How are you feeling on board?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_4"
msgstr ""
"Sayoko-san and Tomaso-san have both left their cell phones in the locker "
"room."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_5"
msgstr ""
"Good for them. We’ll speak again later, once you’ve left Earth’s "
"gravitational field."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_6"
msgstr "I’ll send you a postcard, Takumi-san!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_7"
msgstr "Yon… san… ni… ichi… zerooooo"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_8"
msgstr "Everything’s going according to plan. We did it, Andrea!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_9"
msgstr "It’s been a great honor, Arakawa-buchō!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_1"
msgstr ""
"I must admit my failure, Andrea-san. We need to postpone the rocket launch."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_2"
msgstr ""
"I’m sorry. I’m afraid I underestimated the scale of the job, Arakawa-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_3"
msgstr ""
"It is my responsibility. And I may have lost the title of “buchō.” I will go "
"see the prime minister and offer her my resignation. She will accept it."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_4"
msgstr "I will come with you, Takumi-san."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_5"
msgstr ""
"You won’t do that. You’ll be needed for the next attempt. Someone younger "
"will take over from me. And that’s the right thing to happen."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_6"
msgstr ""
"The three of us know it was my fault. If you resign, Arakawa-buchō, the "
"wrong person will bear the consequences."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_7"
msgstr ""
"Japan won’t pin this failure on any of its partners, Andrea-san. I know that "
"would be the modern thing to do. Modern—and dishonorable. No, it is better "
"this way. And my garden will appreciate the time I get to spend with it from "
"tomorrow."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_ROCKET_START_FAIL_8"
msgstr "I will always seek your advice, Takumi-san."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_A_1"
msgstr "So many workers, and they’re all here to get me to the moon."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_A_2"
msgstr ""
"It’s not about you, Tanizaki-san. It’s about getting three humans to the "
"moon and back alive. Whoever those humans are."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_A_3"
msgstr "That’s what I meant, Murai-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_A_4"
msgstr ""
"Then say what you mean. Or stop meaning what you say. Up there, beyond our "
"atmosphere, only the absolute respect for the truth will help us!"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_B_1"
msgstr "The success of the flight depends more on these workers than on us."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_B_2"
msgstr "What are you trying to tell me, Murai-buchō?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_B_3"
msgstr ""
"Treat them with respect, as if they were your parents, so that they protect "
"you like you were their own child."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_B_4"
msgstr "I understand, Murai-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_C_1"
msgstr ""
"What you’ve accomplished is truly admirable, Andrea-san. The site is buzzing "
"like a beehive."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_C_2"
msgstr "Thank you, Arakawa-buchō."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_C_3"
msgstr ""
"What do you make of young Sayoko? What’s the—well—European perspective?"

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_C_4"
msgstr ""
"Do not doubt her. Every era has produced precisely the children who can "
"handle what it throws at them."

msgid "MISSION_08_CUTSCENE_WORKERS_C_5"
msgstr "That is very true, Andrea-hakase!"

msgid "MISSION_08_DESC"
msgstr ""
"The international space program is on the verge of reaching a major "
"milestone. After lengthy delays, the 21st-century lunar mission is now set "
"to begin, but there’s still lots to prepare before liftoff: Rocket "
"components, fuel, and the crew need to be brought together at the Japanese "
"space center."

msgid "MISSION_08_LOADSCREEN"
msgstr ""
"The first manned lunar landing since ages, and I have the honor of a "
"lifetime to be the director of the program. Nothing can go wrong if Japan "
"doesn’t want to lose face in front of the world. Fortunately, I have Chisato "
"by my side, just like 35 years ago when she became the first Japanese woman "
"in space. And we have secured the services of a Norwegian, whose logistical "
"skills are said to be nothing short of miraculous.\n"
"And we’re going to need them—the countdown is on."

msgid "MISSION_08_LOCATION"
msgstr "Tanegashima, Japan"

msgid "MISSION_08_MEDAL_1"
msgstr "Organize the watch party."

msgid "MISSION_08_MEDAL_1_LOCKED"
msgstr "Organize the watch party."

msgid "MISSION_08_NAME"
msgstr "Final Countdown"

msgid "MISSION_08_STARS_INFO"
msgstr ""
"Prepare everything for the rocket launch, and don’t lose sight of the launch "
"window."

msgid "MISSION_08_STAR_1"
msgstr "Ensure the rocket is launched on schedule."

msgid "MISSION_08_STAR_2"
msgstr ""
"Ensure the rocket is launched on schedule without repeatedly increasing the "
"budget."

msgid "MISSION_08_STAR_3"
msgstr ""
"Ensure the rocket is launched on schedule without increasing the budget."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ADDITIVE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"So, back to square one. Return the kerosene to the refinery and then arrange "
"deliveries of the additive. We should also make sure that both factories can "
"meet their production targets!"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ADDITIVE_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Additive"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ADDITIVE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver additive from the [link=entity_chemical_plant]chemical plant[/link] "
"to the [link=entity_refinery]refinery[/link] so production of stabilized "
"kerosene can start."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_AUDIENCE_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"To keep the distinguished guests from having to ride the public bus to the "
"observation platform, we should arrange a shuttle service to and from the "
"hotel."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_AUDIENCE_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Transport Line"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_AUDIENCE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a new line from the [link=entity_hotel]hotel[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_observation_point]observation platform[/link] to transport the "
"guests."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_CATERING_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"The people on the observation platform shouldn’t go hungry. We should take "
"them fresh fish from the harbor."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_CATERING_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Food"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_CATERING_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver food to the guests on the [link=entity_observation_point]observation "
"platform[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_KEROSENE_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Kerosene"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_KEROSENE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the kerosene from the [link=entity_refinery]refinery[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_space_center]rocket[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MACHINE_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Machine Parts"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MACHINE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the machine parts from the machine factory to the "
"[link=entity_space_center]rocket assembly line[/link] to assemble the rocket."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_A_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Accept"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_A_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Our budget has already been greatly reduced, Andrea-san. With your approval, "
"I can request additional funding from Tokyo."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_A_NAME"
msgstr "Accept More Funding"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_A_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Accept more funds at the cost of losing a star."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_B_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Accept"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_B_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"And once again we seem to be running out of money. If it is absolutely "
"necessary, Andrea-san, I will make another trip to Tokyo."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_B_NAME"
msgstr "Accept Additional Funding"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_MORE_MONEY_B_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Accept additional funds at the cost of losing another star."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_OXIDATOR_NAME"
msgstr "Deliver Oxidizer"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_OXIDATOR_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the oxidizer from the [link=entity_chemical_plant]chemical plant[/"
"link] to the [link=entity_space_center]rocket[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_PREPARATION_HINT"
msgstr ""
"Check what is needed to produce the required cargo. Use enough vehicles to "
"deliver the needed amounts in time but keep an eye on the budget."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_PREPARATION_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"We urgently need machine parts for the assembly of the rocket. It also needs "
"kerosene and the oxidizer. We mustn’t lose track of time, and we also need "
"to think about the workers from Nishinoomote."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_PREPARATION_NAME"
msgstr "Prepare the Launch"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_PREPARATION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Deliver the required amounts of cargo in the specified time window to the "
"[link=entity_space_center]launch pad[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ROCKET_START_BUTTON_1"
msgstr "Call the shuttle"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ROCKET_START_INSTRUCTION"
msgstr ""
"Now all we need to do is bring the astronauts from the space center to the "
"rocket."

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ROCKET_START_NAME"
msgstr "Launch the Rocket"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_ROCKET_START_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "Ready for lift off?"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_WORKERS_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Staff"

msgid "MISSION_08_TASK_WORKERS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Transport staff members to the [link=entity_space_center]launch pad[/link]."

msgid "MISSION_3_MAINTENANCE_NAME"
msgstr "Maintenance"

msgid "MISSION_3_MAINTENANCE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"The harsh conditions of the Wadi Rum desert make vehicles especially prone "
"to wear and tear. To keep them from breaking down, you'll need to deliver "
"tools to the campsite. Once an oasis is established, they act as maintenance "
"buildings and any vehicle within its maintenance radius will be maintained. "
"Outside that radius, however, a vehicle's condition deteriorates rapidly, "
"and once it reaches 0%, the vehicle breaks down. You can see all maintenance "
"areas when you select a truck or an oasis."

msgid "MISSION_3_RIDDLES_NAME"
msgstr "Solve the Riddle"

msgid "MISSION_3_RIDDLES_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To find your way through the desert, listen closely to Salim Al-Zalabia. He "
"often speaks in riddles, but if you pay attention, you'll work out the right "
"path. Follow it, and you can establish an oasis at the campsites along the "
"way. Take a wrong turn, and the desert will punish you, with no way to keep "
"your trucks running."

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_DELIVERY_NAME"
msgstr "On Time Delivery"

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_DELIVERY_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Cargo is expected to be delivered on time. If it arrives too late, the town "
"rating decreases.\n"
"\n"
"To ensure a timely delivery, make sure that transport vehicles are not stuck "
"in traffic and have an optimal transport route. In addition, specialized "
"warehouses extend the time limit for the delivery."

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_HAPPINESS_NAME"
msgstr "Passenger Happiness"

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_HAPPINESS_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Passengers get unhappy, whenever they have to wait for a long time for "
"public transport, or when they have to drive for a while in uncomfortable "
"vehicles.\n"
"\n"
"To improve passenger happiness, make sure that long passenger lines use "
"vehicles with enough comfort. In addition, the bus lane tool can be used to "
"reserve lanes for public transport. Alternatively, underground tram lines "
"can be built which are faster and have more capacity."

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_NOISE_NAME"
msgstr "Noise"

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_NOISE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Noise is caused by too much traffic with loud vehicles and by large "
"buildings such as stations. Industrial and commercial buildings are not "
"affected by noise, but residential ones are. \n"
"\n"
"To relieve the residents, use quiet vehicles in residential areas. Wherever "
"possible, redirect traffic around the residential districts or otherwise use "
"noise barriers along tracks and highways to minimize noise emission."

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_POLLUTION_NAME"
msgstr "Pollution"

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_POLLUTION_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Pollution is mostly caused by dirty vehicles and large buildings, such as "
"stations, warehouses, depots, and also by industries, and the pollution "
"affects the entire town area.\n"
"To counter the pollution, consider using electrified vehicles whenever "
"possible, plant trees along roads and near polluting buildings, and try to "
"minimize the polluting infrastructure. Always check the pollution rating "
"before building infrastructure or buying vehicles."

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_TRAFFIC_NAME"
msgstr "Traffic"

msgid "MISSION_7_GUIDE_TRAFFIC_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Traffic jams can be caused by limited road capacities, a suboptimal road "
"layout that does not fit to the traffic flow or many consecutive "
"intersections on busy roads.\n"
"\n"
"To prevent traffic jams, bypasses around dense areas can be used. Try to "
"distribute traffic across different routes by adding more connections "
"between crowded areas. The intersection and traffic light tools can be used "
"to adjust the flow for individual intersections."

msgid "MISSION_PROPOSAL_FEEDBACK_NOT_A_ROAD_DEPOT"
msgstr "Pick the depot for road vehicles."

msgid "MISSION_PROPOSAL_FEEDBACK_NOT_CONNECTED_TO_STREET"
msgstr "Must be connected to a road."

msgid "MISSION_PROPOSAL_FEEDBACK_NOT_IN_OUTLINED_AREA"
msgstr "Only possible in the highlighted area."

msgid "MISSION_PROPOSAL_FEEDBACK_RESTRICTED_AREA"
msgstr "Construction is not allowed here."

msgid "MOD_NO_COSTS_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The No Costs mod disables money completely. Everything is for free and the "
"bank balance is shown as infinite."

msgid "MOD_NO_COSTS_NAME"
msgstr "No Costs"

msgid "MOD_NO_COSTS_SUMMARY"
msgstr "Everything is for free and there is unlimited money."

msgid "MOD_NO_END_YEAR_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Vehicles that are purchasable by the player do not have an end year. As soon "
"as they become available, they remain available forever."

msgid "MOD_NO_END_YEAR_NAME"
msgstr "Vehicles: No End Year"

msgid "MOD_NO_END_YEAR_SUMMARY"
msgstr "Player vehicles have no end year and are available forever."

msgid "MOD_SANDBOX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Sandbox Mode allows to change various aspects of the game. With this "
"mod, it is possible to modify the bank balance, set the in-game calendar to "
"a specific date, and construct new towns or industries. Additionally, this "
"mod allows adjusting cargo demands and the size of generated towns, or even "
"demolishing them."

msgid "MOD_SANDBOX_NAME"
msgstr "Sandbox Mode"

msgid "MOD_SANDBOX_SUMMARY"
msgstr ""
"Allows to change various aspects of the game, such as the date and bank "
"balance."

msgid "MOD_TYCOON_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Tycoon mod sets the company rank to the highest level and unlocks all "
"perks. All other aspects of the game remain unchanged. This allows to place "
"all landmarks, prospect for resources and use the marketing campaigns and "
"the greenify industry tool."

msgid "MOD_TYCOON_NAME"
msgstr "Tycoon"

msgid "MOD_TYCOON_SUMMARY"
msgstr "The company rank is set to Tycoon and all perks are unlocked."

msgid "MOUSE_EXTEND_LINE_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Extending Lines"

msgid "MOUSE_EXTEND_LINE_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Often you want to modify an existing line. Start by selecting the line you "
"want to change, either in the 3D world or in the line manager window. With "
"the line selected, you can modify it in several ways: drag and drop "
"individual stops in the window to reorder them, remove a stop with the trash "
"bin icon, or add a stop by selecting a station in the 3D world. The new stop "
"is added after the stop that is currently selected in the line manager "
"window."

msgid "MOUSE_WAYPOINT_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Adding Waypoints"

msgid "MOUSE_WAYPOINT_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"If you want to reroute your vehicles to avoid quiet town roads or if you "
"want to ease traffic congestion, you can add waypoints on your line. Select "
"the stop after which you want to add your waypoint in the line manager "
"window and hold [iaHint=IA_PRECISION_MODE/] while clicking on the map to "
"place your waypoint."

