msgstr "Small Street With Tram Tracks"

msgid "STREET_TOWN_OLD_SMALL_TRAM_NAME"
msgstr "Small Street With Tram Tracks"

msgid "STREET_TOWN_OLD_SMALL_TREES_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Two-lane cobblestone road that features a sidewalk, making it well-suited "
"for use in towns. The trees reduce pollution and noise, at the cost of a "
"lower speed limit."

msgid "STREET_TOWN_OLD_SMALL_TREES_NAME"
msgstr "Small Street With Trees"

msgid "STREET_TOWN_OLD_XSMALL_DESC"
msgstr ""
"Narrow two-lane cobblestone road that features a sidewalk, making it well-"
"suited for use in towns."

msgid "STREET_TOWN_OLD_XSMALL_NAME"
msgstr "Narrow Street"

msgid "STREET_TRAM_NEW_DESC"
msgstr "Two-lane tracks that are exclusively for trams."

msgid "STREET_TRAM_NEW_NAME"
msgstr "Tram Tracks"

msgid "STREET_TRAM_OLD_DESC"
msgstr "Two-lane tracks that are exclusively for trams."

msgid "STREET_TRAM_OLD_NAME"
msgstr "Tram Tracks"

msgid "Signals Built"
msgstr "Signals Built"

msgid "Silsden"
msgstr "Silsden"

msgid "Silsden Crop Farm"
msgstr "Silsden Crop Farm"

msgid "Silsden Logging Camp"
msgstr "Silsden Logging Camp"

msgid "Switches Built"
msgstr "Switches Built"

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_1"
msgstr "Build bridges high enough for ships to pass."

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_12"
msgstr ""
"To transfer cargo between different means of transport, a warehouse must be "
"built."

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_2"
msgstr ""
"The construction and upkeep costs of bridges and tunnels depend on their "
"height and depth."

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_3"
msgstr "Use the track modification tool to upgrade non-electrified tracks."

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_4"
msgstr ""
"Follow the contour lines during track construction - terrain adjustments are "
"expensive!"

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_5"
msgstr ""
"Avoid tight radii during track construction, as these reduce the maximum "
"permissible speed."

msgid "TIP_CONSTRUCTION_7"
msgstr ""
"Hold [iaHint=IA_PRECISION_MODE/] when rebuilding roads or tracks to edit "
"them segment by segment only."

msgid "TIP_INDUSTRIES_1"
msgstr ""
"The industry window shows the current production rate, boosters and stocks."

msgid "TIP_INDUSTRIES_2"
msgstr ""
"Check the industry window to see which suppliers cover the demand and to "
"which customers the products are shipped."

msgid "TIP_LVM_1"
msgstr ""
"The line manager allows to create new lines by selecting a station icon in "
"the world."

msgid "TIP_LVM_2"
msgstr ""
"In the line manager, an existing line can be extended by additional stations "
"after selecting the desired line section."

msgid "TIP_LVM_3"
msgstr ""
"The line manager allows to adjust the loading rules for each stop by first "
"selecting the line and then hovering over the stop number."

msgid "TIP_LVM_4"
msgstr ""
"The line manager allows to select vehicles, by selecting their icon in the "
"world."

msgid "TIP_LVM_5"
msgstr ""
"The line manager allows to send vehicles to a line, by selecting the line in "
"the world."

msgid "TIP_MISC_1"
msgstr ""
"Vehicles and people can be tracked via the pin at the top left of their "
"window."

msgid "TIP_MISC_2"
msgstr "The autosave interval can be set in the advanced game options."

msgid "TIP_MISC_3"
msgstr "Right-click can be used to close windows or navigate back."

msgid "TIP_MISC_4"
msgstr ""
"The headquarters can be built in a municipal area to provide increased "
"growth rate for this town."

msgid "TIP_MISC_5"
msgstr ""
"With increasing company level, new side buildings and decorations are "
"unlocked for the headquarters."

msgid "TIP_MISC_6"
msgstr "Pressing [iaHint=IA_QUICKSAVE/] quicksaves the game."

msgid "TIP_MISC_7"
msgstr ""
"Landmarks provide a bonus to certain vehicles within the same municipal area."

msgid "TIP_MOD_1"
msgstr "Download new game content through the Mod Hub."

msgid "TIP_TOWNS_3"
msgstr ""
"Avoid long waiting times, congestion and excessive noise and pollution "
"emissions in towns as these factors hinder growth."

msgid "TIP_TOWNS_4"
msgstr ""
"For towns to grow, their cargo demand must be fulfilled and passengers "
"transported."

msgid "TIP_TOWNS_5"
msgstr ""
"Growing towns increases the company level and unlocks perks and other "
"bonuses."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_1"
msgstr ""
"For the most cost-efficient operation, locomotives and wagons should have "
"similar maximum speeds."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_2"
msgstr "Depots are necessary to buy vehicles and send them on a line."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_4"
msgstr ""
"The frequency of a line indicates the time interval between the vehicles."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_6"
msgstr ""
"For vehicles, a high number of maintenance buildings leads to lower "
"emissions, but causes higher costs."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_7"
msgstr ""
"Some trains and street vehicles are specialized for a specific cargo type. "
"The specialization allows for faster loading and unloading speeds, when used "
"with the corresponding type of terminal."

msgid "TIP_VEHICLES_8"
msgstr ""
"Depots or maintenance buildings allow to maintain vehicles in their "
"catchment area."

msgid "TRACK_HIGHSPEED_CATENARY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"High-speed tracks that enable higher speeds, at the cost of increased "
"pollution. The catenary enables the use of electric trains."

msgid "TRACK_HIGHSPEED_CATENARY_NAME"
msgstr "High-Speed Tracks With Catenary"

msgid "TRACK_HIGHSPEED_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"High-speed tracks that enable higher speeds, at the cost of increased "
"pollution."

msgid "TRACK_HIGHSPEED_NAME"
msgstr "High-Speed Tracks"

msgid "TRACK_SIMPLE_CATENARY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Simple tracks with reduced pollution, at the cost of only supporting slow "
"speeds. The catenary enables the use of electric trains."

msgid "TRACK_SIMPLE_CATENARY_NAME"
msgstr "Simple Tracks With Catenary"

msgid "TRACK_SIMPLE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Simple tracks with reduced pollution, at the cost of only supporting slow "
"speeds."

msgid "TRACK_SIMPLE_NAME"
msgstr "Simple Tracks"

msgid "TRACK_STANDARD_CATENARY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Standard tracks that support medium speeds. The catenary enables the use of "
"electric trains."

msgid "TRACK_STANDARD_CATENARY_NAME"
msgstr "Standard Tracks With Catenary"

msgid "TRACK_STANDARD_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Standard tracks that support medium speeds."

msgid "TRACK_STANDARD_NAME"
msgstr "Standard Tracks"

msgid "TUTORIAL_ASSIGN_VEHICLE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Assign Your Vehicle"

msgid "TUTORIAL_ASSIGN_VEHICLE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Select the [link=entity_depot]road depot[/link] and select the manage "
"vehicles button. This will open up the line manager with your bus selected. "
"Assign the bus to your newly created line with the send to line button."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Connect Industry"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Let's supply [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] with some vegetables! But "
"first, we have to connect the [link=entity_farm]farm[/link] to the town. For "
"that, connect the industry with the town by constructing new roads."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_DECISION_FUEL_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ready to learn more?"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_DECISION_FUEL_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Wonderful, the first passenger has boarded your train! If you're ready to "
"learn how to transport fuel, let me know!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_DECISION_FUEL_TRAIN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Fantastic!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_DECISION_FUEL_TRAIN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Fantastic job! Your town should now start growing more quickly. There's "
"still more to learn, though. Ideally, every town should have sufficient "
"public transport, while its commercial and industrial districts should "
"receive a steady supply of cargo.\n"
"\n"
"When you're ready, choose what to learn next: how to establish a fuel supply "
"line or how to set up a train line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_FUEL_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Fuel Supply"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_FUEL_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Now, we can supply [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] with fuel. Connect "
"the station next to the [link=entity_warehouse]warehouse[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_oil_ref]oil refinery[/link], and the [link=entity_oil_ref]oil "
"refinery[/link] to [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]. You could use one "
"or two different lines for that. Lastly, you need to send some trucks on the "
"lines!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Harbor and Ship Depot"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To transport the oil from the [link=entity_oil_plt]oil platform[/link] to "
"the [link=entity_oil_ref]oil refinery[/link], you need to build up your "
"water infrastructure. Let's start by building a harbor and a ship depot."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_INDUSTRY_WINDOW_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Open Oil Platform Window"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_INDUSTRY_WINDOW_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Open the industry window of your [link=entity_oil_plt]oil platform[/link] "
"too see how much oil is currently being produced."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_LINE_COMMERCIAL_ASSIGN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Buy and Assign Truck"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_LINE_COMMERCIAL_ASSIGN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a truck in the [link=entity_depot]road depot[/link] that can transport "
"vegetables and assign it to your line that connects the farm and the "
"commercial district of [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_LINE_COMMERCIAL_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Create a Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_LINE_COMMERCIAL_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Create a line from the station integrated in the [link=entity_farm]farm[/"
"link] to the commercial district of [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SECOND_VEHICLE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "More Vehicles"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SECOND_VEHICLE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"We noticed that you have only a single vehicle on your line from the "
"[link=entity_oil_ref]oil refinery[/link] to [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/"
"link]. To meet the demands of the town, you should probably use multiple "
"vehicles on each line. Start by adding a second truck on this line!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SHIP_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ship Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SHIP_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Next, create a new line from the [link=entity_oil_plt]oil platform[/link] to "
"the [link=entity_harbor]harbor[/link] and send a suitable ship on the line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SUPPLY_TOWN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Supply Town"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_SUPPLY_TOWN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Great job! Now we have to wait until the goods arrive in [link=entity_town]"
"{TOWN_NAME}[/link]. In the meantime you can optimize your routes or start "
"supplying different towns."

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_TRANSPORT_VEGETABLES_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Vegetables"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_TRANSPORT_VEGETABLES_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Nice work! Now the first vegetables should arrive in [link=entity_town]"
"{TOWN_NAME}[/link] shortly. Let's wait until they arrive!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_TRUCK_STATION_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Cargo Station"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_TRUCK_STATION_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To pick up the oil from the warehouse, we need to build a cargo station "
"close to the [link=entity_warehouse]warehouse[/link].\n"
"Don't forget to connect it to a road!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_WAREHOUSE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Warehouse"

msgid "TUTORIAL_A_WAREHOUSE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a warehouse next to the [link=entity_harbor]harbor[/link] so that you "
"can start bringing your oil barrels ashore. Make sure that the warehouse is "
"in the catchment area of the harbor."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BEFORE_CARGO_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ready to Move On?"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BEFORE_CARGO_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Congratulations! You've created your first passenger line! As soon as the "
"first passengers are transported, the town will begin to grow. To accelerate "
"its growth, the town also needs a steady supply of cargo.\n"
"\n"
"Let me know when you're ready to set up your first cargo line!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BEGINNING_COMPLETE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Learn More"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BEGINNING_COMPLETE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Next, you need set up the infrastructure to start supplying your town. Let "
"me know when you're ready to continue."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_HQ_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Build Your Headquarters"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_HQ_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Construct the headquarters in the region of any town. The headquarters gives "
"this town a 5% growth bonus. With increasing company rank more and more side "
"buildings for the headquarters are unlocked, that come with even more perks."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_HQ_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Your Headquarters"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_HQ_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To get started, build a headquarters as the heart of your business, a symbol "
"of your success, and a starting point for your expansion.\n"
"\n"
"To do so, select the perks button in the construction menu and place the "
"headquarters on the map."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_DEPOT_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Road Depot"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_DEPOT_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"The road depot serves two purposes. It is the vehicle depot for road "
"vehicles, where trucks and buses can be purchased, modified, and replaced. "
"It also provides maintenance for vehicles operating within its maintenance "
"radius."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_DEPOT_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Road Depot"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_DEPOT_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To buy vehicles, you first need to build a road depot. Make sure it is "
"connected to a road."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_1_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Road Stop"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_1_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Road stops are used to load and unload passengers, and to unload cargo. "
"While placing a stop, residential buildings are highlighted in green, "
"commercial buildings in blue, and industrial buildings in yellow.\n"
"\n"
"Buildings within the stop's catchment area receive an additional highlight "
"on their plot: green indicates the building is within range for passengers, "
"blue indicates it is within range for cargo, and white indicates it is "
"within range for both."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_1_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Road Stop"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_1_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Every town needs public transport. So let's start with that. Select a road "
"stop from the construction menu and place it in the residential district of "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_2_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Two More Road Stops"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_ROAD_STOP_2_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Great! Now build two more road stops in [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/"
"link]. Place one in the commercial and the other one in the industrial "
"district."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRACKS_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Tracks"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRACKS_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"There are three track types available, depending on the year you’re playing: "
"simple, standard, and high-speed. Faster track types are more expensive and "
"generate more noise and pollution. Keep these trade-offs in mind when "
"planning your routes."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRACKS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Tracks"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRACKS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Continue by connecting the train station near [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/"
"link] and the one near [link=entity_town_2]{TOWN_NAME_2}[/link] with tracks. "
"Select the tracks in the construction menu and build a consecutive path "
"between the stations."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRAIN_STATIONS_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Train Stations"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRAIN_STATIONS_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Passenger and cargo train stations are available and can be fully customized "
"after construction. To get started, several commonly used templates are "
"provided, including simple terminal and through stations with a single main "
"building.\n"
"\n"
"After construction, the number and length of platforms can be adjusted, as "
"well as the track layout and style."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRAIN_STATIONS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Train Stations"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUILD_TRAIN_STATIONS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Let's establish a passenger train line between [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}"
"[/link] and  [link=entity_town_2]{TOWN_NAME_2}[/link]. For that, we need to "
"place two passenger train stations close to the towns. Since our towns are "
"still quite small, an 80 m long station will be sufficient."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_BUS_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Passenger Vehicle"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_BUS_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"There are several modes of transport available, including road vehicles, "
"trams, trains, ships, airplanes, and helicopters. Each has its own depot, "
"where you can purchase new vehicles.\n"
"\n"
"Use the filter bar to filter vehicles for transporting a specific kind of "
"cargo or passengers. Select a vehicle from the list on the left to view its "
"details on the right, including its capacity, top speed, and power."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_BUS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Buy a Passenger Vehicle"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_BUS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy a vehicle for passenger transport in the store. Select the "
"[link=entity_depot]road depot[/link] and then select the manage vehicles "
"button."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_TRAIN_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Buy Train"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_TRAIN_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buying trains is more complex than buying road vehicles, as trains can be "
"composed to match specific requirements. Start by adding a locomotive, then "
"select wagons that suit the intended purpose.\n"
"\n"
"Pay attention to a few important details when creating a train. Electrified "
"tracks allow the use of electric locomotives. The train length should also "
"match the available station platforms, as trains that are too long will load "
"and unload significantly slower."

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_TRAIN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Buy Train"

msgid "TUTORIAL_BUY_TRAIN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Great! Now we can finally buy a train. Make sure that you add some wagons "
"with passenger capacity."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_1_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Roads"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_1_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Let's supply [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] with some planks! We start "
"to build up the supply chain by constructing roads between the "
"[link=entity_forest]forest[/link] and the [link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_2_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Roads"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_2_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Next, you need to construct roads between the [link=entity_saw]saw mill[/"
"link] and [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_DECISION_FISH_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ready to learn more?"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_DECISION_FISH_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Wonderful, the first passenger has boarded your train! If you're ready to "
"learn how to transport fish, let me know!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_DECISION_FISH_TRAIN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Fantastic!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_DECISION_FISH_TRAIN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Fantastic job! Your town should now start growing more quickly. There's "
"still more to learn, though. Ideally, every town should have sufficient "
"public transport, while its commercial and industrial districts should "
"receive a steady supply of cargo.\n"
"\n"
"When you're ready, choose what to learn next: how to establish a fish supply "
"line or how to set up a train line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_FISH_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Fish Supply"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_FISH_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Now, we can supply [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] with fish. For that, "
"create a line between the station next to the "
"[link=entity_warehouse]warehouse[/link] and the commercial district of "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]. Then, buy and assign a truck to the "
"line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Harbor and Ship Depot"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To transport the fish from the [link=entity_fishing]fishing grounds[/link] "
"to the commercial district of [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link], you need "
"to build up your water infrastructure. Let's start by building a harbor and "
"a ship depot."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_INDUSTRY_WINDOW_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Open Saw Mill Window"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_INDUSTRY_WINDOW_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Open the industry window of the [link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link] too see how "
"many planks are currently being produced."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_LINE_INDUSTRIAL_ASSIGN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Buy and Assign Trucks"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_LINE_INDUSTRIAL_ASSIGN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Buy at least one truck per line in the [link=entity_depot]road depot[/link]. "
"Make sure that the trucks can transport wood and planks and assign them to "
"the line from the [link=entity_forest]forest[/link] to the "
"[link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link] and another one to the line from the "
"[link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link] to the industrial district in "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_LINE_INDUSTRIAL_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Create Lines"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_LINE_INDUSTRIAL_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Now create a line from the station inside the [link=entity_forest]forest[/"
"link] to the station inside the [link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link] and another "
"one from the station inside the [link=entity_saw]saw mill[/link] to the "
"industrial district in [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SECOND_VEHICLE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "More Vehicles"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SECOND_VEHICLE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"We noticed that you have only a single vehicle on your line from the "
"[link=entity_warehouse]warehouse[/link] and the commercial district of "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]. To meet the demands of the town, you "
"should probably use multiple vehicles on each line. Start by adding a second "
"truck on this line!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SHIP_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ship Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SHIP_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Next, create a new line from the [link=entity_fishing]fishing grounds[/link] "
"to the [link=entity_harbor]harbor[/link] and send a suitable ship on the "
"line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SUPPLY_TOWN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Supply Town"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_SUPPLY_TOWN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Great job! Now we have to wait until the goods arrive in [link=entity_town]"
"{TOWN_NAME}[/link]. In the meantime you can optimize your routes or start "
"supplying different towns."

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_TRANSPORT_PLANKS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Transport Planks"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_TRANSPORT_PLANKS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Nice work! Now the planks should arrive in [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/"
"link] shortly. Let's wait until they arrive!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_TRUCK_STATION_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Cargo Stations"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_TRUCK_STATION_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To pick up fish from the warehouse, we need to build a cargo station next to "
"the [link=entity_warehouse]warehouse[/link].\n"
"Don't forget to connect it to a road!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_WAREHOUSE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Warehouse"

msgid "TUTORIAL_B_WAREHOUSE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Build a warehouse next to the [link=entity_harbor]harbor[/link] so that you "
"can start bringing your fish ashore. Make sure that the warehouse is in the "
"catchment area of the harbor."

msgid "TUTORIAL_CAMERA_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Camera Controls"

msgid "TUTORIAL_CAMERA_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Before we continue, we'll make sure that you're familar with the camera "
"controls. For that move, zoom, rotate, and tilt the camera."

msgid "TUTORIAL_COCKPIT_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Enter the Cockpit"

msgid "TUTORIAL_COCKPIT_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"You can also ride along with your train, if you want. Just select the "
"vehicle in the 3D world to open its window and then select the camera icon "
"to jump into the cockpit of the train."

msgid "TUTORIAL_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Building Roads"

msgid "TUTORIAL_CONNECT_INDUSTRY_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Road construction is a central part of building new infrastructure. Three "
"types of roads are available: town streets, country roads, and highways.\n"
"\n"
"Town streets allow towns to expand by enabling new buildings to be "
"constructed alongside them, but they have the lowest speed limit. Country "
"roads are the general-purpose choice for connecting towns and industries, "
"while highways are designed for long-distance travel, offering the highest "
"speed limits."

msgid "TUTORIAL_CONNECT_TRAIN_STATIONS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Connect Train Stations"

msgid "TUTORIAL_CONNECT_TRAIN_STATIONS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Next, establish bus lines to your train stations such that people from all "
"over town can reach the train stations. Make sure that your line in "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] connects to the train station, and "
"estabilish a new line in [link=entity_town_2]{TOWN_NAME_2}[/link] that leads "
"to the train station."

msgid "TUTORIAL_DECISION_TRAIN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Ready to learn more?"

msgid "TUTORIAL_DECISION_TRAIN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr "If you're ready to learn how to create a train line, let me know!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_END_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Congratulations!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_END_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Congratulations! You finished the onboarding and you're ready for the free "
"game. Have fun developing your own world!"

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_LINE_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Create Your First Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_LINE_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"The line manager is the central hub for managing all transport lines. The "
"window consists of three panels: the top panel lists all existing lines, the "
"middle panel shows the vehicles assigned to the selected line, and the "
"bottom panel displays the stops on that line in their current order.\n"
"\n"
"The line manager also provides tools for filtering and modifying lines and "
"vehicles. New lines can be created either by selecting the new line button "
"or by selecting a station in the 3D world."

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_LINE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Create Your First Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_LINE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Open the line manager and create a new line that connects your three "
"stations."

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_PASSENGER_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "First Passenger"

msgid "TUTORIAL_FIRST_PASSENGER_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Awesome! You established your first train connection! Now let's wait until "
"the first passenger boards the train."

msgid "TUTORIAL_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Water Infrastructure"

msgid "TUTORIAL_HARBOR_SHIPYARD_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Water transport infrastructure is simple to set up. Build a harbor and a "
"ship depot, and operations are ready to begin.\n"
"\n"
"Passenger and cargo ships are available in two sizes: small and large. Large "
"ships can only dock at large harbors, so make sure the harbor matches the "
"size of the ships assigned to the line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_LINE_STATISTICS_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Line Statistics"

msgid "TUTORIAL_LINE_STATISTICS_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"The line statistics provide an overview of which lines are profitable and "
"which are operating at a loss. They also display each line's rate, "
"indicating how many units of cargo or passengers are transported per year.\n"
"\n"
"For supply chains with multiple connected lines, keeping their rates "
"balanced is essential. If one line has a lower rate than the next, vehicles "
"may run empty with nothing to load, wasting money. If one line has a higher "
"rate than the next, cargo can accumulate and spoil before it is transported."

msgid "TUTORIAL_LINE_STATISTICS_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Open Statistics"

msgid "TUTORIAL_LINE_STATISTICS_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"While we wait for the first cargo to arrive, you can check out the "
"statistics window. Select the line statistics button to see an overview of "
"all your lines."

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOAN_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Take a Loan"

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOAN_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Loans can be taken from the bank, but they must be repaid with interest "
"within a certain period. Before taking out a first loan, it is important to "
"have a plan for generating income quickly to cover the repayments."

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOAN_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Take a Loan"

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOAN_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Before you can start building your infrastructure, you need some money. You "
"can take a loan from the bank."

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOCATE_VEHICLE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Locate Vehicle"

msgid "TUTORIAL_LOCATE_VEHICLE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To see your vehicles in action, open the vehicle window by selecting the "
"vehicle HUD icon, then select the locate button in the top toolbar. The "
"camera will automatically follow the selected vehicle."

msgid "TUTORIAL_SIMS_WINDOW_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Sims"

msgid "TUTORIAL_SIMS_WINDOW_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To see what your residents are doing, select one and open up their window. "
"You can see how happy they are, where they are living, working, and where "
"they like to go shopping."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_GUIDE_1_NAME"
msgstr "Town Supplies"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_GUIDE_1_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"This tab shows the number of passengers and the types of cargo required by "
"the town. It also displays whether the current supply level is good, medium, "
"or insufficient. Supply levels are the key factor determining town growth.\n"
"\n"
"Once passengers or cargo begin arriving, the town will start to grow... "
"until new challenges begin to emerge."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_GUIDE_2_NAME"
msgstr "Town Districts"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_GUIDE_2_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"This view shows the town's colored districts. Every town consists of three "
"district types: residential (green), commercial (blue), and industrial "
"(yellow).\n"
"\n"
"Commercial and industrial districts require cargo, while residents travel "
"from residential areas to industrial districts for work and to commercial "
"districts for shopping and leisure."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Open Town Supplies"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_SUPPLIES_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"To find out more details, select the supplies button in the town window."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Open Town Window"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TOWN_WINDOW_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Now let's get right into it! To see your towns grow, you first need to find "
"out what they require to do so.\n"
"For that, open up the town window of [link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link]."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRAIN_DEPOT_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Build Train Depot"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRAIN_DEPOT_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Before we can buy a train, we need to build a train depot and connect it to "
"your stations. Select the depot from the construction menu, place it close "
"to your tracks, and then connect it to the existing tracks."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRAIN_LINE_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Train Line"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRAIN_LINE_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Now we need to create a new train line that connects your two stations in "
"[link=entity_town]{TOWN_NAME}[/link] and [link=entity_town_2]{TOWN_NAME_2}[/"
"link] and send your train on the line."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRUCK_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Cargo Vehicles"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRUCK_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"When purchasing cargo vehicles, use the cargo filter to quickly find "
"vehicles suited for transporting a specific type of cargo. The details panel "
"on the right shows all cargo types that each vehicle can carry.\n"
"\n"
"When transporting only a single cargo type, specialized vehicles provide "
"faster loading and unloading than general-purpose vehicles."

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRUCK_STATION_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Cargo Specialization"

msgid "TUTORIAL_TRUCK_STATION_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Small road stops can only be used to unload cargo. To load cargo, a large "
"station is required.\n"
"\n"
"Vehicles and station platforms can be specialized for specific cargo "
"categories: flatbed, bulk, liquid, or goods. Specialization provides a "
"significant loading speed bonus, but reduces flexibility. Loading or "
"unloading the wrong cargo type at a specialized platform results in a severe "
"penalty."

msgid "TUTORIAL_WAREHOUSE_GUIDE_NAME"
msgstr "Build a Warehouse"

msgid "TUTORIAL_WAREHOUSE_GUIDE_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Warehouses are used to transfer cargo between different modes of transport "
"and to create more complex cargo networks. Build warehouses within a "
"station's catchment area and connect them with the appropriate lines. Cargo "
"will then be transferred and stored automatically."

msgid "TUTORIAL_WELCOME_TASK_NAME"
msgstr "Welcome"

msgid "TUTORIAL_WELCOME_TASK_PARAGRAPH"
msgstr ""
"Welcome to your brand new Tycoon map! \n"
"\n"
"Your goal is to bring this vast, open world to life by building a "
"transportation network that connects your towns. As your network grows, your "
"towns will flourish, and as they prosper, so will your business—unlocking "
"new opportunities and challenges along the way.\n"
"\n"
"You have complete freedom to shape the world according to your vision, so "
"let's jump right into it!"

msgid "Trucks Remaining"
msgstr "Trucks Remaining"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ABOAG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This German designed bus featured \"garden bench\" seating on the roof. It "
"offered excellent views of the city, but absolutely no protection from rain."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ABOAG_NAME"
msgstr "Daimler Deck Seat Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_AMERICAN_POST_COACH_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"An ordinary stagecoach used for public transport and mail delivery in the "
"early years. It was essential for travel before the engine era."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_AMERICAN_POST_COACH_NAME"
msgstr "Stagecoach"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_BK_670_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This high-capacity diesel bus was introduced to serve the busiest lines in "
"Beijing, helping the city manage its massive passenger load."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_BK_670_NAME"
msgstr "Beijing BK670"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_CARNIVAL_WAGGON_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr "Mardi Gras parade float."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_CARNIVAL_WAGGON_NAME"
msgstr "Mardi Gras Parade Float"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_CITROEN_CITYRAMA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Currus on a Citroën frame, this exotic sightseeing bus featured a "
"fully glazed double-deck cabin for panoramic views during city cruises."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_CITROEN_CITYRAMA_NAME"
msgstr "Citroën U55 Cityrama"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_D40_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by New Flyer Industries in the United States, it features fiberglass "
"sidewalls over hollow tubes and stainless steel wheel guards for safety."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_D40_NAME"
msgstr "New Flyer D40"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_DROSHKY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally a light coach for noble families, this four-wheeled horse "
"carriage later evolved to become the early predecessor of the modern taxi."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_DROSHKY_NAME"
msgstr "Droshky"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ECITARO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This bus offers a new level of comfort. With a whisper-quiet drive and "
"modern interior, it sets the standard for emission-free city travel."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ECITARO_NAME"
msgstr "Mercedes-Benz eCitaro"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ET13_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The ET 13 was a widely used engine-powered bus built in Austria. It marked a "
"significant shift toward motorized public transport in the region."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ET13_NAME"
msgstr "Postbus ET 13"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_FUSO_B46_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The name Fuso was proposed in an employee competition. It refers to the "
"ancient Chinese word Fusang, a tree of eternal life on a sacred island."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_FUSO_B46_NAME"
msgstr "Mitsubishi Fuso B46"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_GM_FISHBOWL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Nicknamed \"Fishbowl\" for its rounded six-piece windshield, over 44,000 "
"units of this iconic North American city bus were produced."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_GM_FISHBOWL_NAME"
msgstr "GM New Look Fishbowl"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_IRISBUS_CROSSWAY_LE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A versatile intercity bus used all across Europe, the Crossway LE serves "
"long-distance regional transport lines with great efficiency."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_IRISBUS_CROSSWAY_LE_NAME"
msgstr "Irisbus Crossway LE"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ISUZU_BU10P_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A robust and reliable Japanese bus that was used for both urban and "
"intercity routes due to its durability, often outfitted with different "
"bodies."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ISUZU_BU10P_NAME"
msgstr "Isuzu BU10P"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_KING_LONG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Inspired by calligraphy, this Chinese electric coach won a design award for "
"its aerodynamic form and an interior modeled after terraced fields."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_KING_LONG_NAME"
msgstr "King Long Merry Combo"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_LONDON_BUS_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The iconic Routemaster double-decker features an open rear platform. "
"Introduced in the fifties, it is a global symbol of London public transport."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_LONDON_BUS_NAME"
msgstr "AEC Routemaster"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_CITARO_G1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As one of the first modern low-floor articulated buses, the Citaro G1 "
"significantly enhanced passenger flow and accessibility in cities."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_CITARO_G1_NAME"
msgstr "Mercedes-Benz Citaro G1"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_O303_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Renowned for its durability and high passenger comfort, this German bus "
"served as a major benchmark for intercity and tourist coach travel."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_O303_NAME"
msgstr "Mercedes-Benz O303"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_O405G_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This bus was a popular articulated people mover that helped cities manage "
"growing passenger demand thanks to its spacious and efficient design."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_MB_O405G_NAME"
msgstr "Mercedes-Benz O405 G"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_OBEISSANTE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Frenchman Amédée Bollée, this steam bus could travel long "
"distances, famously completing the journey from Le Mans to Paris."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_OBEISSANTE_NAME"
msgstr "L'Obéissante"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_RAMPINI_2025_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built in Italy, this electric bus uses side-view cameras instead of mirrors "
"to fit through narrow streets. It offers a 300 km range for all-day service."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_RAMPINI_2025_NAME"
msgstr "Rampini Eltron"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SAURER_TUESCHER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A classic city bus built on the Saurer 2 BOD-P hood chassis, featuring "
"distinct bodywork by the renowned Swiss coachbuilder Tüscher."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SAURER_TUESCHER_NAME"
msgstr "Saurer Tüscher"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SCANIA_VABIS_H15_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A distinctive front-engined model, this bus played a major role in the "
"evolution of Sweden’s public transport during the mid-twentieth century."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SCANIA_VABIS_H15_NAME"
msgstr "Scania-Vabis H15"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SHINJIN_MICRO_BUS_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"South Korea's first successful bus was built from recycled oil drums and "
"reused parts from decommissioned American military jeeps and trucks."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_SHINJIN_MICRO_BUS_NAME"
msgstr "Shinjin Microbus"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_WRIGHT_STREETCAR_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Developed by Wrightbus and Volvo on a B7LA chassis, this articulated bus "
"features a separate driver's compartment and conditioning."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_WRIGHT_STREETCAR_NAME"
msgstr "Wright StreetCar"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_YELLOW_W_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A simple single-deck bus designed for city and short regional services by "
"the famous American company Yellow Truck and Coach Manufacturing Co."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_YELLOW_W_NAME"
msgstr "Yellow Coach Model W"

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ZUHAI_GTQ_6186BEVBT3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Manufactured in southern China, this futuristic articulated bus is powered "
"entirely by an electric drive system to reduce its carbon footprint."

msgid "VEHICLE_BUS_ZUHAI_GTQ_6186BEVBT3_NAME"
msgstr "Zuhai GTQ"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_AGUSTA_WESTLAND_AW101_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This versatile medium-lift helicopter, known for its exceptional performance "
"in civilian applications, was co-developed by Italy and Great Britain."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_AGUSTA_WESTLAND_AW101_NAME"
msgstr "AgustaWestland AW101 Merlin"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_AIRBUS_HELICOPTERS_H225_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This heavy-lift helicopter designed for long-range missions is an US and "
"European co-production. It is part of the Super Puma family of helicopters."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_AIRBUS_HELICOPTERS_H225_NAME"
msgstr "Airbus H225 Super Puma"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BELL_206_L_LONG_RANGER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Long Ranger is a light, single-engine helicopter that was an elongated "
"version of its predecessor, designed to accommodate additional seating."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BELL_206_L_LONG_RANGER_NAME"
msgstr "Bell 206 Long Ranger"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BELL_47_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Recognized for its distinctive bubble canopy, this American helicopter was "
"used in applications such as agricultural work and medical transport."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BELL_47_NAME"
msgstr "Bell 47"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BOEING_VERTOL_234_CHINOOK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Chinook is an iconic dual-rotor helicopter built in the United States "
"and often featured in movies. It is also widely used in Europe and Japan."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_BOEING_VERTOL_234_CHINOOK_NAME"
msgstr "Boeing Vertol 234 Chinook"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_EC120B_COLIBRI_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on a French design, the Colibri was developed by many nations around "
"the world. It is mainly used for rescue missions and surveillance."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_EC120B_COLIBRI_NAME"
msgstr "Eurocopter 120B Colibri"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_KAMAN_K_MAX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Thanks to its unique German engineered intermeshing rotor design, this "
"American helicopter is offering unmatched lifting power and maneuverability."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_KAMAN_K_MAX_NAME"
msgstr "Kaman K-MAX"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_LEONARDO_AW609_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A product of multinational engineering efforts, the \"Leonardo\" is one of "
"the first next-generation vertical take-off and landing (VTOL) aircrafts."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_LEONARDO_AW609_NAME"
msgstr "NextGen VTOL"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_MIL_MI26TC_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Developed in Soviet Russia, this the largest civilian helicopter in the "
"world. It is widely used in China, where it is called \"The Flying Dragon\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_MIL_MI26TC_NAME"
msgstr "Mil Mi-26TC"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_PIASECKI_H21_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Due to the neccessity to mount the rear rotor high enough to avoid "
"collisions in forward flight, its angled fuselage gave it the nickname \"The "
"Flying Banana\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_PIASECKI_H21_NAME"
msgstr "Piasecki H-21 Workhorse"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_SIKORSKY_S64_SKYCRANE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This heavy-lift helicopter known for its unique design was specifically "
"engineered to carry external loads especially useful in construction and "
"firefighting."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_SIKORSKY_S64_SKYCRANE_NAME"
msgstr "Sikorsky S-64 Skycrane"

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_SIKORSKY_S76_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally designed for passenger transport to oil rigs, this medium-sized "
"helicopter is used by the British Royal Family for official engagements."

msgid "VEHICLE_HELICOPTER_SIKORSKY_S76_NAME"
msgstr "Sikorsky S-76 Spirit"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_AVELIA_LIBERTY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on the most recent TGV-concepts, the Avelia Liberty is adapted for use "
"on the East corridor of the United States, still including tilting "
"technology."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_AVELIA_LIBERTY_NAME"
msgstr "Avelia Liberty"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_DB_VT_11_5_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a symbol of Europe's integration after World War II, the TEE was visiting "
"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_DB_VT_11_5_NAME"
msgstr "TEE VT 11.5"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_EMD_F_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by the Electro-Motive Divison of General Motors, these machines were "
"available as A-units and cabless B-units to form more powerful consists."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_EMD_F_NAME"
msgstr "EMD F-Unit"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_ES1_LASTOCHKA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Primarily purchased for use during the Winter Olympics in Sochi, these "
"modern electric railcars are now used to transport passengers on regional "
"lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_ES1_LASTOCHKA_NAME"
msgstr "ES1 Lastochka"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_FS_ETR_450_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Italy’s first high-speed tilting train featured an innovative system that "
"allowed for higher speeds on curved tracks, significantly reducing travel "
"times."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_FS_ETR_450_NAME"
msgstr "Italian Class ETR 450"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_FUXING_HAO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series ranks among the fastest operating in passenger service. During a "
"test, two trains safely passed each other at a relative speed of 840 km/h."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_FUXING_HAO_NAME"
msgstr "Fuxing Hao"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_HST_125_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by British Rail Engineering Limited for non-electrified main lines in "
"Great Britain, this train holds the world speed record for diesel trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_HST_125_NAME"
msgstr "Inter-City 125"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_ICE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Germany's first mass-produced high-speed train set a new speed record for "
"rail vehicles, reaching 406.9 km/h during test runs in 1988."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_ICE1_NAME"
msgstr "ICE 1"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_METROLINER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series of self-powered electric multiple-unit cars was used as extra-"
"fare express trains between Washington, D.C., and New York City."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_METROLINER_NAME"
msgstr "Metroliner"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_RE_450_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"These double-decker trains are used for commuter services on agglomeration "
"lines. The locomotives luggage compartment is rarely used though."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_RE_450_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss Re 450 DPZ"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_SHAOSHAN_4G_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A powerhouse built in China, this twin-unit electric locomotive used an "
"eight-axle design to haul cargo trains that stretched over two kilometers in "
"length."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_SHAOSHAN_4G_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class SS4G"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_SHINKANSEN_0S_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In contrast to previous Japanese trains, the first series of the iconic "
"Shinkansen train is constructed with the standard gauge to allow higher "
"speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_SHINKANSEN_0S_NAME"
msgstr "Shinkansen 0 Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_TGV_DUPLEX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_TGV_DUPLEX_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_TWINDEXX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Canadian manufacturer Bombardier, this double deck multiple unit is "
"used on Intercity main lines that require high capacity at high speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_MULTIPLEUNIT_TWINDEXX_NAME"
msgstr "RABe 502 Twindexx"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_AIRBUS_A310_300F_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This versatile cargo aircraft is offering significant payload capacity and "
"long-range capabilities, making it a popular choice for freight carriers "
"worldwide."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_AIRBUS_A310_300F_NAME"
msgstr "Airbus A310 300F Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_AIRBUS_A320_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As the best-selling airliner in history, it pioneered the transition to "
"digital cockpits and fly-by-wire technology, replacing manual cables with "
"electronic signals."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_AIRBUS_A320_NAME"
msgstr "Airbus A320"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BAE_146_CARGO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Characteristic features of this British airplane are its forward-angled "
"wings and the bulky fuselage with ample space, which earned it the nickname "
"\"Jumbolino\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BAE_146_CARGO_NAME"
msgstr "Br. Aerospace 146 Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BAE_146_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Characteristic features of this British airplane are its forward-angled "
"wings and the bulky fuselage with ample space, which earned it the nickname "
"\"Jumbolino\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BAE_146_NAME"
msgstr "Br. Aerospace 146"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOEING_737_700_CARGO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This model was the first version of the \"Next-Generation\" models by "
"Boeing. It is designed to be convertible between passenger and cargo in "
"under one hour."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOEING_737_700_CARGO_NAME"
msgstr "Boeing 737-700-C Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOEING_737_700_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This model was the first version of the \"Next-Generation\" models by "
"Boeing. Its 737 family of aircraft is on of the most widespread type of "
"plane in the world."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOEING_737_700_NAME"
msgstr "Boeing 737-700"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_CS300_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally developed and built by Bombardier, the program was taken over by "
"Airbus due to financial difficulties. The aircraft was later renamed to "
"\"Airbus A220\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_CS300_NAME"
msgstr "Airbus Canada A220"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_DHC_8_402PF_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The \"Dash 8\" is a successful series of the manufacturers De Havilland "
"Canada and Bombardier. This model is a conversion for the transport of cargo "
"on pallets."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_DHC_8_402PF_NAME"
msgstr "Bombardier DHC-8 Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_Q400_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a further development from the De Havilland Canada Dash 8, this aircraft "
"features improved flight characteristics along with active noise and "
"vibration insulation."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BOMBARDIER_Q400_NAME"
msgstr "Bombardier DHC-8"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BRISTOL_FREIGHTER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Nicknamed the \"Superwayfarer\", this British aircraft was used in the "
"fifties to simultaneously transport passengers and cars between islands and "
"the main land."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_BRISTOL_FREIGHTER_NAME"
msgstr "Bristol Type 170 Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CANADAIR_CL_44_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This commercial and cargo aircraft featured a hydraulically foldable rear "
"section of the fuselage that enabled the transport of oversized goods and "
"facilitated loading."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CANADAIR_CL_44_NAME"
msgstr "Canadair CL-44 Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CONCORDE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A British and French collaboration, this jet is known for its speed and "
"elegance. It is capable of flying from New York to London in under four "
"hours."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CONCORDE_NAME"
msgstr "Aérospatiale-BAC Concorde"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CONVAIR_CV_990_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Known for its distinctive \"fat\" fuselage this aircraft had supersonic "
"cruise capabilities. During its production run, however, it only found "
"limited commercial success."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CONVAIR_CV_990_NAME"
msgstr "Convair CV 990 Coronado"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CURTISS_C46_COMMANDO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built in the United States, this large twin-engine transport aircraft was "
"widely used in World War II. It was capable of carrying heavy loads over "
"long distances."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_CURTISS_C46_COMMANDO_NAME"
msgstr "Curtiss C-46 Commando"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DE_HAVILLAND_COMET_4B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally developed as 4A for Capital Airlines, the 4B was an improved "
"design with higher capacity, thanks to a longer fuselage, and a smaller "
"wingspan."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DE_HAVILLAND_COMET_4B_NAME"
msgstr "De Havilland DH.106 Comet"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC10_30_CF_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This plane is fitted with a three-engine setup that was novel at its time. "
"It was the first aircraft model produced after the merger between McDonnell "
"and Douglas."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC10_30_CF_NAME"
msgstr "McDonnell Douglas DC-10-30CF"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC10_30_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This plane is fitted with a three-engine setup that was novel at its time. "
"It was the first aircraft model produced after the merger between McDonnell "
"and Douglas."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC10_30_NAME"
msgstr "McDonnell Douglas DC-10-30"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed in the United States, this propeller-driven aircraft boasted "
"extraordinary speed and range, and revolutionized air travel in the nineteen "
"thirties and fourties."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC3_NAME"
msgstr "Douglas DC-3"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This four-engine American aircraft with piston-engine propulsion has its "
"origins in military applications but was later widely used in civil aviation "
"as well."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_DOUGLAS_DC4_NAME"
msgstr "Douglas DC-4"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_FOKKER_100_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This jet is known for its quiet operation and efficiency, commonly used for "
"short to medium-haul flights and beloved for its spacious and comfortable "
"cabin."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_FOKKER_100_NAME"
msgstr "Fokker 100"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_FOKKER_F_VII_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In the nineteen twenties, Dutch engineers designed this long-range passenger "
"plane to create an air bridge from the Netherlands to the Dutch East Indies."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_FOKKER_F_VII_A_NAME"
msgstr "Fokker F VII A"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_HERCULES_L100_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As the civilian version of Lockheed's C-130E military transport aircraft, "
"the Hercules is equipped with military grade navigation and communication "
"equipment."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_HERCULES_L100_NAME"
msgstr "Lockheed L-100 Hercules"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_JUNKERS_F_13_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed and developed in Germany, this airplane was the first all-metal "
"aircraft used for civilian applications and featured padded seats and "
"heating."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_JUNKERS_F_13_NAME"
msgstr "Junkers F 13 Herta"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_JUNKERS_JU_52_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This German Aircraft, nicknamed \"Iron Annie\", was designed as a low-"
"maintenance aircraft made to carry large cargo volumes in areas with poor "
"infrastructure."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_JUNKERS_JU_52_NAME"
msgstr "Junkers JU-52 Iron Annie"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SHORT_330_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed as short-haul aircraft with a cabin for mixed passenger-freight "
"operations, this British plane uniquely has all its fuel stored in the "
"ceiling."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SHORT_330_NAME"
msgstr "Short 330 Sherpa"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUKHOI_SUPERJET_100_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This Eastern European regional airliner is built with a specific low-wing "
"design. It was designed this way so that it could also be sold on the "
"Western market."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUKHOI_SUPERJET_100_NAME"
msgstr "Sukhoi Superjet 100"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUPER_CONNIE_CARGO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This variation of the first generation \"Super Connie\" was equipped with a "
"large cargo door as well as a heavy-duty floor to enable transport of goods."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUPER_CONNIE_CARGO_NAME"
msgstr "Lockheed L-1049D/H Super Connie"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUPER_CONNIE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Generally referred to as the \"Super Connie\", this four-engine commercial "
"aircraft from America was the most successful version of the Constellation "
"series."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_SUPER_CONNIE_NAME"
msgstr "Lockheed L-1049 Super Connie"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_TUPOLEV_TU_204_CARGO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A medium-range aircraft, it was among the first Russian designs of its "
"generation to feature new technologies such as fly-by-wire, supercritical "
"wings, and winglets."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_TUPOLEV_TU_204_CARGO_NAME"
msgstr "Tupolev Tu-204C Freighter"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_TUPOLEV_TU_204_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A medium-range aircraft, it was among the first Russian designs of its "
"generation to feature new technologies such as fly-by-wire, supercritical "
"wings, and winglets."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_TUPOLEV_TU_204_NAME"
msgstr "Tupolev Tu-204"

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_VICKERS_VICTORIA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Notable for its reliability in both commercial and mail transport, it lay "
"the groundwork for modern aviation. Only around 100 units of this plane were "
"built."

msgid "VEHICLE_PLANE_VICKERS_VICTORIA_NAME"
msgstr "Vickers J6860 Victoria"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_BALTICA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Due to its compactness, this trawler is mostly used for generic cargo "
"transportation of small quantities over short distances near the shore."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_BALTICA_NAME"
msgstr "Baltica"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_BRITISH_COLUMBIA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With its compact size and low costs, this agile trawler is perfect for "
"transporting small quantities of a variety of cargo types over short "
"distances."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_BRITISH_COLUMBIA_NAME"
msgstr "Canadian Trawler"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_CAP_ARKONA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Offering scenic tours and transport, this passenger ferry provides a "
"comfortable way to explore the North Sea’s stunning coastline and islands."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_CAP_ARKONA_NAME"
msgstr "Cap Arkona"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DAMEN_FERRY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With its robust aluminum hull, this ferry can withstand even rough seas. "
"Four powerful MTU engines provide high-speed performance for this catamaran."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DAMEN_FERRY_NAME"
msgstr "Damen Fast Ferry"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DAMEN_TANKER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Dutch shipbuilder Damen, this modern and compact tanker is designed "
"for the efficient transport of liquid cargo such as oil or chemicals."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DAMEN_TANKER_NAME"
msgstr "Damen Tanker 800"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DUNARA_CASTLE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Named after a castle, this ship was the first to offer regular passenger and "
"cargo services between the islands of Scotland, thereby enabling tourism."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_DUNARA_CASTLE_NAME"
msgstr "Dunara Castle"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HADAG_TYPE_2000_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Hamburg relies on this series of passenger ferries, known for their "
"reliability, to provide fast connections between the city's waterfront "
"promenades."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HADAG_TYPE_2000_NAME"
msgstr "HADAG Type 2000"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HERKULES_XI_UNIVERSAL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Operating on the Danube and Rhine rivers, this sturdy cargo towboat was "
"specially designed to push flat-bottomed barges through shallow inland "
"waters."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HERKULES_XI_UNIVERSAL_NAME"
msgstr "Hercules XI Towboat"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HONG_KONG_FERRY_BOAT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The color scheme and double-deck design characterize this passenger ferry. "
"Several of these ships are used in Hong Kong for passenger ferry services."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HONG_KONG_FERRY_BOAT_NAME"
msgstr "Meridian Ferry"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HOVERCRAFT_AP1_88_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With its unique ability to glide over surfaces and its four diesel engines, "
"it offers a smooth and fast ride even in shallow waters and coastal areas."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_HOVERCRAFT_AP1_88_NAME"
msgstr "AP1-88 Hovercraft"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_KAKADUA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This small, low-cost trawler is used to carry various cargo in small amounts "
"over short distances, mainly along the coast and in nearshore waters."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_KAKADUA_NAME"
msgstr "Borealis"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_LUISE_DEYMANN_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This German tanker is designed for transporting liquid cargo. Like all ships "
"owned by this family business, it is named after a member of the family."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_LUISE_DEYMANN_NAME"
msgstr "Luise Deymann"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_MS_DIAMANT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Renowned for its elegant design and amenities, this ship allows passengers "
"to enjoy breathtaking views of the surroundings during their journey."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_MS_DIAMANT_NAME"
msgstr "MS Diamant"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_MS_STADT_KIEL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Compared to larger ones, this small passenger ship has much more charm and "
"allows for a more relaxed journey on beautiful routes between destinations."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_MS_STADT_KIEL_NAME"
msgstr "MS Stadt Kiel"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_OITA_HOVERCRAFT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Offering faster transit than road vehicles, this hovercraft was introduced "
"in 2025 to improve the connection between Oita City and its airport."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_OITA_HOVERCRAFT_NAME"
msgstr "GHL Oita Hovercraft"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_PS_TRILLIUM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Used for passenger and cargo transport on the Great Lakes, this ship is an "
"example of steam-powered vessels at the beginning of the twentieth century."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_PS_TRILLIUM_NAME"
msgstr "PS Trillium"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_SOLAR_SHUTTLE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Powered by solar energy, this small passenger ferry enables quiet transport "
"over short distances, while reducing emissions and protecting the "
"environment."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_SOLAR_SHUTTLE_NAME"
msgstr "Solar Shuttle"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_STERNWHEELER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Powered by a steam engine driving a wheel at the rear, this type of boat was "
"used for cargo and passenger transport on rivers like the Mississippi."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_STERNWHEELER_NAME"
msgstr "Sternwheeler"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_SYDFART_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This Swedish cargo ship has been in continuous service for over a century, "
"making it the oldest motorized cargo ship that is still in operation today."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_SYDFART_NAME"
msgstr "Sydfart"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TERRA_NOVA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Famous for its long service life, this historic Dutch cargo ship was dubbed "
"the “Luxe Motor” because of its luxurious captain's cabin and engine."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TERRA_NOVA_NAME"
msgstr "Terra Nova"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TORA_TYP_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Often found in the North and Baltic Seas, this class of small, versatile "
"coaster ships was built for regional cargo transport on short sea routes."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TORA_TYP_NAME"
msgstr "Tora Coaster Ship"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TS_QUEEN_MARY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Launched in the thirties, this historic British passenger ship was powered "
"by three steam turbines. It's currently being restored as a museum ship."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_TS_QUEEN_MARY_NAME"
msgstr "TS Queen Mary"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VIRGO_UNIVERSAL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed specifically for pushing river barges, this towboat belongs to a "
"seven-ship fleet whose members are all named after the signs of the zodiac."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VIRGO_UNIVERSAL_NAME"
msgstr "Virgo Towboat"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VOTRANS_TANKER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The quarterdeck for storing a car makes this German towboat unique. It is "
"designed for pushing barges, making it ideal for transport on rivers."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VOTRANS_TANKER_NAME"
msgstr "Votrans Towboat Tanker"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VOTRANS_UNIVERSAL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The quarterdeck for storing a car makes this German towboat unique. It is "
"designed for pushing barges, making it ideal for transport on rivers."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_VOTRANS_UNIVERSAL_NAME"
msgstr "Votrans Towboat Cargo"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_WAIMARIE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Formerly known for transporting cargo and passengers on the Whanganui River "
"in New Zealand, a restored version of this ship is still in use today."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_WAIMARIE_NAME"
msgstr "Waimarie"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_WOPPER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This classic Dutch coaster ship is known for its robustness and versatility. "
"It remains a reliable workhorse for navigating short-sea routes."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_WOPPER_NAME"
msgstr "Wopper"

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_YARA_BIRKELAND_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This electric container ship was developed for short sea shipping with low "
"emissions. It is planned to be the world's first unmanned surface vessel."

msgid "VEHICLE_SHIP_YARA_BIRKELAND_NAME"
msgstr "Yara Birkeland"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ALCO_HH600_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by the American Locomotive Company (ALCO) in Schenectady, New York, "
"this series was one of the earliest diesel-electric locomotives."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ALCO_HH600_NAME"
msgstr "ALCO HH 600"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ATLANTIC_4_4_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The Atlantic class, also known as \"Milwaukee\", with four leading wheels "
"and just two trailing wheels, was used for pulling trains across long "
"distances."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ATLANTIC_4_4_2_NAME"
msgstr "4-4-2 Atlantic"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on the most recent TGV-concepts, the Avelia Liberty is adapted for use "
"on the East corridor of the United States, still including tilting "
"technology."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Avelia Liberty"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on the most recent TGV-concepts, the Avelia Liberty is adapted for use "
"on the East corridor of the United States, still including tilting "
"technology."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "Avelia Liberty"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on the most recent TGV-concepts, the Avelia Liberty is adapted for use "
"on the East corridor of the United States, still including tilting "
"technology."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "Avelia Liberty"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on the most recent TGV-concepts, the Avelia Liberty is adapted for use "
"on the East corridor of the United States, still including tilting "
"technology."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_AVELIA_LIBERTY_MIDDLE3_NAME"
msgstr "Avelia Liberty"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BIGBOY_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This articulated locomotive was a real monster and used the latest steam "
"locomotive technology. It was primarily used for towing freight trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BIGBOY_NAME"
msgstr "ALCO 4-8-8-4 Big Boy"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR75_4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Specifically designed to haul passenger wagons on sloped rail lines, this "
"small but powerful tank locomotive was initially used in south-western "
"Germany."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR75_4_NAME"
msgstr "Baden Class VI c"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR89_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The small Prussian T 3 locomotive is well known today, as it is a common "
"starter both for many museum railways and scale model railway enthusiasts."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR89_NAME"
msgstr "Prussian Class T 3"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_185_TRAXX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The two-system capable electric series was developed for \"Transnational "
"Railway Applications with extreme flexibility\", or in short \"TRAXX\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_185_TRAXX_NAME"
msgstr "German Class 185"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_246_TRAXX_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"For use on non-electrified lines, the diesel variant of the \"TRAXX\" family "
"features diesel tanks instead of the transformers found in the electric "
"version."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_246_TRAXX_NAME"
msgstr "German Class 246"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_E94_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Although its muzzles are shorter than the ones from its Swiss pendant, this "
"heavy electric locomotive still earned the nickname \"German Crocodile\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_BR_E94_NAME"
msgstr "German Class E 94"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_C6_8_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mostly used for cargo trains on winding lines such as the Gotthard Railway, "
"it got its nickname \"Crocodile\" thanks to its long muzzles and the green "
"color."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_C6_8_NAME"
msgstr "Ce 6/8 II Crocodile"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_DF4B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"To boost the change from steam to diesel, over 5000 locomotives of the "
"\"Dangfeng\" series were produced by various Chinese manufacturies."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_DF4B_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class DF4B"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_DF5_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed as a road switcher locomotive, the DF5 is China's most common "
"series used both for hauling freight as well as shunting in local areas."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_DF5_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class DF5"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_HXD3B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Derived from European locomotives for heavy iron ore trains, this model has "
"a particularly high power output to handle very long cargo trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_HXD3B_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class HXD3B"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_JF1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This locomotive was originally introduced to cope with the increasing "
"freight traffic during the First World War on the South Manchuria railway."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_JF1_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class JF1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_RM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The successor of the SL6 Pacific locomotive was China's last steam passenger "
"design before being replaced by diesel locomotives in the late eighties."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CHINA_RM_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class RM"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CLASS_PRR_GG1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With its iconic streamlined design, it not only had a great design, it was "
"also capable of high speeds and remained in service for many years."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_CLASS_PRR_GG1_NAME"
msgstr "Pennsylvanian Class GG1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_V100_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"To replace the steamers used for passenger and freight service on non-"
"electrified branch lines in Germany, this diesel-hydraulic series was "
"developed."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_V100_NAME"
msgstr "German Class V 100"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a symbol of Europe's integration after World War II, the TEE was visiting "
"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "TEE VT 11.5"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a symbol of Europe's integration after World War II, the TEE was visiting "
"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE1_NAME"
