"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "TEE VT 11.5"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a symbol of Europe's integration after World War II, the TEE was visiting "
"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE3_NAME"
msgstr "TEE VT 11.5"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a symbol of Europe's integration after World War II, the TEE was visiting "
"at its peak over 130 different cities across the entire continent."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_DB_VT_11_5_MIDDLE4_NAME"
msgstr "TEE VT 11.5"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EL_18_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Specifically adapted for operation on the scenic but harsh railway lines of "
"Scandinavia, this series is an adaption of the Swiss Re 460 locomotives."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EL_18_NAME"
msgstr "Norwegian Class El 18"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_AEM_7_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Novel technology, known as thyristor control, was implemented for the "
"traction motors, ensuring that maximum power was available without wheel "
"slip."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_AEM_7_NAME"
msgstr "EMD AEM-7"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_FA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by the Electro-Motive Divison of General Motors, these machines were "
"available as A-units and cabless B-units to form more powerful consists."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_FA_NAME"
msgstr "EMD F A-Unit"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_FB_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by the Electro-Motive Divison of General Motors, these machines were "
"available as A-units and cabless B-units to form more powerful consists."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_FB_NAME"
msgstr "EMD F B-Unit"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_SD40_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The heavy \"Special Duty\" locomotive of the Dash 2 portfolio by EMD is one "
"of the most built diesel engines in American railroad history."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EMD_SD40_NAME"
msgstr "EMD SD40-2"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Primarily purchased for use during the Winter Olympics in Sochi, these "
"modern electric railcars are now used to transport passengers on regional "
"lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "ES1 Lastochka"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Primarily purchased for use during the Winter Olympics in Sochi, these "
"modern electric railcars are now used to transport passengers on regional "
"lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "ES1 Lastochka"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Primarily purchased for use during the Winter Olympics in Sochi, these "
"modern electric railcars are now used to transport passengers on regional "
"lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ES1_LASTOCHKA_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "ES1 Lastochka"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Italy’s first high-speed tilting train featured an innovative system that "
"allowed for higher speeds on curved tracks, significantly reducing travel "
"times."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Italian Class ETR 450"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Italy’s first high-speed tilting train featured an innovative system that "
"allowed for higher speeds on curved tracks, significantly reducing travel "
"times."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "Italian Class ETR 450"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Italy’s first high-speed tilting train featured an innovative system that "
"allowed for higher speeds on curved tracks, significantly reducing travel "
"times."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ETR_450_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "Italian Class ETR 450"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EURODUAL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"To pull freight trains on electrified main routes as well as non-electrified "
"branch lines, this series has equipment for diesel and electric traction on "
"board."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_EURODUAL_NAME"
msgstr "Stadler Eurodual"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series ranks among the fastest operating in passenger service. During a "
"test, two trains safely passed each other at a relative speed of 840 km/h."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Fuxing Hao"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series ranks among the fastest operating in passenger service. During a "
"test, two trains safely passed each other at a relative speed of 840 km/h."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "Fuxing Hao"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series ranks among the fastest operating in passenger service. During a "
"test, two trains safely passed each other at a relative speed of 840 km/h."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_FUXING_HAO_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "Fuxing Hao"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_GE_P42_DC_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The GE Genesis series is rather lightweight in comparison to other current "
"North American locomotives, due to its full shell construction."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_GE_P42_DC_NAME"
msgstr "GE P42DC"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HANDCAR_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A handcar is part railway history, part teamwork, and just enough exercise "
"to earn the ride. It is powered entirely by pure human strength."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HANDCAR_NAME"
msgstr "Handcar"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by British Rail Engineering Limited for non-electrified main lines in "
"Great Britain, this train holds the world speed record for diesel trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Inter-City 125"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by British Rail Engineering Limited for non-electrified main lines in "
"Great Britain, this train holds the world speed record for diesel trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "British Mark 3 Coach"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by British Rail Engineering Limited for non-electrified main lines in "
"Great Britain, this train holds the world speed record for diesel trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_HST_125_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "British Mark 3 Coach"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Germany's first mass-produced high-speed train set a new speed record for "
"rail vehicles, reaching 406.9 km/h during test runs in 1988."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "ICE 1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Germany's first mass-produced high-speed train set a new speed record for "
"rail vehicles, reaching 406.9 km/h during test runs in 1988."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "ICE 1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Germany's first mass-produced high-speed train set a new speed record for "
"rail vehicles, reaching 406.9 km/h during test runs in 1988."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ICE1_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "ICE 1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_JR_EF66_100_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The JR Class EF66-100 was a powerful Japanese electric locomotive designed "
"for fast freight transport, and later also used for heavy passenger trains."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_JR_EF66_100_NAME"
msgstr "Japanese Class EF66"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_LNER_CLASS_A4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"London and North Eastern Railway's express steam locomotive set the world "
"speed record for steam locomotives in 1938, which it still holds today."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_LNER_CLASS_A4_NAME"
msgstr "British Class A4"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_METROLINER_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series of self-powered electric multiple-unit cars was used as extra-"
"fare express trains between Washington, D.C., and New York City."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_METROLINER_NAME"
msgstr "Metroliner"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_MOGUL_2_6_0_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Rumors say, this early cargo locomotive with 3 axles for traction earned the "
"name \"Mogul\" due to the comparison of its power with the Mughal Empire."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_MOGUL_2_6_0_NAME"
msgstr "2-6-0 Mogul"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_M_300_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by American Car & Foundry, this railcar earned its nickname “Skunk” "
"because people often said, “You can smell it before you can see it.”"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_M_300_NAME"
msgstr "ACF M-300"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_OBB_1042_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"For winding lines like the Semmering route, the Austrian Federal Railways "
"ordered a series of electric locomotives for passenger and cargo service."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_OBB_1042_NAME"
msgstr "Austrian Class 1042"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_44I_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As a lightweight electric locomotive, it was used both for regional "
"transport and for hauling high-quality long-distance trains to neighboring "
"countries."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_44I_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss Re 4/4 I"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_BACK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This double deck coach with seats in a vis-a-vis arrangement offers high "
"capacity for crowded passenger services on agglomeration lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_BACK_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss DPZ Cab Coach"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"These double-decker trains are used for commuter services on agglomeration "
"lines. The locomotives luggage compartment is rarely used though."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss Re 450 DPZ"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This double deck coach with seats in a vis-a-vis arrangement offers high "
"capacity for crowded passenger services on agglomeration lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RE_450_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss DPZ Coach"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ROTERPFEIL_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally intended for fast local trains with low demands, this series "
"became a victim of its own success and was moved to more exclusive rail "
"services."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_ROTERPFEIL_NAME"
msgstr "CLe 2/4 Roter Pfeil"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RUSSIAN_CLASS_OB_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"With over 9000 built units, the so-called \"Osnovnoi\" cargo steam "
"locomotive became one of the most-built series in both Russia and the world."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RUSSIAN_CLASS_OB_NAME"
msgstr "Russian Class OB"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RUSSIAN_CLASS_SU_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This new design, which could be operated with inferior coal after World War "
"I, was so successful that it ended up being used for decades."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_RUSSIAN_CLASS_SU_NAME"
msgstr "Russian Class SU"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SCHIENENBUS_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This series got introduced to provide efficient passenger services on "
"unprofitable secondary lines. This lead to its nickname \"The savior of "
"branch lines\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SCHIENENBUS_NAME"
msgstr "Uerdingen Railbus"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHAOSHAN_4G_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"A powerhouse built in China, this twin-unit electric locomotive used an "
"eight-axle design to haul cargo trains that stretched over two kilometers in "
"length."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHAOSHAN_4G_NAME"
msgstr "Chinese Class SS4G"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_BACK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In contrast to previous Japanese trains, the first series of the iconic "
"Shinkansen train is constructed with the standard gauge to allow higher "
"speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_BACK_NAME"
msgstr "Shinkansen 0 Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In contrast to previous Japanese trains, the first series of the iconic "
"Shinkansen train is constructed with the standard gauge to allow higher "
"speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "Shinkansen 0 Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In contrast to previous Japanese trains, the first series of the iconic "
"Shinkansen train is constructed with the standard gauge to allow higher "
"speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "Shinkansen 0 Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In contrast to previous Japanese trains, the first series of the iconic "
"Shinkansen train is constructed with the standard gauge to allow higher "
"speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_SHINKANSEN_0S_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "Shinkansen 0 Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TALENT1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As one of the late nineties products, this series had a modular design to "
"support the needs of different train companies in whole Europe and beyond."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TALENT1_NAME"
msgstr "Talbot Talent 1"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE2_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE3_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE4_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE4_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE5_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The double-decker version of the famous French high-speed train offers even "
"higher passenger capacity at almost the same travel speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TGV_MIDDLE5_NAME"
msgstr "TGV Duplex"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TWINDEXX_FRONT_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Canadian manufacturer Bombardier, this double deck multiple unit is "
"used on Intercity main lines that require high capacity at high speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TWINDEXX_FRONT_NAME"
msgstr "RABe 502 Twindexx"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TWINDEXX_MIDDLE1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built by Canadian manufacturer Bombardier, this double deck multiple unit is "
"used on Intercity main lines that require high capacity at high speeds."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAIN_TWINDEXX_MIDDLE1_NAME"
msgstr "RABe 502 Twindexx"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_ATM_4000_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Although it featured the same suspended center box mounted between the ends, "
"it was cheaper to run than its predecessor, the ATM 3000."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_ATM_4000_NAME"
msgstr "Milano Series 4000"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BE4_6MIRAGE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As with the procurement of the Mirage fighter planes, there was a large cost "
"overrun for this tram project, earning it its nickname."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BE4_6MIRAGE_NAME"
msgstr "Zurich Be 4/6 Mirage"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOMBARDIER_K4000_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Thanks to its step-free access, the introduction of the first Flexity Swift "
"series improved accessibility for light rail passengers significantly."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOMBARDIER_K4000_NAME"
msgstr "Bombardier K4000"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Early cargo tram wagons were small enough to feature a fixed two-axle design "
"and were usually adapted to individual types of cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_A_NAME"
msgstr "Box Car 1896"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mid-century cargo tram wagons were often built for a specific purpose, but "
"featured bogies to allow for greater length and better maneuverability."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_B_NAME"
msgstr "Box Car 1950"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_C_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Modern cargo tram wagons are modular in design, with a shared base platform "
"for all models and superstructures tailored to specific cargo types."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BOX_CAR_C_NAME"
msgstr "Box Car 2005"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Early cargo tram wagons were small enough to feature a fixed two-axle design "
"and were usually adapted to individual types of cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_A_NAME"
msgstr "Gondola Car 1898"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mid-century cargo tram wagons were often built for a specific purpose, but "
"featured bogies to allow for greater length and better maneuverability."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_B_NAME"
msgstr "Gondola Car 1950"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_C_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Modern cargo tram wagons are modular in design, with a shared base platform "
"for all models and superstructures tailored to specific cargo types."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_BULK_CAR_C_NAME"
msgstr "Gondola Car 2005"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CAF_URBOS3_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Colorful interiors are a unique feature of this tram used in Luxembourg, "
"which is part of the third generation of CAF's Urbos platform."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CAF_URBOS3_NAME"
msgstr "CAF Urbos 3"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CAR_GO_TRAM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Built from parts of older trams, the CarGoTram was developed to transport "
"machine parts to a Volkswagen factory in the center of Dresden."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CAR_GO_TRAM_NAME"
msgstr "Dresden CarGoTram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CHANGCHUN3000_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The light rail vehicles in the city of Changchun are among the longest "
"single vehicles on the market, providing high capacity for crowded lines."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CHANGCHUN3000_NAME"
msgstr "Changchun 3000"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CLOSED_PAX_WAGON_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Closed cars offered more comfort during the cold season. On the other hand, "
"this increased the weight of the cars and made them more expensive."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_CLOSED_PAX_WAGON_NAME"
msgstr "Closed Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DAMPFTRAM_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The boxed shape of the steam locomotive stands out but had some advantages. "
"It allowed the driver to stand near the front and observe the tracks."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DAMPFTRAM_NAME"
msgstr "Steam Tram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_DECK_WAGON_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In order to increase capacity without increasing length, a second level was "
"added. However, it was not very comfortable, especially in the rain."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_DECK_WAGON_NAME"
msgstr "Double Deck Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_HORSE_CARGO_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Rolling resistance on tracks is significantly lower than on rough "
"cobblestones, which is a important factor for the efficient transport of "
"cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_HORSE_CARGO_NAME"
msgstr "Horse Tram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_HORSE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"In times of bumpy cobblestone streets, the first horse-drawn passenger tram "
"offered a somewhat smoother and quieter ride on rails."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DOUBLE_HORSE_NAME"
msgstr "Horse Tram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_BW_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Matching the rail car of the same name, this series offers a lot of capacity "
"in a single spacious car and many doors for quick passenger exchange."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_BW_NAME"
msgstr "DUEWAG Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_N8C_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Fulfilling the needs of various German light rail systems, this series was "
"built in high numbers. Many of them got a second life in Eastern Europe."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_N8C_NAME"
msgstr "DUEWAG Typ N8C"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_TW_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"It received its name from the spacious interior and a modern design for its "
"time to accommodate high passenger volumes and was widely used."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_DUEWAG_TW_NAME"
msgstr "DUEWAG Motor Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_FREIGHTCAR_24S_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Being used to carry cargo between depots, workshops and other yards in "
"Sydney, this tram car was built from wood on a metal frame."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_FREIGHTCAR_24S_NAME"
msgstr "Sydney 24s Motor Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_F_TRAM_UNIV_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed for urban freight service, this cargo tram combines a reinforced "
"frame and modular cargo compartments with a modern design."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_F_TRAM_UNIV_NAME"
msgstr "Articulated Cargo Tram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_GE_25_TON_SW_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"This American series of 25-ton switchers was built for light switching "
"duties, often used in factories, ports, and small rail yards."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_GE_25_TON_SW_NAME"
msgstr "GE 25-ton Switcher"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_HALLE_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As one of the first electric streetcars with an open platform on both sides, "
"it was used by the \"Allgemeine Elektrizitaets-Gesellschaft Stadtbahn "
"Halle\"."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_HALLE_NAME"
msgstr "AEG Motor Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_HONGKONG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As an iconic part of the public transport system, the double deck tram used "
"in Hong Kong is equally popular among tourists and residents."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_HONGKONG_NAME"
msgstr "Hong Kong Tram"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_LVS_86_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"When the tram network of St. Petersburg needed larger trams, this series was "
"developed and received various technical upgrades and modernizations."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_LVS_86_NAME"
msgstr "St.Petersburg LVS-86"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_MOSCOW_F_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Literally called a \"Lantern\" due to their roof, more than 600 of these "
"streetcars circulated in the city of Moscow for over 50 years."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_MOSCOW_F_NAME"
msgstr "Nuremberg F Motor Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_MOSCOW_NUREMBERG_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Derived from a series of tram cars from the German town of Nuremberg, this "
"unmotorized car was used on the streets of Moscow."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_MOSCOW_NUREMBERG_NAME"
msgstr "Nuremberg F Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_ODESSA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Odessa's first open streetcar series launched through the support of a "
"Belgian company, marking a milestone in the town's transit."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_ODESSA_NAME"
msgstr "Open Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_PCC_1643_PITTSBURGH_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"The PCC \"Presidents' Conference Committee\" streetcar design, as seen in "
"Pittsburgh, proved to be very successful not only in North America."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_PCC_1643_PITTSBURGH_NAME"
msgstr "Pittsburgh PCC 1643"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SCHOEMA_GM_2_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Designed for industrial and light shunting tasks, this small diesel "
"locomotive built by Schoema in Germany is widely used in private sidings."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SCHOEMA_GM_2_2_NAME"
msgstr "Schöma Tm 2/2"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SERIES_X_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Based on a similar passenger tram series, the soviet X or Kh-series was a "
"very sturdy type that could transport cargo on local tram networks."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SERIES_X_NAME"
msgstr "Russian X-Series"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SIG_GE_2_2_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Originally used in cargo trams around the local steel mill, this small "
"electric locomotive is preserved near the office of Urban Games."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SIG_GE_2_2_NAME"
msgstr "Swiss Ge 2/2"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SKODA_10T_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"As part of the renaissance of trams in the United States, Skoda adapted one "
"of its European tram types for the American market."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_SKODA_10T_NAME"
msgstr "Skoda 10 T"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STADLER_CITYLINK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"One of the most recent representatives of tram-trains, featuring both an "
"electric and diesel motor to extend tram lines into the outer suburbs."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STADLER_CITYLINK_NAME"
msgstr "Stadler Citylink"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STADLER_TINA_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Standing for \"Totally Integrated Low-floor Drive\", Stadler's newest "
"generation of trams features modular options for length and door "
"arrangements."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STADLER_TINA_NAME"
msgstr "Stadler TINA"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Early cargo tram wagons were small enough to feature a fixed two-axle design "
"and were usually adapted to individual types of cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_A_NAME"
msgstr "Stake Car 1897"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mid-century cargo tram wagons were often built for a specific purpose, but "
"featured bogies to allow for greater length and better maneuverability."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_B_NAME"
msgstr "Stake Car 1950"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_C_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Modern cargo tram wagons are modular in design, with a shared base platform "
"for all models and superstructures tailored to specific cargo types."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_STAKE_CAR_C_NAME"
msgstr "Stake Car 2005"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TANK_CAR_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Early cargo tram wagons were small enough to feature a fixed two-axle design "
"and were usually adapted to individual types of cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TANK_CAR_A_NAME"
msgstr "Tank Car 1899"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TANK_CAR_B_DESCRIPTION"
