msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TATRA_T4_TANK_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Some Eastern European cities converted passenger trams to service vehicles "
"to transport cargo and other materials within their own network."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TATRA_T4_TANK_NAME"
msgstr "Tatra T4 Tank"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TORONTO_CLRV_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Acting as a successful replacement for the aging PCCs, the Canadian Light "
"Rail Vehicle was developed as a modern, standardized streetcar."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TORONTO_CLRV_NAME"
msgstr "Toronto CRLV"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TOYAMA_8000_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"To replace older, non-air-conditioned trams of the 7000 series, the new "
"generation of single-car trams was introduced for the town of Toyama."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TOYAMA_8000_NAME"
msgstr "Toyama 8000"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYP1_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"For its time, the tram built by Gothaer Waggonfabrik featured a rather "
"unconventional front window to cover the windshield wiper mount."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYP1_NAME"
msgstr "Gotha T1 Motor Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYP1_WAGON_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Extending the capacity of the T1 motor car, the unmotorized wagon had the "
"same style to visually match the pulling front car."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYP1_WAGON_NAME"
msgstr "Gotha T1 Car"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYPE_LH_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Recognized for its distinctive color, the Viennese locomotive is used for "
"maintenance and service tasks across the whole tram network."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_TYPE_LH_NAME"
msgstr "Vienna Type LH"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_UNIV_CAR_A_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Early cargo tram wagons were small enough to feature a fixed two-axle design "
"and were usually adapted to individual types of cargo."

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_UNIV_CAR_A_NAME"
msgstr "Cargo Car 1895"

msgid "VEHICLE_TRAM_UNIV_CAR_B_DESCRIPTION"
msgstr ""
"Mid-century cargo tram wagons were often built for a specific purpose, but "
"featured bogies to allow for greater length and better maneuverability."

